-- Non-WSQ (C-prefix) course descriptions: expand + re-align to the course title (2026-10-05).
--
-- The admin Edit Course "Course Description" panel = short_description (storefront "What's This
-- Course About"). Audit of all 216 ENABLED SG C-prefix courses on prod: 184 were under 1,500 plain-text
-- chars (one, C818, was a 287-char single line about OpenAI Codex under the title "ChatGPT WORK for
-- Digital Marketing"); many named the wrong course (old WSQ titles, "Build Autonomous AI Agent with ...",
-- "AI-102" under AI-103, "ITF+" under Tech+, MS Project under Microsoft Planner) or carried a day count
-- ("1-day"/"2-day"/"4-day") that contradicts the Duration tile. C012 (Copilot never mentioned) and C181
-- (drifted to a Desktop-cert overview) were re-aligned too although already long enough.
--
-- 186 courses rewritten: 3 paragraphs, 1,500-2,000 plain-text chars, course title named in the opening
-- sentence, content grounded in each course's own topic list, ASCII only, no day/hour counts, no
-- funding references. Disabled C-prefix courses are not touched.
--
-- Guard: store 0 row only (no store-scope overrides exist), matched by TRIM(sku) AND the pre-migration
-- CHAR_LENGTH of the prod value -> a description edited since the audit is left alone, and a re-run
-- matches nothing (idempotent). SG-only (store guard) -> no-op on MY/GH.
-- Post-deploy: flat reindex + cache flush (/reindex/api/run?flush=1).

SET @sg := (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM core_store WHERE store_id = 1 AND code = 'singapore');
SET @a_short := (SELECT attribute_id FROM eav_attribute WHERE entity_type_id = 4 AND attribute_code = 'short_description');

-- C6 AI Powered Wordpress eCommerce
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI Powered Wordpress eCommerce shows you how to build, run and grow an online store on WordPress with artificial intelligence doing much of the heavy lifting. Working with WordPress and WooCommerce, you will see how AI assistants can speed up store setup, generate product content and images, personalise the shopping experience and turn store data into clear decisions. The course is designed for business owners, marketers and eCommerce executives who want a professional, revenue-generating WordPress shop without relying on an agency for every change.</p><p>You will start by setting up an AI-enabled WordPress store, choosing a theme, installing the essential plugins and using AI to draft pages and policies. Next you will build an AI-assisted product catalogue, writing product titles, descriptions and SEO metadata at scale, and creating supporting web content. The course then covers payments, shipping options and customer experience improvements such as chat support and recommendations, followed by AI-powered sales, order and promotion management, including discount campaigns and abandoned cart recovery.</p><p>The final part focuses on eCommerce analytics and performance optimisation. You will read store reports, use AI to interpret traffic, conversion and sales trends, and decide which products, pages and promotions to improve next. Every topic is hands-on, so you finish with a working store you have configured yourself and a repeatable AI workflow for keeping it fresh. By the end, you will be able to launch and manage a WordPress eCommerce site with confidence and use AI responsibly to save time and lift sales.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C6' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1476;

-- C8 Basic Hydroponics Course for Urban Farming
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Basic Hydroponics Course for Urban Farming introduces the science and practice of growing plants without soil, with a focus on what works in a dense city environment like Singapore. Hydroponics lets you grow leafy greens, herbs and fruiting vegetables using nutrient-rich water, less space and far less water than conventional farming. The course suits hobbyists, educators, aspiring urban farmers and anyone considering a home, rooftop or community hydroponic setup, and no prior farming experience is required.</p><p>You will begin with the history and advantages of hydroponics and compare the main system types, including wick, deep water culture, nutrient film technique, ebb and flow and drip systems. Next you will look at growing media, plant nutrition, pH and electrical conductivity, and learn how to mix and monitor a nutrient solution. Practical sessions cover the basic techniques of hydroponic farming, such as germinating seeds, transplanting seedlings, managing light and temperature, and preventing common pests, algae and root problems.</p><p>The course closes with urban farming practices in Singapore, looking at how hydroponics supports local food resilience, what makes a small system viable and how to plan a setup that fits your available space and budget. Throughout the session you will work hands-on with real equipment and plants, so the concepts are easy to apply at home. By the end, you will understand how hydroponic systems work, be able to set up and maintain a basic system, and confidently grow your own fresh produce.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C8' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1062;

-- C11 Generative AI for SEO
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Generative AI for SEO teaches you how to use tools such as ChatGPT, Claude and Gemini to plan, create and optimise content that ranks in search engines. Search engine optimisation has always demanded time-consuming research, writing and on-page tuning; generative AI can compress much of that work while you stay in control of quality and strategy. The course is built for digital marketers, content writers, business owners and website managers who want to grow organic traffic more efficiently.</p><p>You will start by getting set up with generative AI for SEO: understanding how search engines evaluate content, how AI fits into an SEO workflow and how to write effective prompts. You will use AI to research keywords and search intent, group keywords into topic clusters, analyse competing pages and plan a content calendar. The second part focuses on creating and optimising SEO content with generative AI, including drafting articles and landing pages, writing title tags and meta descriptions, structuring headings, adding internal links and generating FAQ and schema ideas.</p><p>Throughout the course you will also learn how to keep AI-assisted content accurate, original and genuinely helpful, in line with search engine quality guidelines, and how to check results with free SEO tools. All exercises are hands-on, using your own website or a sample site. By the end, you will have a practical, repeatable AI workflow for keyword research, content creation and on-page optimisation that helps your pages rank higher and attract the right visitors.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C11' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 927;

-- C012 Microsoft Copilot for Powerpoint Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Microsoft Copilot for Powerpoint Masterclass shows you how to build clear, professional and visually engaging presentations faster with Copilot, the AI assistant built into Microsoft PowerPoint. Instead of starting from a blank slide, you will learn to turn a prompt, a Word document or a set of data into a structured draft deck, then refine it into compelling visuals and infographics. The masterclass is designed for executives, managers, sales and marketing teams, trainers and anyone who regularly presents ideas or reports.</p><p>You will begin with AI-assisted planning, using Copilot to outline a storyline, summarise source material and pull out the key data insights your audience needs. Next you will create slides and infographics with Copilot in PowerPoint, generating layouts, rewriting text, adding images and icons, and using Designer, SmartArt, charts and diagrams to turn dense information into simple visual stories. You will practise prompting Copilot to adjust tone, length and structure, and combining its suggestions with your own design judgement and brand guidelines.</p><p>The final part covers evaluating and presenting infographics for business: checking accuracy, readability and visual balance, adding speaker notes with Copilot, and rehearsing delivery for maximum impact. All activities are hands-on, so you leave with decks you have built yourself and reusable prompts for future work. By the end, you will be able to use Microsoft Copilot in PowerPoint to produce polished, persuasive presentations in a fraction of the usual time.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C012' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1746;

-- C013 Generative AI for Project Management
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Generative AI for Project Management shows project managers how to use tools such as ChatGPT, Claude and Microsoft Copilot to work faster and make better decisions across the project lifecycle. Generative AI can draft charters and plans, summarise stakeholder input, generate schedules and risk registers, and turn status data into clear reports, freeing you to focus on leadership and problem solving. The course suits project managers, team leads, PMO staff and professionals who manage projects as part of their role.</p><p>You will start with project initiation and planning using generative AI: defining objectives and scope, identifying stakeholders, drafting the project charter, building a work breakdown structure and estimating timelines and resources. The next topic covers project execution and delivery, where you will use AI to prepare meeting agendas and minutes, track progress, write status reports and communicate effectively with sponsors and team members. You will learn prompting techniques that produce structured, reusable outputs such as tables, checklists and templates.</p><p>The final topic focuses on managing project risks with generative AI, including brainstorming risks, assessing likelihood and impact, planning responses and monitoring issues as the project evolves. Throughout the course you will also learn how to verify AI output, protect confidential project information and keep human judgement at the centre of key decisions. By the end, you will have a practical AI toolkit for initiating, planning, executing and controlling projects more efficiently and with greater confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C013' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 975;

-- C16 Generative AI for Adobe Photoshop
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Generative AI for Adobe Photoshop teaches you how to use Adobe Firefly and the generative AI features built into Photoshop to create, edit and enhance images in a fraction of the usual time. Features such as Generative Fill, Generative Expand and text-to-image let you add or remove objects, extend backgrounds and produce original visuals from a simple text prompt. The course is designed for designers, marketers, photographers, content creators and anyone who produces visual content for print, web or social media.</p><p>You will begin with generative AI for visual communication, exploring how AI image tools work, what they do well and how to write prompts that deliver the look you want. Next you will work in Adobe Firefly to generate images, text effects and style variations, and learn how to choose and refine the best results. You will then move into Photoshop, using Generative Fill and Generative Expand to remove distractions, swap backgrounds, add new elements and extend compositions while keeping lighting and perspective consistent.</p><p>The final topic covers adjusting AI images so they are ready for real projects: combining generative layers with selections, masks, adjustment layers and retouching tools, and preparing files for different output formats. You will also learn about responsible use, content credentials and the commercial safety of Firefly-generated content. By the end, you will be able to blend traditional Photoshop skills with generative AI to produce professional, on-brand images quickly and confidently.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C16' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1130;

-- C21 Agentic AI for Email Marketing
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Agentic AI for Email Marketing shows you how to use AI agents and generative AI tools to plan, write, automate and optimise email campaigns. Unlike a chatbot that only answers questions, an AI agent can carry out multi-step tasks, such as researching your audience, drafting a sequence, personalising content and reviewing performance, while you stay in control of the strategy and final approval. The course is designed for marketers, business owners and communications professionals who want to grow revenue from email without growing their workload.</p><p>You will start by getting set up with agentic AI for email marketing: understanding how AI agents work, how they connect to your email platform and data, and how to write clear briefs and prompts. You will use AI to define audience segments, plan campaigns, write subject lines and email copy in your brand voice, and create variations for testing. The second part focuses on automating email campaigns with AI agents, including welcome series, nurture flows, re-engagement sequences and event or promotion campaigns.</p><p>Throughout the course you will learn how to analyse open, click and conversion data with AI, decide what to improve and set up simple A/B tests. You will also cover deliverability basics, consent and data protection, so your automation stays compliant and trustworthy. All exercises are hands-on, giving you ready-to-use prompts and workflows. By the end, you will be able to run smarter, more personalised email marketing that is largely automated by AI agents and measurably more effective.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C21' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 910;

-- C22 Communication Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Communication Masterclass helps you communicate more clearly, confidently and effectively at work, whether you are speaking with colleagues, managers or customers. Poor communication is behind many missed deadlines, conflicts and lost customers; strong communication builds trust, collaboration and results. This masterclass is designed for executives, team leaders, managers and customer-facing staff who want practical techniques they can apply immediately to improve working relationships and service quality.</p><p>You will start by evaluating workplace communication practices, looking at how information flows in your team and organisation, the channels people use and where messages get lost or misunderstood. Next you will develop a communications plan, learning how to set objectives, analyse your audience, choose the right channel for each message and structure information so it is easy to understand and act on. You will also practise core skills such as active listening, questioning, giving and receiving feedback, and adapting your style to different personalities.</p><p>The final topic focuses on identifying solutions to address communication gaps and barriers, including cultural differences, remote and hybrid working, information overload and difficult conversations. Through role plays, case studies and group discussions, you will apply each technique to realistic workplace scenarios. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to diagnose communication problems, plan and deliver messages more effectively, and foster stronger collaboration and customer satisfaction in your organisation.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C22' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 837;

-- C23 Adobe InDesign CC Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Adobe InDesign CC Masterclass teaches you how to design professional print and digital layouts with Adobe InDesign, the industry standard for page layout and publishing. From brochures, flyers and posters to magazines, reports and interactive PDFs, InDesign gives you precise control over text, images and graphics. This masterclass is suitable for beginners, marketing and communications staff, and designers who want a structured, hands-on path to producing polished publications with confidence.</p><p>You will start by getting familiar with InDesign: the workspace, tools and panels, setting up documents with the right size, margins, columns and bleed, and working with pages and master pages. Next you will learn basic InDesign drawing techniques, including frames, shapes, lines, colour swatches and gradients, placing and fitting images, and formatting text with character and paragraph settings. You will build real layouts step by step and learn how to keep designs consistent using styles and grids.</p><p>The final topic covers refining your InDesign designs: working with layers, text wrap, tables, effects and typography details, applying paragraph and object styles, and checking your work with preflight. You will then package and export your files for commercial print and for digital use as PDF. Along the way you will pick up time-saving shortcuts and good file-management habits used by professional designers. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to plan, build and export complete multi-page layouts in Adobe InDesign and produce professional publications efficiently, ready for print or screen.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C23' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 831;

-- C024 SQL Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>SQL Masterclass gives you the practical skills to store, query, analyse and transform data using Structured Query Language, the universal language of relational databases. Whether you work with MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQL Server or a cloud data platform, SQL lets you answer business questions directly from the data instead of waiting for reports. The masterclass is designed for analysts, developers, business users and anyone who wants a solid, hands-on foundation in working with databases.</p><p>You will begin with data modelling, learning how relational databases are structured, how to design tables, choose data types and define primary keys, foreign keys and relationships. Next you will move into data processing and analysis, writing queries to create, read, update and delete records, filter and sort results, and use aggregate functions with GROUP BY and HAVING. You will then join multiple tables, write subqueries and use common table expressions to answer more complex questions.</p><p>The course continues with data transformation, covering string, date and conditional functions, views and techniques for cleaning and reshaping data for reporting. Finally, you will get an introduction to data warehousing, including fact and dimension tables, star schemas and how SQL supports business intelligence and dashboards. Every topic includes guided exercises on a real database. By the end, you will be able to design simple databases and write efficient SQL queries to turn raw data into reliable insights.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C024' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 852;

-- C027 Microsoft 365 Copilot Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Microsoft 365 Copilot Masterclass shows you how to use Copilot, the AI assistant built into Microsoft 365, to get more done across the apps you use every day. Copilot can draft documents in Word, analyse data in Excel, build presentations in PowerPoint, summarise and reply to email in Outlook, and recap meetings in Teams, all from plain-English prompts. The masterclass is designed for professionals, managers and teams who want to save time on routine work and focus on higher-value tasks.</p><p>You will start by getting started with Microsoft 365 Copilot: what it can and cannot do, how it uses your organisational data through Microsoft Graph, and how to write effective prompts using goal, context, source and expectations. You will try Copilot Chat for research and drafting, and learn how to refine responses. Next you will apply Copilot across your everyday work apps, creating and rewriting documents, generating formulas and insights from spreadsheets, turning outlines into slide decks, triaging your inbox and catching up on meetings and chats.</p><p>Throughout the masterclass you will also cover responsible use, including checking accuracy, protecting sensitive information and understanding data security in Microsoft 365. Every activity is hands-on with realistic workplace scenarios, and you will leave with a library of reusable prompts that you can adapt for your own role. By the end, you will be able to use Microsoft 365 Copilot confidently to work faster, communicate more clearly and boost your daily productivity.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C027' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1000;

-- C30 Smart Phone Photography Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Smart Phone Photography Masterclass shows you how to take stunning photos with the camera you already carry every day. Modern smartphones offer powerful lenses, manual controls and computational features, but most people only ever use point-and-shoot mode. This masterclass is designed for beginners, social media users, small business owners and content creators who want to capture professional-looking images for personal memories, marketing or social media without buying expensive equipment.</p><p>You will start by setting up your mobile camera for shooting, exploring camera modes, resolution, grid lines, HDR, focus and exposure lock, and when to use portrait, night and pro modes. Next you will build basic mobile photography skills, including holding the phone steady, controlling focus and exposure, and working with natural and artificial light. The course then covers framing and composition, with practical techniques such as the rule of thirds, leading lines, symmetry, perspective, depth and negative space.</p><p>The final topic focuses on enhancing visual quality and effects, using editing apps to crop, straighten, adjust colour and light, retouch details and apply consistent styles. You will also learn simple accessories and tricks for product shots, portraits, food and travel photography. Every topic includes hands-on shooting exercises and feedback. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to plan, capture and edit eye-catching photos with your smartphone that look polished and professional.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C30' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 860;

-- C34 Microsoft 365 Copilot for Excel
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Microsoft 365 Copilot for Excel shows you how to use Copilot, the AI assistant built into Microsoft Excel, to analyse data, create formulas and build reports using plain-English prompts. Instead of searching for the right function or spending ages on manual analysis, you can ask Copilot to highlight trends, summarise results, create charts and suggest next steps. The course is designed for professionals, analysts, finance and operations staff and anyone who works with spreadsheets regularly.</p><p>You will start by getting started with Copilot in Excel: preparing your data as tables, understanding what Copilot can do, and writing clear prompts to sort, filter, format and clean data. You will use Copilot to generate and explain formulas, from lookups and conditional calculations to date and text functions, so you understand the logic as well as the result. Next you will move into AI-powered data analysis and insights, asking Copilot to identify patterns and outliers, build PivotTables and charts, and add calculated columns.</p><p>Throughout the course you will learn how to check Copilot\'s results, combine its suggestions with your own Excel skills and present findings clearly to stakeholders. You will also cover practical limits and good data habits that help Copilot give better answers. Every exercise uses realistic business datasets, and you will leave with reusable prompts for common tasks. By the end, you will be able to use Microsoft 365 Copilot in Excel to analyse data faster, reduce errors and turn spreadsheets into clear business insights.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C34' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1050;

-- C037 Adobe Illustrator Fundamentals for Beginners
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Adobe Illustrator Fundamentals for Beginners introduces you to Adobe Illustrator, the industry-standard tool for creating vector graphics such as logos, icons, illustrations, infographics and marketing materials. Because vector artwork scales to any size without losing quality, Illustrator is essential for professional branding and print work. This course is designed for complete beginners, marketing staff, small business owners and aspiring designers who want to create clean, professional graphics with confidence.</p><p>You will begin with basic digital graphics design in Illustrator, exploring the workspace, artboards, layers and the essential selection, shape and drawing tools. You will learn how to draw with the Pen, Pencil and Shape Builder tools, work with fills, strokes, colour swatches and gradients, and add and format text. Next you will improve your digital graphics designs by combining and aligning shapes, using pathfinder operations, applying effects and patterns, and creating simple logos and icons step by step.</p><p>The final topic covers evaluating graphics designs in Illustrator: reviewing your artwork against design principles such as balance, contrast, hierarchy and consistency, refining typography, and preparing files correctly for print and digital use. You will practise exporting in the right formats, including PDF, PNG and SVG. Every topic is hands-on, so you build a small portfolio of your own work. By the end, you will be able to design, refine and export professional vector graphics in Adobe Illustrator.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C037' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 805;

-- C104 AI for Accounting
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI for Accounting shows accountants and finance teams how to bring modern AI tools such as ChatGPT, Claude and Microsoft Copilot into everyday accounting work. AI can extract data from invoices and receipts, categorise transactions, assist with reconciliations, draft reports and flag unusual entries, reducing manual effort and the risk of errors. The course is designed for accountants, bookkeepers, finance executives and SME owners who want practical, responsible ways to use AI in their accounting practice.</p><p>You will begin with an introduction to AI for accounting, covering what current AI tools can do, where they fit in the accounting workflow, and how to write effective prompts for finance tasks. Next you will apply AI to bookkeeping and transactions, using it to read and extract data from documents, classify expenses, prepare journal entries and support bank reconciliations. You will then use AI for reporting and analysis, summarising financial statements, explaining variances, building simple forecasts and preparing management commentary.</p><p>The final topic covers AI for compliance, audit and automation, including reviewing transactions for anomalies, preparing audit schedules, checking policy and GST considerations, and automating repetitive steps with AI-powered workflows. Throughout the course you will learn how to verify AI output, protect confidential financial data and keep professional judgement at the centre of your work. By the end, you will be able to use AI confidently to work faster, improve accuracy and add more value as an accounting professional.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C104' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1012;

-- C134 QuickBooks Fundamentals
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>QuickBooks Fundamentals gives you hands-on training in QuickBooks Online, one of the most widely used cloud accounting systems for small and medium-sized businesses. You will learn how to set up a company file, record day-to-day transactions, manage Goods and Services Tax and produce the financial reports business owners and accountants rely on. The course is designed for SME owners, administrative and accounts staff, and anyone new to QuickBooks who wants to keep accurate books with confidence.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to QuickBooks Online Plus, covering the dashboard, navigation, company settings, chart of accounts and how to configure products and services. Next you will input data into QuickBooks, creating customers and suppliers, issuing quotes and invoices, receiving payments, entering bills and expenses, and recording bank transactions. You will also learn how to connect bank feeds, categorise transactions and complete a bank reconciliation so your records always match your statements.</p><p>The course then covers managing Goods and Services Tax in QuickBooks, including setting up tax codes, applying GST correctly to sales and purchases and preparing GST reports for filing. The final topic focuses on financial and accounting reports, such as the profit and loss statement, balance sheet, aged receivables and payables and sales reports, and how to customise them. By the end, you will be able to manage your business accounts in QuickBooks Online accurately and efficiently.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C134' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 970;

-- C135 Basic Accounting for Non-Finance Managers
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Basic Accounting for Non-Finance Managers gives managers and professionals without a finance background a clear, practical understanding of how accounting works and how to use financial information to make better decisions. You do not need to become an accountant to read a profit and loss statement, understand your department\'s costs or have confident conversations with your finance team. The course is designed for managers, team leaders, entrepreneurs and professionals who need to manage budgets or interpret financial reports.</p><p>You will start with the basics of financial accounting: the accounting equation, double-entry bookkeeping, the accounting cycle, and how transactions flow into the income statement, balance sheet and cash flow statement. You will learn how to read these statements and what key figures and ratios tell you about performance and financial health. Next you will cover the basics of managerial accounting, including cost behaviour, fixed and variable costs, break-even analysis, budgeting and how cost information supports pricing and operational decisions.</p><p>The final topic introduces common accounting issues and income taxes, such as revenue recognition, depreciation, accruals and how business income tax works in practice. Throughout the course you will work through simple examples and case studies drawn from real business situations. By the end, you will be able to understand and interpret financial statements, use accounting information to plan and control your area of responsibility, and communicate more effectively with finance professionals.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C135' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 947;

-- C140 Blender Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Blender Masterclass takes you into the world of 3D modelling, animation and rendering with Blender, the powerful free and open-source 3D creation suite used by artists, designers and studios worldwide. Blender lets you build anything from product prototypes and architectural visuals to game assets and animated scenes. This masterclass is designed for beginners, designers, engineers, marketers and hobbyists who want a structured, hands-on introduction to creating professional 3D work.</p><p>You will begin by getting started with 3D modelling in Blender, learning the interface, navigation, object and edit modes, and the essential modelling tools for shaping meshes. Next you will develop 3D prototypes, using modifiers, extrusion, loop cuts, subdivision and boolean operations to build accurate models, then add materials, textures and lighting to make them look realistic. You will then animate your 3D prototype, setting keyframes, using the timeline and graph editor, and creating simple camera and object animations.</p><p>The final topic covers optimising your 3D prototype for its intended use, including cleaning up geometry, managing polygon counts, setting up render engines such as Eevee and Cycles, and exporting models for 3D printing, games or presentations. Every topic is hands-on, so you build complete models and scenes step by step, with tips on keyboard shortcuts and efficient workflows. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to model, texture, animate and render your own 3D projects in Blender with confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C140' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 853;

-- C142 Certified Lean Six Sigma White Belt (CLSSWB)
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Certified Lean Six Sigma White Belt (CLSSWB) gives you a clear, foundational understanding of Lean Six Sigma and how it helps organisations improve quality, reduce waste and serve customers better. Lean Six Sigma combines Lean thinking, which removes non-value-adding activities, with Six Sigma, which reduces variation using data. The White Belt level is ideal for team members, supervisors and professionals who want to understand the language of process improvement and support improvement projects in their organisation.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to quality, exploring what quality means to customers, the cost of poor quality, the history of Six Sigma and Lean, and the roles of White, Yellow, Green and Black Belts. Next you will cover the Six Sigma Define, Measure and Analyse phases, learning how to define a problem and project scope, map a process, identify customer requirements, collect data and use simple tools such as cause-and-effect diagrams and Pareto charts to find root causes.</p><p>The final topic covers the Six Sigma Improve and Control phases, including generating and selecting solutions, piloting changes and sustaining gains with standard work and simple control methods. Practical examples and group activities help you see how the DMAIC framework applies in real workplaces. By the end, you will understand the core principles of Lean Six Sigma, be able to contribute effectively to improvement teams, and be prepared to sit for the Certified Lean Six Sigma White Belt (CLSSWB) certification.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C142' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 889;

-- C148 Google Workspace Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Google Workspace Masterclass helps you and your team get far more out of Gmail, Google Drive, Docs, Sheets, Slides, Meet, Calendar and the other apps in Google Workspace. Many organisations use only a fraction of what Workspace can do; used well, it streamlines collaboration, keeps information organised and secure, and reduces time spent on email and admin. The masterclass is designed for SME owners, administrators, office staff and team leads who want to work smarter with Google\'s cloud productivity suite.</p><p>You will start with an overview of Google Workspace, exploring how the apps work together and how to set up an efficient, collaborative way of working. Next you will work with Google Workspace contents and assets, organising Google Drive and shared drives, setting sharing permissions and policies, and creating and collaborating on documents, spreadsheets and presentations in real time. You will learn practical features such as version history, comments and suggestions, templates, forms and calendar scheduling to keep projects moving.</p><p>The final topic covers Google Admin and add-ons, including managing users and groups, applying security and data-sharing settings, and extending Workspace with add-ons, integrations and built-in AI features. Every topic is hands-on with realistic workplace scenarios. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to organise and manage your organisation\'s content in Google Workspace, collaborate more effectively, and keep data accessible, well-structured and secure.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C148' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 820;

-- C152 Generative AI for Adobe Illustrator
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Generative AI for Adobe Illustrator shows you how to use Adobe Firefly, the generative AI engine built into Illustrator, to create logos, icons, illustrations and patterns faster than ever. Features such as Text to Vector Graphic, Generative Recolor and Generative Shape Fill let you turn a simple prompt into editable vector artwork that you can refine with Illustrator\'s precise tools. The course is designed for graphic designers, marketers, illustrators and content creators who want to speed up vector design without sacrificing quality.</p><p>You will start with generative vector design essentials in Illustrator: how Firefly works, writing effective prompts, and generating scenes, subjects, icons and patterns as fully editable vectors. You will learn how to control style, detail and colour, and how to refine generated artwork with the Pen, Shape Builder and Direct Selection tools. Next you will explore advanced generative workflows, using Generative Recolor to explore colour themes, Generative Shape Fill to add detail, and matching new artwork to an existing brand style.</p><p>Throughout the course you will combine AI output with your own design judgement, checking for consistency, typography and layout, and preparing files for print and digital use. You will also cover responsible use, licensing and the commercial safety of Firefly content. All exercises are hands-on, building a small set of finished assets. By the end, you will be able to use generative AI in Adobe Illustrator to produce professional, on-brand vector graphics quickly and confidently.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C152' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1173;

-- C156 Canva Design Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Canva Design Masterclass teaches you how to create professional, eye-catching visual content with Canva, the easy-to-use online design platform. From social media posts, presentations and posters to brochures, videos and brand kits, Canva makes design accessible, but great results still depend on sound design principles. This masterclass is designed for marketers, small business owners, educators, administrators and anyone who wants to produce polished visuals quickly without specialist design software.</p><p>You will begin with an introduction to Canva and basic design principles, learning the interface, templates and elements, and how hierarchy, alignment, contrast and spacing make a design work. Next you will explore colour and form, building colour palettes, choosing fonts and combining shapes, images and icons effectively. You will then cover storyboarding and flow design in Canva, planning multi-page presentations, carousels and short videos so your message flows logically from start to finish.</p><p>The later topics focus on best practices and aesthetic analysis, critical review and enhancement strategies, and innovative applications of Canva. You will learn to critique and improve your own designs, set up brand kits for consistency, collaborate with your team, use Canva\'s AI-powered Magic tools, and export work correctly for print and digital channels. Every topic is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to plan, design and refine compelling visual communication in Canva with confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C156' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1218;

-- C162 Generative AI for 3D Modeling
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Generative AI for 3D Modeling shows you how AI-assisted design tools can turn text descriptions, reference images and sketches into 3D models, and how to refine those models into production-ready assets. Generative AI is changing how designers, engineers and creators approach concept development, prototyping and visualisation, cutting long stretches of manual modelling down to minutes. The course is designed for product designers, engineers, architects, game and animation artists, and makers who want to bring AI into their 3D workflow.</p><p>You will begin with generative AI for 3D design concepts and modelling, exploring current text-to-3D and image-to-3D tools, writing effective prompts and generating multiple design options quickly. Next you will move to AI-assisted 3D model analysis, validation and refinement, learning how to inspect generated meshes, fix geometry and topology issues, check scale and proportions, and refine models in tools such as Blender. You will also explore how AI can suggest design variations and textures.</p><p>The final topic covers 3D model optimisation, standards and production workflows, including reducing polygon counts, preparing models for 3D printing, games, AR and rendering, and choosing the right export formats. Throughout the course you will also discuss intellectual property and responsible use of AI-generated content. Every topic is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to combine generative AI with traditional 3D skills to create, refine and optimise 3D models efficiently.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C162' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1300;

-- C163 Adobe After Effects Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Adobe After Effects Masterclass teaches you how to create professional motion graphics, visual effects and animations with Adobe After Effects, the industry-standard tool for video compositing. From animated titles and logo reveals to explainer graphics and cinematic effects, After Effects lets you add the polish that makes video content stand out. This masterclass is designed for video editors, designers, marketers and content creators who want to take their video work to a professional level.</p><p>You will begin by reviewing video content for editing with After Effects, understanding compositions, layers, the timeline and how After Effects fits alongside Premiere Pro in a production workflow. Next you will learn core video editing and animation techniques, including keyframes, transform properties, easing, masks, shape layers and text animation, so you can build smooth, engaging motion graphics. You will practise creating lower thirds, title sequences and animated graphics step by step.</p><p>The final topic covers advanced video editing techniques with After Effects, such as motion tracking, green screen keying, compositing, effects and presets, 3D layers and cameras, and expressions for more efficient animation. You will also learn how to render and export your work for web, social media and broadcast. Every topic is hands-on, and you will complete several short projects that you can add to your portfolio. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to plan and produce compelling motion graphics and visual effects in Adobe After Effects.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C163' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 808;

-- C165 AI for Logistics
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI for Logistics shows logistics and supply chain professionals how artificial intelligence, including agentic AI that can plan, decide and act on your behalf, can make operations faster, more accurate and more resilient. From demand planning and route optimisation to shipment tracking and exception handling, AI helps teams cut costs, improve visibility and respond quickly when things go wrong. The course is designed for logistics coordinators, warehouse and transport managers, supply chain planners and operations staff.</p><p>You will start with AI for logistics efficiency, exploring how AI tools and AI agents can forecast demand, optimise inventory, plan routes and loads, and automate routine tasks such as documentation, scheduling and customer updates. You will learn how to write effective prompts and design simple agent workflows for common logistics processes. The second topic focuses on AI for tracking and monitoring, using AI to consolidate shipment data, monitor delivery performance, detect delays and anomalies, and trigger alerts and follow-up actions.</p><p>Throughout the course you will work with realistic logistics scenarios and data, and learn how to evaluate AI recommendations, keep humans in control of key decisions, and manage data quality and security. You will also discuss how to start small and build a business case for AI in your own operation. By the end, you will be able to identify high-value AI opportunities in logistics and apply AI tools and agents to improve efficiency, visibility and service levels.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C165' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 968;

-- C171 Git and Github Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Git and Github Masterclass gives you hands-on mastery of Git, the world\'s most popular version control system, and GitHub, the platform where developers store, share and collaborate on code. Version control lets you track every change, experiment safely and work with others without overwriting each other\'s work. This masterclass is designed for developers, data analysts, IT professionals, students and anyone who works with code, scripts or documentation and wants to collaborate professionally.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to Git and GitHub, installing Git, creating repositories and learning the core workflow of staging, committing and viewing history. Next you will work with GitHub repositories, pushing and pulling changes, cloning and forking projects, and writing good README files. You will then explore collaboration features, including branching and merging, pull requests, code reviews, resolving merge conflicts and managing issues, so you can work confidently in a team.</p><p>The course continues with modern development practices such as GitHub Actions for automation, GitHub Codespaces and AI coding assistance with GitHub Copilot, followed by GitHub Projects for planning and tracking work. The final topic covers privacy, security and administration, including access control, branch protection, secret management and organisation settings. Every topic is hands-on. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to manage your code with Git and collaborate effectively on GitHub.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C171' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 891;

-- C177 AI Agents for Stock Trading
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI Agents for Stock Trading shows you how to put AI agents to work on your stock trading research in a structured, disciplined way. Rather than chasing tips or relying on gut feel, you will learn how an AI agent can help turn trading ideas into testable hypotheses, gather and check market data, and analyse results, while you stay in control of every decision. The course is designed for retail investors, active traders, finance professionals and anyone curious about applying AI to the markets.</p><p>You will start by going from trading idea to quality market data: framing an idea clearly, connecting your AI agent to reliable price, volume and fundamental data sources, and checking that data for gaps, errors and bias before you rely on it. You will learn how to brief an agent effectively so it produces structured, reproducible analysis rather than vague opinions. The second topic covers a six-step trading workflow, taking a hypothesis through research, signal definition, testing, evaluation, risk planning and review with the agent\'s help.</p><p>Throughout the course you will focus on staying in control: understanding the limits of AI, avoiding over-fitting and look-ahead bias, setting position sizing and risk rules, and keeping a clear audit trail of decisions. The course is educational and does not provide financial advice. All exercises are hands-on with real market data. By the end, you will be able to use AI agents to research trading ideas more rigorously, efficiently and responsibly.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C177' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 996;

-- C179 Python Fundamentals Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Python Fundamentals Masterclass gives you a solid, hands-on foundation in Python, one of the most versatile and widely used programming languages in the world. Python powers data analysis, automation, web development, artificial intelligence and much more, and its clean syntax makes it ideal for beginners. This masterclass is designed for complete beginners, career switchers, analysts and professionals who want to start programming or automate everyday tasks.</p><p>You will begin by getting started with Python, installing the tools, using an editor and Jupyter notebooks, and writing your first programs. Next you will learn Python data types, including numbers, strings, lists, tuples, dictionaries and sets, and how to work with each of them. You will then explore operators for arithmetic, comparison and logic, followed by control structures, including if statements, for and while loops, and list and dictionary comprehensions that let you write concise, readable code.</p><p>The later topics cover functions, where you will define your own reusable functions with parameters and return values, and modules and packages, where you will import Python\'s standard library and install third-party packages with pip. Every topic includes practical coding exercises that build on the previous one, so you steadily gain confidence, and you will also learn good habits for naming, commenting and organising your code. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to write, read and debug Python programs and have a strong base for further study in data, automation or AI.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C179' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 835;

-- C181 Tableau Data Prep Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Tableau Data Prep Masterclass gives you the practical skills to connect to, clean, shape and analyse data in Tableau so that every dashboard you build rests on reliable, well-prepared data. Most analytics time is spent preparing data rather than visualising it; Tableau\'s data preparation features let you combine sources, fix quality issues and structure data for analysis quickly and repeatably. The masterclass is designed for analysts, business users and reporting staff, and also supports preparation for the Salesforce Certified Tableau Desktop Foundations certification.</p><p>You will start by connecting to and preparing data in Tableau Desktop, working with Excel, CSV and database sources, and using joins, relationships, unions and data interpreter to combine and clean data. You will learn to rename and split fields, change data types, handle nulls, create groups, hierarchies and calculated fields, and build data extracts. Next you will explore and analyse your prepared data, using filters, sorting, aggregation and table calculations to uncover patterns and answer business questions.</p><p>The course then covers sharing insights with dashboards and workbooks, designing clear views, adding interactivity and publishing your work. The final topic consolidates key Tableau concepts such as dimensions and measures, discrete and continuous fields and level of detail, along with exam preparation tips. Every topic is hands-on with realistic datasets. By the end, you will be able to prepare data confidently in Tableau and turn it into trustworthy, insightful visual analysis.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C181' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1653;

-- C182 Data Analytics with R
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Data Analytics with R teaches you how to transform raw data into actionable insights using R, the powerful open-source language for statistics and data analysis. Widely used in research, finance, healthcare and business analytics, R offers a rich ecosystem of packages for cleaning, analysing and visualising data. This course is designed for analysts, researchers, students and professionals who want a practical, hands-on introduction to data analytics using R and RStudio.</p><p>You will begin with data preparation and transformation, importing data from files and databases, and using the tidyverse, including dplyr and tidyr, to clean, filter, reshape, join and create new variables. Next you will learn to produce data summaries, calculating descriptive statistics and grouping data to compare segments. You will then move into quantitative data analysis, applying techniques such as correlation, hypothesis testing and regression to explore relationships and test assumptions in numeric data.</p><p>The course continues with qualitative data analysis, working with categorical and text data, frequency tables and cross-tabulations, followed by data visualisation with ggplot2 to create clear bar charts, histograms, scatter plots and multi-panel charts. Every topic is hands-on with real datasets and reproducible R scripts, and you will learn how to document your analysis with R Markdown. By the end, you will be able to prepare, analyse and visualise data in R confidently and communicate your findings in a way that supports better decisions.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C182' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 838;

-- C188 AI Vibe Coding for Python Financial Analysis
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI Vibe Coding for Python Financial Analysis teaches you how to use AI coding assistants such as Cursor, GitHub Copilot and Claude to analyse financial data with Python. Instead of writing every line of code yourself, you describe what you want in plain English, review what the AI produces and steer it until the analysis is right. The course is designed for finance professionals, analysts, investors and accountants who want to harness Python for financial work without needing to be expert programmers.</p><p>You will start by getting set up with AI vibe coding for financial analysis, installing the tools and learning how to prompt an AI assistant to write, explain and debug Python code using pandas and related libraries. Next you will analyse financial data with AI, importing price and financial statement data, cleaning it, calculating returns, ratios and growth rates, and exploring trends. You will then apply vibe coding to portfolio and investment analysis, measuring risk and return, volatility, correlation and diversification, and comparing portfolio strategies.</p><p>The final topic covers building financial dashboards and reports, turning your analysis into clear charts and interactive dashboards that communicate insights to stakeholders. Throughout the course you will learn to check AI-generated code and results carefully, avoid common data pitfalls and keep your analysis reproducible. All exercises are hands-on with real financial data. By the end, you will be able to use AI-assisted Python to perform financial analysis faster and with confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C188' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1152;

-- C193 Python Data Analysis Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Python Data Analysis Masterclass gives you hands-on skills to prepare, transform, visualise and analyse data using Python and its powerful data libraries. Python has become the language of choice for data analytics because it combines readable code with tools such as pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib and Seaborn that handle everything from simple summaries to advanced analysis. This masterclass is designed for analysts, business users, researchers and professionals with basic Python knowledge who want to work with data more effectively.</p><p>You will start with data preparation, loading data from CSV, Excel and other sources into pandas, inspecting it and handling missing values, duplicates and incorrect data types. Next you will learn data transformation, including filtering, sorting, grouping, merging and reshaping datasets, and creating new calculated columns. You will then move into data visualisation, using Matplotlib and Seaborn to build clear line, bar, scatter and distribution charts that reveal patterns and communicate results effectively.</p><p>The later topics cover data analysis, applying descriptive statistics, correlation and grouping to answer business questions, followed by advanced data analytics such as time series analysis and an introduction to predictive techniques. Every topic is hands-on with realistic datasets in Jupyter notebooks, so you build a portfolio of working analyses. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to use Python confidently to turn raw data into reliable insights that support decision-making.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C193' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 902;

-- C197 Claude Microsoft 365 Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Claude Microsoft 365 Masterclass shows you how to use Claude, Anthropic\'s AI assistant, to work smarter across Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook and Teams. Claude excels at drafting, summarising, analysing and reasoning through complex information, and when connected to your Microsoft 365 environment it can help you produce documents, spreadsheets, presentations and emails faster and to a higher standard. The masterclass is designed for professionals, managers and teams who use Microsoft 365 every day and want to save time on routine work.</p><p>You will start by getting started with Claude for Microsoft 365, setting up access, understanding how Claude works with your files and data, and learning prompting techniques that give clear, reliable results. You will explore how to share documents with Claude, ask it to analyse content and turn its responses into ready-to-use outputs. Next you will boost productivity across Microsoft 365 with Claude, drafting and editing Word documents, analysing data and building formulas for Excel, outlining and writing slide decks, and composing and summarising emails and meeting notes.</p><p>Throughout the masterclass you will also cover responsible use, including checking accuracy, protecting confidential information and following your organisation\'s data policies. Every activity is hands-on with realistic workplace tasks, and you will leave with a set of reusable prompts. By the end, you will be able to use Claude confidently alongside Microsoft 365 to work faster, communicate more clearly and produce higher quality work.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C197' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 896;

-- C200 Adobe Lightroom Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Adobe Lightroom Masterclass teaches you how to organise, edit and share your photos professionally with Adobe Lightroom, the go-to tool for photographers who want consistent, beautiful results. Lightroom combines powerful non-destructive editing with a smart cataloguing system, so you can manage thousands of images and edit them efficiently. This masterclass is designed for photographers, content creators, marketers and hobbyists who want to take their photo editing to a professional standard.</p><p>You will begin by getting started with digital imagery techniques using Lightroom, learning how to import photos, organise them with collections, keywords, ratings and flags, and navigate the workspace. Next you will evaluate Lightroom\'s digital imaging capabilities, adjusting exposure, contrast, white balance, colour and tone curves, and using cropping, straightening, sharpening and noise reduction. You will also learn masking and local adjustments, including AI-powered subject and sky selections, to enhance specific areas of an image.</p><p>The final topic covers the process of digital image production, including creating and applying presets for a consistent style, batch editing, syncing settings across images, and exporting photos in the right size and format for print, web and social media. Every topic is hands-on using a variety of sample images. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to manage an efficient photo workflow in Adobe Lightroom and produce polished, professional images.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C200' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 824;

-- C201 Claude Design Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Claude Design Masterclass shows you how to use Claude, Anthropic\'s AI assistant, to design faster and better. Claude can turn a plain-English brief into working visual output, including interactive UI mockups and prototypes, presentation decks, infographics, posters and social media graphics, and then refine them through conversation. The masterclass is designed for designers, marketers, product managers, entrepreneurs and anyone who needs professional visual assets but wants to move from idea to finished design in a fraction of the usual time.</p><p>You will start by getting started with Claude for design, learning how Claude creates visual artefacts, how to write effective design briefs and how to iterate on layout, colour, typography and content through follow-up prompts. You will explore how to supply reference images, brand guidelines and data so Claude\'s output matches your needs. Next you will create professional design assets with Claude, building a landing page mockup, an interactive prototype, a slide deck, an infographic and a set of social media visuals step by step.</p><p>Throughout the masterclass you will learn to evaluate designs against good design principles such as hierarchy, contrast, accessibility and consistency, and to combine Claude\'s speed with your own creative judgement. You will also learn how to export and hand off your work to other tools and team members. All activities are hands-on. By the end, you will be able to use Claude confidently to produce polished, on-brand designs quickly.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C201' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 997;

-- C203 IoT with Raspberry Pi
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>IoT with Raspberry Pi teaches you how to build real Internet of Things projects using the Raspberry Pi, a low-cost, credit-card-sized computer that is ideal for connecting sensors and devices to the cloud. Working with our IoTFlow platform, you will connect hardware, collect data, visualise it on dashboards and control devices remotely. The course is designed for engineers, IT professionals, educators, students and makers who want a practical, hands-on introduction to IoT.</p><p>You will begin with an overview of the Internet of Things, exploring IoT architecture, sensors and actuators, communication protocols such as MQTT and HTTP, and real-world applications in smart homes, buildings, agriculture and industry. Next you will collect and post environmental data to the cloud, wiring temperature, humidity and light sensors to the Raspberry Pi and writing Python code to read them and send the data to the IoTFlow cloud platform.</p><p>The course then covers IoT data analytics and visualisation, building dashboards, charts and simple analyses that turn sensor readings into useful insights. The final topic focuses on monitoring data to trigger control from the cloud, setting thresholds and rules that switch LEDs, relays or other devices automatically or remotely. Every topic is hands-on with real hardware, and you will also cover basic IoT security practices such as protecting device credentials and keeping software up to date. By the end, you will be able to design, build and run a complete IoT solution using the Raspberry Pi and a cloud platform.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C203' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 845;

-- C204 3D Printing Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>3D Printing Masterclass gives you a comprehensive, practical understanding of 3D printing and additive manufacturing, and how these technologies are transforming product development, prototyping and production. From desktop FDM printers to industrial resin, powder and metal systems, 3D printing lets you turn digital designs into physical parts quickly and economically. The masterclass is designed for engineers, product designers, manufacturing professionals, educators and makers who want to use 3D printing effectively.</p><p>You will start with an overview of additive manufacturing and 3D printing, comparing the main process families, including material extrusion, vat photopolymerisation, powder bed fusion and material jetting, and the materials each uses. You will learn the end-to-end workflow, from CAD model and STL file to slicing, printing and post-processing. Next you will examine process-related issues, such as design for additive manufacturing, orientation, support structures, tolerances, warping, layer adhesion and surface finish.</p><p>The final topic covers process improvement for additive manufacturing, including selecting the right technology and material for an application, optimising print settings, inspecting quality and reducing cost and lead time. You will also discuss real case studies from industry. The masterclass combines theory with hands-on printing activities. By the end, you will be able to evaluate additive manufacturing options, design better parts for 3D printing and troubleshoot and improve print quality with confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C204' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 903;

-- C207 AI for Finance
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI for Finance prepares finance professionals for the next era of financial work, where AI and AI agents do far more than answer questions. Agentic AI can plan, reason and act, extracting financial data, analysing statements, building forecasts, monitoring risks and preparing reports with minimal manual effort. The course is designed for finance managers, analysts, accountants, controllers and business leaders who want to understand and apply AI to improve the speed, accuracy and insight of their finance function.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to AI and agentic AI for finance, covering generative AI, AI agents and the tools available today, and how to write effective prompts for financial tasks. Next you will use AI agents for financial data and analysis, extracting data from documents, reconciling figures, calculating ratios and explaining variances. You will then design agentic workflows for financial planning and reporting, using AI to build budgets and forecasts, run scenarios and produce management reports and commentary.</p><p>The final topic covers risk, compliance and deploying finance AI agents, including monitoring transactions for anomalies, supporting audit and regulatory requirements, and putting governance, controls and human review in place before scaling. Throughout the course you will work with realistic financial scenarios and learn how to verify AI output and protect sensitive data. By the end, you will be able to identify high-value AI opportunities in finance and apply AI agents confidently and responsibly.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C207' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1131;

-- C208 Financial Ratio Analysis
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Financial Ratio Analysis teaches you how to calculate, interpret and apply the key financial ratios that reveal an organisation\'s true performance and financial health. Ratios turn the numbers in financial statements into meaningful indicators of profitability, liquidity, efficiency, solvency and value, helping managers, investors and lenders make better decisions. The course is designed for managers, finance and accounts staff, business owners, analysts and investors who want to read financial statements with confidence.</p><p>You will start by assessing an organisation\'s profitability, learning how to calculate and interpret gross, operating and net profit margins, return on assets and return on equity, and how to trace changes in profitability back to their causes. You will review how the income statement, balance sheet and cash flow statement link together so that each ratio is grounded in the underlying figures. Next you will evaluate an organisation\'s performance using ratios, including liquidity ratios such as the current and quick ratio, efficiency ratios such as inventory and receivable turnover, and gearing and coverage ratios.</p><p>The course also covers valuation ratios such as price-to-earnings and dividend yield, and how to compare ratios over time, against competitors and against industry benchmarks. You will learn the limitations of ratio analysis and how to avoid misleading conclusions. Practical exercises use real company financial statements. By the end, you will be able to perform a structured ratio analysis and use the results to support sound business and investment decisions.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C208' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 912;

-- C209 Automate Business Processes with Agentic AI Workflows
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Automate Business Processes with Agentic AI Workflows shows you how to use agentic AI and the n8n workflow automation platform to take repetitive, multi-step business processes off your team\'s plate. Unlike traditional automation that follows fixed rules, AI agents can reason, use tools and handle variation, such as reading an email, deciding what it needs and taking the right action. The course is designed for operations staff, business analysts, IT professionals and managers who want to build practical, reliable automations.</p><p>You will start with the fundamentals of agentic AI and n8n AI agents, understanding how agents reason, call tools and keep memory, and building your first AI agent workflows connected to apps such as email, spreadsheets and chat. Next you will learn webhook automation and human-in-the-loop workflows, triggering automations from forms, websites and other systems, and adding approval steps so people review and approve important decisions before the agent acts.</p><p>The final topic covers building an agentic RAG chatbot, where you connect an AI agent to your own documents and knowledge base so it can answer questions accurately with company-specific information. Throughout the course you will also learn how to test, monitor and secure your workflows and handle errors gracefully. Every topic is hands-on in n8n, using realistic business scenarios such as lead handling, customer enquiries and document processing. By the end, you will be able to design, build and deploy agentic AI workflows that automate real business processes.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C209' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1223;

-- C218 Arduino Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Arduino Masterclass gives you hands-on skills to design and build electronic and robotics projects with Arduino, the popular open-source microcontroller platform. Arduino makes it easy to read sensors, control motors and lights, and create interactive devices, which is why it is used by engineers, educators and makers worldwide. This masterclass is designed for beginners, engineering and technical staff, teachers and hobbyists who want to learn embedded systems and electronics through practical projects.</p><p>You will begin with an introduction to embedded systems, learning how microcontrollers work, setting up the Arduino IDE and writing your first programs. Next you will cover basic electronics, including voltage, current and resistance, using breadboards, reading circuit diagrams and safely connecting LEDs, buttons and resistors. You will then work with analogue sensors and transducers, such as light, temperature and potentiometer inputs, reading their values and converting them into meaningful measurements.</p><p>The course continues with digital sensors and transducers, including ultrasonic distance sensors, infrared sensors and digital temperature and humidity modules, followed by actuators, where you will control DC motors, servo motors, buzzers and relays. You will combine these skills to build simple robotics applications such as obstacle detection and line following. Every topic is hands-on with real components. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to design, program and build your own Arduino-based projects.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C218' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1065;

-- C233 Mastering Service Branding Strategies to Grow Your Business
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Mastering Service Branding Strategies to Grow Your Business shows you how to build a strong service brand that customers recognise, trust and recommend. In service businesses, the brand is delivered through every interaction, from your website and advertising to how your staff answer the phone, so branding is as much about people and processes as logos. The course is designed for business owners, marketing and customer experience professionals, and managers who want to use service branding to differentiate and grow.</p><p>You will start by understanding service branding and its business impact, exploring how it fits within an organisation\'s overall branding strategy and why consistent service experiences drive loyalty, referrals and pricing power. Next you will develop an appreciation for service branding in practice, defining your brand promise, values and personality, and identifying the touchpoints where customers experience your brand. You will analyse examples of service brands that excel and those that fall short.</p><p>The course then covers service branding communication strategy and customer experience, aligning marketing messages, staff behaviour and service standards so customers get what your brand promises. The final topic focuses on evaluating the impact of service branding initiatives, using customer feedback, satisfaction and loyalty measures to track results and improve. Practical activities let you apply each step to your own business. By the end, you will have a clear service branding plan to strengthen your brand and grow your business.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C233' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1021;

-- C239 ISO 9001:2015 Quality Management System
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>ISO 9001:2015 Quality Management System introduces you to the world\'s most widely adopted quality management standard and shows how it helps organisations deliver consistent products and services, satisfy customers and improve continuously. ISO 9001 certification is often a requirement for tenders and supplier approval, and a well-run quality management system (QMS) brings real operational benefits. The course is designed for managers, quality and operations staff, and anyone involved in implementing or maintaining an ISO 9001 QMS.</p><p>You will start with an overview of the ISO 9001 quality management system, covering the seven quality management principles, the process approach, risk-based thinking and the high-level structure of the standard, including context of the organisation and leadership. Next you will work through the planning, support and operation clauses, learning how to set quality objectives, address risks and opportunities, manage resources, competence and documented information, and control operational processes, suppliers and nonconforming outputs.</p><p>The course then covers performance evaluation, including monitoring and measurement, customer satisfaction, internal audits and management review, and finally continual improvement, with corrective action and improvement techniques. Practical examples and exercises show how each requirement applies in real organisations. By the end, you will understand the requirements of ISO 9001:2015 and be able to contribute effectively to implementing, maintaining and improving a quality management system.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C239' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 858;

-- C324 Generative AI for Agile Project Management
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Generative AI for Agile Project Management shows agile teams, Scrum Masters and product owners how to use generative AI tools such as ChatGPT, Claude and Gemini to plan, run and improve agile projects more effectively. AI can write user stories and acceptance criteria, refine backlogs, prepare sprint plans, summarise stand-ups and produce clear progress reports, giving the team more time to build and deliver value. The course is designed for agile practitioners, project managers and team members working in Scrum or Kanban environments.</p><p>You will start by getting started with generative AI for agile, understanding where AI fits into agile values and ceremonies, and learning prompting techniques that produce useful, structured outputs. Next you will use AI for backlogs, user stories and planning, turning requirements into epics and stories, writing acceptance criteria, estimating and prioritising work, and preparing for backlog refinement and release planning. You will then apply AI to sprints, stand-ups and delivery, including sprint goals, task breakdowns, impediment tracking and team communications.</p><p>The final topic covers AI for reporting, retrospectives and improvement, using AI to create burndown commentary and stakeholder updates, facilitate retrospectives and identify improvement actions. Throughout the course you will learn how to validate AI output and protect project information. All activities are hands-on with realistic agile scenarios. By the end, you will be able to use generative AI to make your agile team faster, better organised and more focused on delivering value.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C324' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 946;

-- C325 Microsoft Planner Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Microsoft Planner Masterclass teaches you how to plan, organise and track your team\'s work with Microsoft Planner, the task and project management app in Microsoft 365. Planner brings together simple task boards, timelines, schedules and project management features in one place, making it easy to see who is doing what and by when. The masterclass is designed for team leaders, project coordinators, managers and anyone who needs to manage tasks and small-scale projects efficiently using Microsoft 365.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to Microsoft Planner and its premium project management capabilities, and see how Planner connects with Microsoft Teams, Outlook and To Do. Next you will set up a plan, create buckets and tasks, assign team members, set due dates, priorities and labels, and add checklists, attachments and notes. You will then learn to schedule work using the board, grid, schedule and timeline views, choose between manual and automatic scheduling, and build a work breakdown structure for your project.</p><p>The course continues with identifying task relationships and dependencies, defining and assigning resources, tracking progress and using charts to spot bottlenecks before they cause delays. You will also learn how to share plans, collaborate in Teams and keep stakeholders informed. Every topic is hands-on with a realistic project. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to manage tasks and small projects confidently in Microsoft Planner and keep your team aligned and on schedule.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C325' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1295;

-- C329 Generative AI for Business Presentation
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Generative AI for Business Presentation shows you how to create clear, persuasive and visually striking business presentations in a fraction of the usual time. Using generative AI tools such as ChatGPT, Claude, Microsoft Copilot and AI slide generators, you will research a topic, structure a storyline, write compelling content and design professional slides, then rehearse your delivery. The course is designed for executives, managers, sales and marketing professionals, consultants and anyone who presents ideas, proposals or reports.</p><p>You will start by getting started with generative AI for presentations, understanding which tools to use for research, writing, design and images, and how to write prompts that produce structured, on-message content. You will use AI to analyse your audience, define key messages and build a logical storyline for pitches, project updates and proposals. Next you will design and deliver AI-powered presentations, generating slide drafts, data visualisations and images, refining layout and branding, and creating speaker notes.</p><p>Throughout the course you will also use AI as a rehearsal partner, anticipating questions, tightening your talking points and improving clarity and confidence. You will learn to check AI content for accuracy, keep your own voice and protect confidential information. All exercises are hands-on, so you finish with a presentation you have built yourself and reusable prompts. By the end, you will be able to use generative AI to prepare and deliver impactful business presentations quickly.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C329' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 707;

-- C337 Electrostatic Discharge Control (ESD) Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Electrostatic Discharge Control (ESD) Masterclass equips engineers, technicians and managers with the knowledge and skills to protect sensitive electronic components and assemblies from electrostatic discharge in laboratory and factory environments. ESD damage is often invisible, causing immediate failures or latent defects that surface later in the field, costing manufacturers yield, reputation and money. This masterclass is designed for electronics manufacturing, quality, engineering and facilities personnel responsible for ESD-safe operations.</p><p>You will begin with the basics of ESD, including how static charge is generated, triboelectric charging, induction, how ESD damages devices and the concept of ESD-sensitive items. Next you will study ESD control principles, equipment and practices, covering grounding, wrist straps, footwear and flooring, ESD mats, ionisers, packaging, handling procedures and setting up an ESD protected area (EPA). You will learn how each control element works and how they combine into an effective programme.</p><p>The course then covers ESD control standards, testing and auditing, with reference to ANSI/ESD S20.20 and IEC 61340-5-1, including how to verify equipment, measure resistance and conduct compliance audits. The final topic focuses on employee training and awareness, so ESD discipline becomes part of everyday behaviour. Practical demonstrations reinforce each topic. By the end, you will be able to implement, maintain and audit an effective ESD control programme in your organisation.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C337' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 823;

-- C348 ITIL 4 Foundation Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>ITIL 4 Foundation Training gives you a thorough understanding of ITIL 4, the world\'s most widely adopted framework for IT service management, and prepares you for the ITIL 4 Foundation certification exam. ITIL 4 helps organisations co-create value with customers by managing IT-enabled services in a flexible, coordinated and customer-focused way, integrating well with Agile, DevOps and Lean practices. The course is designed for IT professionals, service desk and operations staff, managers and anyone involved in delivering or supporting IT services.</p><p>You will start with the key concepts of service management, including value, outcomes, costs, risks, utility and warranty, and the relationships between service providers and consumers. Next you will explore how the seven ITIL guiding principles help organisations adopt and adapt service management, and the four dimensions of service management: organisations and people, information and technology, partners and suppliers, and value streams and processes. You will then study the purpose and components of the ITIL service value system and the activities of the service value chain.</p><p>The course also covers the purpose and key terms of important ITIL practices, such as incident, problem, change enablement, service request, service level and continual improvement management. Throughout the course you will work through practice questions and exam strategies. By the end, you will understand how ITIL 4 creates value through IT services and be well prepared to sit and pass the ITIL 4 Foundation exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C348' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1257;

-- C349 Multi AI Agents System for Digital Marketing
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Multi AI Agents System for Digital Marketing shows you how to put a whole team of AI agents to work on your marketing. Instead of one person prompting a chatbot for one caption at a time, a multi-agent system assigns specialised agents to market research, SEO and content, social media, advertising and analytics, and coordinates them so campaigns move from insight to execution with far less manual effort. The course is designed for digital marketers, marketing managers, agency teams and business owners who want to scale their marketing output intelligently.</p><p>You will start with multi-agent foundations for marketing: how AI agents reason, use tools and hand work to one another, and how to design roles, instructions and guardrails for a marketing agent team. Next you will build research and content agents that analyse competitors and audiences, identify keywords and trends, and draft blog posts, social content and email copy in your brand voice. You will then create campaign execution agents that plan content calendars, prepare ad variations, schedule posts and coordinate multi-channel launches.</p><p>The final topic covers analytics and optimisation, where agents pull performance data, summarise results, flag what is and is not working and recommend next actions. Throughout the course you will keep humans in the loop for approvals, brand consistency and compliance, and learn how to monitor and improve agent quality over time. Every topic is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to design and run a multi AI agents system that makes your digital marketing faster, more consistent and more data-driven.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C349' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1366;

-- C355 Agentic AI for Google Ads
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Agentic AI for Google Ads shows you how to use AI agents and generative AI tools to research, build, optimise and scale Google Ads campaigns that drive more conversions for less effort. Managing search and Performance Max campaigns involves constant keyword research, copywriting, bid and budget decisions and reporting; AI agents can take on much of this work while you focus on strategy and results. The course is designed for digital marketers, business owners, agency staff and anyone responsible for paid search performance.</p><p>You will start by getting started with agentic AI for Google Ads, reviewing how Google Ads works, how AI agents can connect to your account data and how to write effective briefs and prompts. Next you will use AI for keyword research and ad copy, discovering high-intent keywords, grouping them into tightly themed ad groups, identifying negative keywords and generating responsive search ad headlines and descriptions. You will then build and optimise campaigns with AI, setting up campaign structure, targeting, bidding strategies and conversion tracking.</p><p>The final topic covers automating and scaling Google Ads with AI agents, including monitoring performance, analysing search terms, recommending bid and budget changes, running ad tests and producing clear reports. Throughout the course you will keep human approval on spend and brand decisions and learn to verify AI recommendations against real data. All exercises are hands-on. By the end, you will be able to use agentic AI to run Google Ads campaigns more efficiently and achieve a better return on ad spend.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C355' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 902;

-- C356 AI for Network Security
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI for Network Security equips you with practical skills to apply artificial intelligence to protecting an organisation\'s network. Attackers are already using automation and AI, and defenders face ever-growing volumes of alerts, logs and vulnerabilities; AI helps security teams detect threats earlier, prioritise risks and respond faster. The course is designed for network and system administrators, security analysts, IT managers and engineers who want to strengthen network defence with AI-assisted tools and techniques.</p><p>You will start with AI-assisted network threat and vulnerability analysis, using AI to analyse traffic patterns and logs, detect anomalies and suspicious behaviour, and interpret vulnerability scan results. Next you will cover AI-powered network risk assessment and management, prioritising vulnerabilities by likelihood and impact, mapping threats to frameworks such as MITRE ATT&amp;CK, and recommending mitigations. You will then design and implement AI-enhanced network security, including segmentation, firewall and access policies, intrusion detection and automated monitoring workflows.</p><p>The final topic covers AI-assisted security incident documentation and response, using AI to triage alerts, summarise incidents, draft response playbooks and prepare clear reports for management. Throughout the course you will also learn the limitations and risks of AI in security, how to validate AI findings and how to protect sensitive data. Hands-on labs use realistic network scenarios. By the end, you will be able to apply AI confidently to monitor, assess and secure network environments.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C356' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1321;

-- C385 Github Foundations Certification Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Github Foundations Certification Training prepares you for the GitHub Foundations certification while giving you the practical Git and GitHub skills used by developers and technical teams every day. The certification validates your understanding of version control, repositories, collaboration workflows and the wider GitHub platform. This course is designed for developers, students, IT professionals, data practitioners and project contributors who want to collaborate professionally on GitHub and earn an industry-recognised credential.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to Git and GitHub, covering version control concepts, commits, branches and the GitHub interface. Next you will work with GitHub repositories, creating and cloning repositories, managing files, writing README and markdown documentation, and pushing and pulling changes. You will then explore collaboration features, including issues, pull requests, code reviews, discussions, forks and resolving merge conflicts, so you can contribute confidently to team and open-source projects.</p><p>The course continues with modern development on GitHub, including GitHub Actions, Codespaces and GitHub Copilot, followed by GitHub Projects for planning and tracking work. The final topic covers privacy, security and administration, such as repository visibility, permissions, branch protection, Dependabot and organisation settings. Throughout the course you will practise with exam-style questions and review key concepts. By the end, you will be confident using GitHub in real projects and well prepared to pass the GitHub Foundations certification exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C385' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 716;

-- C387 Adobe Premiere Pro Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Adobe Premiere Pro Masterclass teaches you how to edit professional-quality videos with Adobe Premiere Pro, the industry-standard video editing software used for film, television, corporate and social media content. Whether you are producing marketing videos, training content, vlogs or event highlights, Premiere Pro gives you the tools to tell a compelling story with polished sound and visuals. The masterclass is designed for beginners, content creators, marketers and communications staff who want to edit videos efficiently and professionally.</p><p>You will begin by getting started with Premiere Pro, setting up projects and sequences, importing and organising media, and understanding the editing workspace and timeline. Next you will learn shot editing, including trimming, cutting, ripple and roll edits, and arranging clips to build a clear narrative. You will then cover audio and graphics editing, cleaning up and balancing sound, adding music and voiceovers, and creating titles, lower thirds and simple motion graphics with the Essential Graphics panel.</p><p>The course continues with clip and colour editing, applying transitions and effects, adjusting speed, and using Lumetri Color for colour correction and grading. The final topic covers the final touch-up, including captions, reviewing your edit and exporting your video in the right formats for YouTube, social media and presentations. Every topic is hands-on. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to plan, edit and export engaging, professional videos in Adobe Premiere Pro.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C387' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 861;

-- C391 AutoCAD Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AutoCAD Masterclass gives you practical, hands-on skills to create accurate 2D technical drawings with AutoCAD, the world\'s leading computer-aided design software for engineering, architecture, construction and manufacturing. AutoCAD lets you draft precise plans, layouts and details that can be shared, revised and printed to scale. This masterclass is designed for beginners, draughtspersons, engineers, architects, designers and technical staff who want to produce professional drawings efficiently.</p><p>You will begin by getting started with AutoCAD, learning the interface, drawing setup, units, coordinate systems and the essential draw and modify commands such as line, circle, offset, trim, extend and fillet. Next you will move into technical drawing with AutoCAD, using layers, object snaps, polar tracking, blocks and hatching to build accurate orthographic drawings and plans. You will then create part lists, adding attributes, tables and bills of materials linked to your drawing components.</p><p>The course continues with design documentation, covering dimensions, text, annotation styles, layouts, viewports and plotting drawings to scale, followed by design specification, where you will apply standards, title blocks and drawing conventions so your work is clear and consistent. Every topic includes guided exercises based on real engineering and architectural examples. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to produce, annotate and publish professional 2D technical drawings in AutoCAD with confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C391' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 843;

-- C398 AI for Shopify eCommerce
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI for Shopify eCommerce shows you how to build, manage and grow a Shopify online store with artificial intelligence. Shopify makes it easy to sell online, and AI tools, including Shopify Magic and AI vibe coding assistants, can speed up store setup, write product content, personalise the customer experience and turn sales data into decisions. The course is designed for entrepreneurs, small business owners, eCommerce executives and marketers who want a professional Shopify store that runs efficiently and sells more.</p><p>You will start with AI vibe coding for eCommerce store setup and customisation, configuring your store, choosing and adjusting a theme and using AI to draft pages, policies and simple code changes. Next you will manage your product catalogue and web content, using AI to create product titles, descriptions, images and SEO metadata at scale. You will then use AI to improve the storefront and customer experience, with better navigation, search, recommendations and customer support chat.</p><p>The course continues with shopping cart, checkout and order management, followed by payment, tax, shipping and fulfilment settings, and AI-assisted marketing, promotions and analytics. You will learn to read Shopify reports, use AI to interpret trends and decide what to improve next. Every topic is hands-on, so you finish with a working store you have configured yourself. By the end, you will be able to launch and run a Shopify eCommerce store with confidence and use AI to save time and grow sales.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C398' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1487;

-- C402 CompTIA Tech+ Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>CompTIA Tech+ Training prepares you for the CompTIA Tech+ certification (exam FC0-U71), the entry-level credential that replaced CompTIA IT Fundamentals (ITF+). Tech+ validates the foundational knowledge needed to work with technology confidently, from hardware and networks to software, data and security. The course is ideal for students, career switchers, non-technical professionals working with IT teams, and anyone starting a career in technology who wants a recognised first certification.</p><p>You will start with IT concepts and terminology, including notational systems, units of measure, the basics of computing and troubleshooting methodology. Next you will cover infrastructure: computer components, peripherals, storage, networking concepts, wireless and wired connectivity, and cloud and virtualisation fundamentals. You will then explore applications and software, including operating systems, common business software and how software is installed and managed, followed by software development concepts such as programming languages, logic and basic data structures.</p><p>The course continues with data and database fundamentals, explaining the value of data, database types and simple queries, and closes with security, covering confidentiality, integrity and availability, authentication, malware, safe browsing and best practices for protecting devices and data. Each domain is mapped to the official exam objectives and reinforced with practice questions. By the end, you will have a solid IT foundation and be well prepared to pass the CompTIA Tech+ exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C402' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1428;

-- C427 ChatGPT WORK Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>ChatGPT WORK Masterclass shows you how to use ChatGPT Work, the agentic work mode in the ChatGPT desktop app, to take repetitive, multi-step tasks off your plate. Rather than chatting one prompt at a time, ChatGPT Work can plan a task, work through it step by step with your files, documents and connected apps, and return a finished deliverable for you to review. The masterclass is designed for professionals, managers, analysts and administrators who want to save time on everyday knowledge work without writing code.</p><p>You will start by getting started with ChatGPT Work: setting it up, understanding how it differs from standard ChatGPT chat and from Codex, and learning how to write clear task briefs with goals, context, sources and the output you expect. You will practise giving ChatGPT Work access to the right files and tools while keeping control through permissions and approvals. Next you will automate real work tasks, such as researching and summarising information, drafting reports and emails, organising and analysing spreadsheet data, and preparing presentations.</p><p>Throughout the masterclass you will learn how to review and refine ChatGPT Work\'s output, break large jobs into reliable steps, reuse successful instructions and keep sensitive information protected. Every activity is hands-on with realistic workplace scenarios, so you leave with workflows you can apply immediately. By the end, you will be able to use ChatGPT Work confidently as an AI teammate that completes routine tasks quickly and accurately while you focus on higher-value work.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C427' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1232;

-- C428 AI Vibe Coding for REST API
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI Vibe Coding for REST API teaches you how to build production-grade REST APIs with Python and FastAPI by directing AI coding assistants such as Cursor, GitHub Copilot and Claude instead of typing every line yourself. Vibe coding lets you describe what you want in plain English, review the code the AI produces and steer it until it meets your requirements. The course is designed for developers, data professionals and technical learners who want to create reliable APIs faster with AI assistance.</p><p>You will start with the AI vibe coding workflow and FastAPI project set-up, learning how to plan an API, prompt an AI assistant effectively, structure a project and run a development server. Next you will design REST endpoints and data models with AI, applying REST principles, HTTP methods and status codes, and using Pydantic for request validation and response models. You will then integrate a database and add authentication with vibe coding, connecting to SQL databases, implementing CRUD operations and securing endpoints with token-based authentication.</p><p>The final topic covers testing, documenting and shipping your API, including automated tests with pytest, interactive OpenAPI documentation, error handling and deploying your API to the cloud. Throughout the course you will learn to review AI-generated code critically, catch security issues and keep your project maintainable. Every topic is hands-on, building a complete API from start to finish. By the end, you will be able to design, build, test and deploy REST APIs efficiently using AI vibe coding.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C428' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1053;

-- C430 AI Vibe Coding for Machine Learning
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI Vibe Coding for Machine Learning shows you how to build, train, evaluate and deploy machine learning models by directing AI coding assistants such as Cursor, GitHub Copilot and Claude. Instead of memorising every library function, you describe your goal in plain English, review the Python code the AI writes and guide it until your model performs well. The course is designed for analysts, developers, engineers and data enthusiasts who want to apply machine learning to real problems faster and with confidence.</p><p>You will start by getting started with AI vibe coding for machine learning, setting up your environment and learning how to prompt an AI assistant to load, explore and prepare data with pandas and scikit-learn. Next you will build and train models with AI, covering regression, classification and clustering, feature engineering and train-test splits, and introducing neural networks with TensorFlow or PyTorch. You will then evaluate and improve your models, using appropriate metrics, cross-validation, hyperparameter tuning and techniques to reduce overfitting.</p><p>The final topic covers deploying machine learning with AI, packaging your model, serving predictions through a simple API or web app and planning for monitoring and retraining. Throughout the course you will learn to check AI-generated code carefully, understand what each step does and avoid common pitfalls such as data leakage. All exercises are hands-on with real datasets. By the end, you will be able to use AI vibe coding to deliver working machine learning solutions from data to deployment.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C430' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1086;

-- C431 AI for Career Coaching
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI for Career Coaching equips coaches, HR professionals and managers with the knowledge and AI-enabled tools to guide individuals through their career development more effectively. Generative AI can help analyse skills and experience, research career pathways and labour market trends, draft development plans and prepare personalised coaching materials, giving coaches more time for meaningful conversations. The course is designed for career coaches, HR and talent development professionals, people managers and educators.</p><p>You will start with career development principles, including career theories, the stages of a career, motivation and the role of a career coach, and how AI can support each stage. Next you will assess employee competencies, using structured tools and AI to analyse skills, strengths, interests and gaps, and to map them against job roles and skills frameworks. You will then cover career management, using AI to explore career options, research industries and roles, and help clients set realistic goals and action plans.</p><p>The final topic focuses on supporting career plan implementation, including coaching conversations, monitoring progress, preparing resumes and interview practice with AI assistance, and adjusting plans as circumstances change. Throughout the course you will also discuss ethics, privacy and bias when using AI with personal data, and how to keep human judgement and empathy at the centre of coaching. By the end, you will be able to use AI responsibly to deliver more effective and personalised career coaching.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C431' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1055;

-- C434 AI for Cyber Security
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI for Cyber Security gives you practical knowledge of how artificial intelligence is transforming cyber defence, from threat detection and security analysis to incident response and governance. Organisations face growing volumes of attacks and alerts, and AI helps security teams see threats sooner, prioritise risks and act faster, while also introducing new risks that must be managed. The course is designed for security analysts, IT managers, risk and compliance professionals and technology leaders who want to apply AI to strengthen their security posture.</p><p>You will start with AI-assisted security risk, threat and control analysis, using AI to analyse threat intelligence, logs and vulnerabilities, assess risks and evaluate the effectiveness of existing controls. Next you will design AI-powered cybersecurity programmes, defining objectives, use cases and processes for applying AI to areas such as detection, phishing defence and vulnerability management. You will then develop AI-driven security architecture and operations, integrating AI into monitoring, security operations centre workflows and automated response.</p><p>The final topic covers monitoring, evaluating and governing AI security, including measuring the performance of AI tools, managing risks such as prompt injection, data leakage and model manipulation, and aligning with policies and regulations. Throughout the course you will work with realistic scenarios and case studies. By the end, you will be able to identify where AI adds the most value in cyber security, design practical AI-enabled security measures and govern their use responsibly.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C434' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1366;

-- C436 Agentic AI for Video Creation
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Agentic AI for Video Creation shows you how to produce short-form videos at scale by building AI agent workflows that plan, script, generate and edit content for social media, marketing and training. Video is the most engaging format online, but producing it consistently takes time and specialist skills; AI agents can handle much of the research, writing, generation and assembly so you can publish more, faster. The course is designed for marketers, content creators, social media managers, trainers and business owners.</p><p>You will start by getting started with agentic AI for video, exploring the current AI video, voice and image tools, how AI agents coordinate multi-step tasks and how to define your content strategy and brand style. Next you will script and generate content with AI, researching topics and trends, writing hooks and scripts, creating voiceovers and generating video clips, avatars and visuals from prompts. You will then edit and assemble videos with AI, adding captions, music, transitions and branding, and adapting formats for TikTok, Instagram Reels, YouTube Shorts and LinkedIn.</p><p>The final topic covers automating and scaling video production, building an end-to-end agent workflow that turns an idea or article into a finished video, with human review before publishing. Throughout the course you will also cover copyright, disclosure and responsible use of AI-generated media. Every topic is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to run an efficient AI-powered video production pipeline that consistently delivers engaging short-form content.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C436' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 757;

-- C437 Claude Certified Architect - Foundations Certification
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Claude Certified Architect - Foundations Certification prepares you for the Claude Certified Architect - Foundations exam (CCAR-F), which validates that you can make sound design decisions and tradeoffs when building real-world, production-grade solutions with Claude. The certification is aimed at developers, solution architects, AI engineers and technical leads who design applications, agents and workflows on Anthropic\'s platform and want to demonstrate their expertise with an industry-recognised credential.</p><p>The course follows the official exam domains. You will start with agentic architecture and orchestration, covering agent loops, single and multi-agent patterns, subagents and when to use workflows versus autonomous agents. Next you will study tool design and Model Context Protocol (MCP) integration, including writing clear tool definitions, handling tool results and connecting Claude to external systems securely. You will then cover Claude Code configuration and workflows, such as project instructions, permissions, hooks, skills and automation in the development lifecycle.</p><p>The course continues with prompt engineering and structured output, including system prompts, examples, reasoning and reliable JSON output, and closes with context management and reliability, covering context windows, caching, memory, evaluation, error handling and guardrails. Each domain combines explanation, architecture scenarios and exam-style practice questions. By the end, you will be able to design robust Claude-based systems with confidence and be well prepared to pass the Claude Certified Architect - Foundations exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C437' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1269;

-- C439 Generative AI for Content Creation
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Generative AI for Content Creation shows you how to plan, produce and manage high-quality content with generative AI tools such as ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and AI image generators, guided by a clear content strategy. AI can help you brainstorm ideas, draft articles and social posts, create visuals and repurpose content across channels, but quality, accuracy and brand consistency still depend on human judgement. The course is designed for marketers, communications professionals, content writers, business owners and creators.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to content strategy and AI generation, defining goals, audiences, channels and brand voice, and learning how to brief generative AI tools to produce on-strategy blog posts, newsletters, social media content, scripts and images. You will build prompt templates and workflows that make content production faster and more consistent. Next you will evaluate AI-generated content, checking it for accuracy, originality, tone, readability and alignment with your objectives, and editing it into publish-ready work.</p><p>The final topic covers the ethical and legal concerns of managing AI-generated content, including copyright and intellectual property, disclosure, bias, misinformation and data privacy, and how to set guidelines and review processes for your team. Throughout the course you will work on hands-on exercises using your own brand or a sample business. By the end, you will be able to use generative AI to create compelling content efficiently while managing quality and risk responsibly.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C439' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1107;

-- C440 Statistics Fundamentals Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Statistics Fundamentals Masterclass gives you a clear, practical understanding of the statistical concepts and techniques used to make sense of data and support sound decisions. Statistics underpins data analysis, research, quality improvement, finance and marketing, yet many professionals find it intimidating. This masterclass explains each concept step by step with real examples and is designed for analysts, researchers, managers, students and anyone who needs to interpret data or reports with confidence.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to statistics, covering types of data, measures of central tendency and spread, distributions and how to summarise and visualise data. Next you will learn about sampling, including sampling methods, sampling error, the central limit theorem and confidence intervals. You will then move into hypothesis testing, understanding null and alternative hypotheses, p-values, significance levels and errors, and applying t-tests to compare groups, followed by the chi-square test for categorical data and relationships between variables.</p><p>The later topics cover ANOVA (analysis of variance) for comparing more than two groups, regression for modelling and predicting relationships, and correlation analysis for measuring the strength of associations. Every topic includes hands-on exercises using Excel or statistical software and practical interpretation of results. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to choose and apply the right statistical method, interpret results correctly and communicate findings clearly to support better decisions.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C440' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 839;

-- C469 Tableau Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Tableau Masterclass teaches you how to turn data into clear, interactive visual stories with Tableau, one of the world\'s leading data visualisation and business intelligence tools. Tableau lets you connect to almost any data source, explore it visually and share dashboards that help decision-makers see what matters at a glance. The masterclass is designed for analysts, managers, business users and anyone who works with data and wants to communicate insights more effectively.</p><p>You will start with basic Tableau features, connecting to data, understanding dimensions and measures, and building your first charts with drag-and-drop. Next you will cover data visualisation, creating bar, line, scatter, map and other chart types and applying best practices for colour, labels and layout. You will then learn data transformation in Tableau, including joins, relationships, unions, pivots, groups, sets and hierarchies, so your data is structured correctly for analysis.</p><p>The course continues with dashboards and stories, combining views into interactive dashboards with filters and actions, and building story points that guide your audience through your findings. You will also master calculations and parameters, including calculated fields, table calculations, level of detail expressions and what-if analysis, and finish with analytics features such as trend lines, forecasts and clustering. Every topic is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to design compelling, insightful dashboards in Tableau.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C469' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 810;

-- C476 CompTIA DataAI Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>CompTIA DataAI Training prepares you for CompTIA DataAI (formerly CompTIA DataX), the expert-level certification that validates the advanced data science and artificial intelligence skills needed to build, deploy and operate real-world data and AI solutions. It is designed for experienced data scientists, machine learning engineers, analysts and technical professionals who want to demonstrate mastery across the full data science lifecycle with a vendor-neutral credential.</p><p>The course follows the official exam domains. You will start with mathematics and statistics, including probability, distributions, hypothesis testing, linear algebra and calculus concepts that underpin modern models. Next you will cover modelling, analysis and outcomes, such as exploratory data analysis, feature engineering, model selection, evaluation metrics and communicating results to stakeholders. You will then study machine learning in depth, including supervised and unsupervised learning, ensemble methods, deep learning and generative AI concepts.</p><p>The course continues with operations and processes, covering data pipelines, MLOps, deployment, monitoring, model drift and governance, and closes with specialised applications of data science, such as natural language processing, computer vision, time series and optimisation. Each domain combines concept reviews, worked scenarios and exam-style practice questions. By the end, you will have consolidated your advanced data and AI expertise and be well prepared to pass the CompTIA DataAI certification exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C476' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 936;

-- C481 Certified Lean Six Sigma Green Belt (CLSSGB)
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Certified Lean Six Sigma Green Belt (CLSSGB) gives you the knowledge and tools to lead process improvement projects using the Lean Six Sigma DMAIC methodology. Green Belts play a key role in organisations, identifying problems, analysing data and implementing improvements that reduce defects, waste and cost while increasing customer satisfaction. The course is designed for engineers, quality and operations professionals, supervisors and managers who want to lead improvement projects and earn the Certified Lean Six Sigma Green Belt credential.</p><p>You will start with Six Sigma and organisational goals, understanding how improvement projects link to strategy, and Lean principles in the organisation, including value, waste, flow and pull. You will also be introduced to Design for Six Sigma (DFSS). Next you will cover the Define phase, project management basics and other Define tools, such as project charters, voice of the customer, SIPOC and stakeholder analysis. The course then moves through the Measure phase, covering process mapping, data collection, basic statistics, measurement system analysis and process capability.</p><p>You will then apply Analyse phase tools to find root causes, including hypothesis testing, correlation and regression, followed by the Improve and Control phases, where you will select and pilot solutions and sustain gains with control charts and control plans. Practical exercises and case studies reinforce every phase. By the end, you will be able to lead Green Belt improvement projects confidently and be prepared to sit for the CLSSGB certification exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C481' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 825;

-- C485 AI Vibe Coding for Geofencing
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI Vibe Coding for Geofencing teaches you how to build location-aware applications by directing AI coding assistants such as Cursor, GitHub Copilot and Claude. Geofencing triggers actions when a device enters or leaves a defined area, powering use cases such as attendance tracking, delivery notifications, field service, asset monitoring and location-based marketing. The course is designed for developers, technical professionals and product builders who want to create mapping and geofencing solutions faster with AI.</p><p>You will start by getting started with AI vibe coding for geofencing, setting up your tools and learning how to prompt an AI assistant to plan, write and debug code. You will understand GPS, coordinates and location services on web and mobile. Next you will build maps and location features with AI, displaying interactive maps, markers and routes, capturing a user\'s location and drawing geofence areas as circles and polygons. You will then implement geofencing logic and real-time events, detecting entry and exit, handling accuracy and battery considerations, and sending alerts and notifications.</p><p>The final topic covers building and deploying a complete geofencing app with AI, adding a backend to store locations and events, a simple dashboard and deployment to the cloud. Throughout the course you will learn to review AI-generated code, test location features and handle privacy and consent for location data responsibly. Every topic is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to build and deploy working geofencing applications using AI vibe coding.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C485' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1057;

-- C506 Cyber Security Awareness Workshop
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Cyber Security Awareness Workshop shows you how to recognise and defend against the cyber threats that target individuals and businesses every day. Most successful attacks start with a human mistake, such as clicking a phishing link, reusing a password or installing a malicious app, so security awareness is one of the most effective defences an organisation can have. This workshop is designed for employees at every level, managers, small business owners and anyone who wants to stay safe online.</p><p>You will start with cyber security threats, learning how phishing, social engineering, malware, ransomware, scams, identity theft and data breaches work, with real-world examples of how attackers operate. Next you will cover protection against cyber security threats, including creating strong passwords and using a password manager, enabling multi-factor authentication, securing devices and home networks, safe browsing and email habits, protecting personal data on social media and recognising scam messages and calls.</p><p>The final topic focuses on security management for businesses, covering basic security policies, data protection obligations, secure remote working, backups, incident reporting and building a security-aware culture in your team. The workshop uses interactive examples, quizzes and practical demonstrations. By the end, you will be able to spot common cyber threats, apply practical safeguards to protect yourself and your organisation, and know what to do if something goes wrong.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C506' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 975;

-- C508 Autodesk Revit Architecture Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Autodesk Revit Architecture Masterclass teaches you how to design, document and coordinate building projects using Autodesk Revit and Building Information Modelling (BIM). Unlike traditional 2D drafting, Revit builds an intelligent 3D model in which plans, sections, elevations and schedules update automatically when the design changes. This masterclass is designed for architects, architectural designers, draughtspersons, engineers and construction professionals who want to work productively in BIM.</p><p>You will start with design modelling in Revit, learning the interface, project setup, levels and grids, and creating walls, doors, windows, floors, roofs, ceilings, stairs and railings to build a complete architectural model. You will work with families and views to control how your design is displayed. Next you will create part lists for modelling in Revit, generating schedules and quantities for doors, windows, rooms and materials directly from the model.</p><p>The course then covers model documentation, including dimensions, tags, annotations, sections, elevations, detail views and sheet layouts, so you can produce a professional drawing set. The final topic focuses on design specification, applying standards, materials and parameters and preparing your model for collaboration and export. Every topic is hands-on with a realistic building project, developed step by step. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to model, document and present architectural designs in Autodesk Revit with confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C508' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 861;

-- C523 Project Management Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Project Management Masterclass equips you with the practical knowledge and tools to plan, lead and deliver projects successfully from start to finish. Built around the project lifecycle and globally recognised good practice from the Project Management Institute (PMI), it also provides a strong foundation for those working towards the Project Management Professional (PMP) certification. The masterclass is designed for project managers, team leads, coordinators and professionals who manage projects as part of their role.</p><p>You will start with the business environment, understanding how projects deliver value, align with strategy and operate within governance, compliance and organisational change. Next you will learn how to start the project, defining objectives, identifying stakeholders and developing the project charter. You will then plan the project in detail, covering scope and work breakdown structures, schedules, budgets, resources, quality, communications and risk management, using both predictive and agile approaches where appropriate.</p><p>The course continues with executing the project, including leading and motivating teams, managing stakeholders and resolving conflict, followed by monitoring and controlling the project, where you will track progress, manage changes, issues and risks and report performance. The final topic covers closing the project, capturing lessons learned and handing over deliverables. Case studies and practical exercises reinforce every stage. By the end, you will be able to manage projects with greater structure, confidence and success.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C523' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 911;

-- C524 Certified Lean Six Sigma Yellow Belt (CLSSYB)
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Certified Lean Six Sigma Yellow Belt (CLSSYB) gives you a solid understanding of Lean, Six Sigma and Kaizen principles and the skills to contribute meaningfully to process improvement projects. Yellow Belts support Green and Black Belt projects, collect and analyse data, and lead small improvements in their own work areas. The course is designed for team members, supervisors, administrators and professionals in any industry who want to improve quality and efficiency and earn the Certified Lean Six Sigma Yellow Belt credential.</p><p>You will start with the Define phase, covering the fundamentals of Six Sigma and Lean, the types of waste, voice of the customer, process mapping and how improvement projects are selected and scoped with a project charter. Next you will move into the Measure phase, learning about process definition, basic statistics, data types and collection, measurement system basics and process capability, so you can quantify how a process is really performing.</p><p>The course then covers the Control phase, including Lean controls, 5S, mistake-proofing, standard work, statistical process control and control plans that sustain improvements over time. Throughout the course you will see how Analyse and Improve activities fit within the full DMAIC framework, and practise with real-world examples and group exercises. By the end, you will be able to apply Lean Six Sigma tools in your daily work, support improvement teams effectively and be prepared for the CLSSYB certification exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C524' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 995;

-- C525 Finance for Non-Finance Managers
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Finance for Non-Finance Managers helps managers and professionals without a financial background understand the numbers that drive business decisions. You will learn how to read and interpret financial statements, analyse profitability and cash flow, and use financial information to plan, evaluate options and communicate confidently with finance colleagues. The course is designed for managers, department heads, project leaders, entrepreneurs and professionals who are responsible for budgets or performance.</p><p>You will start with the process of financial statement analysis, understanding how the income statement, balance sheet and cash flow statement fit together and what each tells you about an organisation. Next you will learn the different financial ratios used to measure liquidity, efficiency, gearing and returns, and apply them in profitability analysis to see where a business makes and loses money. You will then explore cash flow analysis, understanding why profitable companies can still run out of cash and how to manage working capital.</p><p>The course also covers preparing projected financial and cash flow statements, using financial analysis to determine the health of an organisation, and evaluating its historical performance to inform future plans. Practical exercises use real company figures and simple case studies relevant to everyday management decisions. By the end, you will be able to interpret financial information with confidence, contribute to budgeting and planning, and make better-informed decisions for your team and organisation.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C525' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1080;

-- C526 No Code and Low Code Agentic AI Applications
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>No Code and Low Code Agentic AI Applications shows you how to build agentic AI applications with n8n, using visual no-code and low-code approaches instead of traditional programming. AI agents can reason, use tools, connect to business applications and carry out multi-step tasks, and n8n lets you assemble them by connecting nodes on a canvas. The course is designed for business users, operations staff, analysts, IT professionals and entrepreneurs who want to automate work with AI agents without becoming full-time developers.</p><p>You will start by developing no-code agentic AI workflows, learning the n8n interface, triggers, nodes and credentials, and building AI agents that read emails and forms, look up information, make decisions and update spreadsheets, CRMs and chat tools. Next you will develop low-code agentic AI workflows, adding small snippets of JavaScript or Python, calling APIs with HTTP requests, using webhooks and giving agents memory and custom tools to handle more complex logic.</p><p>The final topic covers real-life applications of agentic AI workflows, such as customer support assistants, lead qualification, document processing, report generation and knowledge-base chatbots, with human-in-the-loop approvals for important actions. Throughout the course you will also learn how to test, monitor and secure your workflows and manage costs. Every topic is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to design, build and deploy practical agentic AI applications using n8n with confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C526' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1515;

-- C529 Customer Service Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Customer Service Masterclass equips you with the skills and mindset to deliver consistently excellent service that keeps customers satisfied, loyal and willing to recommend your business. Great customer service is a major competitive advantage, and it depends on understanding customer needs, communicating effectively and handling difficult situations with professionalism. The masterclass is designed for frontline staff, customer service officers, supervisors, sales and retail teams, and anyone who interacts with customers.</p><p>You will start by understanding who your customers are and what your organisation does for them, including customer expectations and the moments that shape their experience. Next you will focus on establishing the right attitude, building a positive, customer-centred mindset and managing your own emotions under pressure. You will then learn how to identify and address the customer\'s needs, using active listening, questioning and empathy, and collecting and analysing customer feedback to improve service.</p><p>The course continues with in-person customer service, covering body language, first impressions and face-to-face communication, and customer service over the phone, including tone, call handling and following up. You will also practise managing complaints and difficult customers and turning service failures into opportunities. Role plays and real-life scenarios bring each topic to life. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to deliver professional, empathetic service across channels and strengthen customer loyalty.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C529' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 877;

-- C538 Basic Accounting using Xero
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Basic Accounting using Xero gives you hands-on skills to manage your business accounts in Xero, the popular cloud accounting software used by small and medium-sized businesses. You will learn how to set up Xero, record everyday transactions accurately, handle Goods and Services Tax and produce the financial reports needed to run the business and meet compliance requirements. The course is designed for SME owners, administrative and accounts staff, and anyone new to Xero or to basic bookkeeping.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to the Xero accounting system, covering the dashboard, organisation settings, chart of accounts, contacts and how to import existing data. Next you will input data into Xero, creating quotes and sales invoices, recording customer payments, entering bills and expenses, and managing bank accounts. You will learn how to connect bank feeds, use bank rules and complete bank reconciliations so your records always match your bank statements.</p><p>The course then covers managing Goods and Services Tax in Xero, including setting up tax rates, applying GST correctly to sales and purchases and preparing GST returns. The final topic focuses on financial and accounting reports, such as the profit and loss statement, balance sheet, aged receivables and payables, and how to customise and interpret them. Practical exercises use a realistic sample company and its transactions. By the end, you will be able to keep accurate books in Xero and produce reliable financial reports with confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C538' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 690;

-- C539 AI Vibe Coding for Deep Learning
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI Vibe Coding for Deep Learning shows you how to build real deep learning models with PyTorch by directing AI coding assistants such as Cursor, GitHub Copilot and Claude, instead of writing every line yourself. You describe what you want in plain English, review the code the AI produces and guide it until the model works, which lets you focus on understanding the concepts and results. The course is designed for developers, data scientists, engineers and technical learners with basic Python knowledge.</p><p>You will start with AI vibe coding for PyTorch fundamentals, setting up your environment and using AI to work with tensors, automatic differentiation, datasets and data loaders. Next you will vibe code neural networks, building, training and evaluating feedforward networks, choosing loss functions and optimisers, and tackling overfitting with regularisation and dropout. You will then vibe code convolutional neural networks for image classification, applying data augmentation and transfer learning with pre-trained models.</p><p>The final topic covers recurrent networks for sequence data, including RNNs, LSTMs and GRUs for time series and text, and an introduction to attention and transformers. Throughout the course you will learn to read and check AI-generated code, debug training problems, track experiments and interpret model performance. Every topic is hands-on with real datasets. By the end, you will be able to use AI vibe coding to build, train and improve deep learning models in PyTorch efficiently and with understanding.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C539' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1041;

-- C544 Blockchain Fundamentals Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Blockchain Fundamentals Masterclass gives you a clear, practical understanding of blockchain technology and how it powers cryptocurrencies, smart contracts and decentralised applications (dApps). Blockchain enables trusted, tamper-resistant records without a central authority, with applications in finance, supply chains, digital identity and more. The masterclass is designed for business professionals, developers, IT staff, entrepreneurs and anyone who wants to understand blockchain and Web3 beyond the headlines, with a hands-on, AI-assisted approach to building.</p><p>You will start with the fundamentals of blockchain, cryptocurrency, smart contracts and Web3, covering how blocks, hashing, consensus mechanisms, public and private keys and wallets work, and the differences between major networks such as Bitcoin and Ethereum. You will also discuss real-world use cases, benefits and limitations. Next you will develop a simple dApp using vibe coding, directing AI coding assistants to write a Solidity smart contract and connect it to a web front end.</p><p>The course continues with smart contract testing, learning how to test contracts on a local blockchain and identify common security vulnerabilities, followed by smart contract deployment to a test network and interacting with it through a wallet. Throughout the masterclass, concepts are explained step by step so no prior blockchain experience is needed. By the end, you will understand how blockchain works, be able to evaluate blockchain opportunities and have built and deployed your own simple decentralised application.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C544' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1265;

-- C579 Linux Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Linux Masterclass gives you practical, hands-on skills to use and administer Linux, the operating system that powers most servers, cloud platforms, containers and embedded devices. Whether you are an aspiring system administrator, a developer, a DevOps engineer or an IT professional, confidence with the Linux command line is an essential career skill. This masterclass is designed for beginners and IT practitioners who want a structured path from Linux basics to everyday administration and automation.</p><p>You will start with Linux fundamentals, including the file system hierarchy, navigating with the command line, managing files and directories, permissions and ownership, users and groups, package management and process control. Next you will learn Linux shell scripting, writing Bash scripts with variables, conditions, loops and functions to automate repetitive tasks, and scheduling jobs with cron. You will also use powerful text-processing tools such as grep, sed and awk.</p><p>The course continues with Linux networking configuration, covering IP addressing, network interfaces, DNS, SSH remote access, firewalls and troubleshooting connectivity, followed by Linux security, including securing user accounts, SSH hardening, file permissions, firewall rules, system updates and log monitoring. Every topic is hands-on in a real Linux environment with guided labs. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to manage Linux systems confidently, automate tasks with scripts and apply core security practices.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C579' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 916;

-- C590 Copilot Studio and Power Automate
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Copilot Studio and Power Automate shows you how to build your own AI agents and automate business processes using two of Microsoft\'s most powerful low-code tools. Microsoft Copilot Studio lets you create custom AI agents that answer questions from your organisation\'s knowledge and take actions, while Power Automate connects hundreds of apps and services to automate workflows. The course is designed for business users, analysts, IT professionals and process owners who want to deliver AI-powered automation without traditional coding.</p><p>You will start by getting started with Copilot Studio, understanding agents, topics, knowledge sources and generative answers, and creating your first agent grounded in your own documents and websites. Next you will build and publish intelligent agents, designing conversations, adding actions and variables, testing and publishing to channels such as Microsoft Teams and websites. You will then learn workflow automation with Power Automate, building cloud flows with triggers, conditions, approvals and connectors to Outlook, SharePoint, Excel and other services.</p><p>The final topic covers integrating Copilot Studio with Power Automate, so your agents can trigger flows to look up records, create requests, send notifications and update systems on a user\'s behalf. Throughout the course you will also cover governance, security and best practices for responsible AI. Every topic is hands-on with realistic business scenarios. By the end, you will be able to design, build and deploy AI agents and automated workflows that save time and improve service.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C590' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1140;

-- C592 AI Vibe Coding for Computer Vision
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI Vibe Coding for Computer Vision teaches you how to build computer vision applications in Python by directing AI coding assistants such as Cursor, GitHub Copilot and Claude. Computer vision lets software understand images and video, powering applications such as quality inspection, people counting, document scanning, security monitoring and retail analytics. With vibe coding you describe what you want in plain English and guide the AI as it writes the code, so you can build working solutions quickly. The course suits developers, engineers and technical learners.</p><p>You will start by getting set up and covering image processing with AI vibe coding, using OpenCV to load, display, resize, filter and transform images, detect edges and contours, and work with colour spaces and live webcam video. You will learn how to prompt an AI assistant effectively, review the code it produces and fix problems quickly. Next you will move into detection and building vision apps with AI, using pre-trained deep learning models such as YOLO to detect and track objects, recognise faces and read text.</p><p>Throughout the course you will turn these capabilities into small, practical applications, such as an object counter or an automated inspection tool, and learn how to evaluate accuracy and performance. You will also consider privacy and responsible use of camera data. Every activity is hands-on with real images and video. By the end, you will be able to use AI vibe coding to build, test and improve computer vision applications confidently.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C592' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1018;

-- C605 Semiconductor Device and Process Integration Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Semiconductor Device and Process Integration Masterclass gives you an in-depth understanding of semiconductor device physics and how individual fabrication processes are integrated to produce working, reliable devices. As devices continue to shrink and become more complex, engineers need to understand how each process step affects device performance and yield. This masterclass is designed for process, device, integration, yield and equipment engineers, technicians and technical professionals working in or entering the semiconductor industry.</p><p>You will start with the fundamentals of device physics and device fabrication, covering semiconductor materials, energy bands, doping, carriers, p-n junctions and the operation of MOSFETs and other key devices. You will then review the major fabrication steps, including oxidation, lithography, etching, deposition, ion implantation, diffusion, chemical mechanical planarisation and metallisation, and how they combine to build front-end and back-end structures.</p><p>The second topic focuses on process integration issues, examining how process interactions affect threshold voltage, leakage, reliability and yield, and exploring challenges such as short-channel effects, isolation, contact and interconnect resistance, and defect control. You will analyse real integration problems and discuss approaches to solving them. By the end of the masterclass, you will understand the link between device physics and fabrication, and be better able to diagnose integration issues and contribute to improving device performance and yield.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C605' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 878;

-- C628 CompTIA Security+ Exam  Prep
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>CompTIA Security+ Exam Prep prepares you for the CompTIA Security+ certification (exam SY0-701), the globally recognised baseline credential for cyber security professionals. Security+ validates the core skills needed to assess the security posture of an organisation, recommend and implement security solutions, and monitor and secure hybrid environments. The course is designed for IT administrators, network and security professionals, and career switchers who want to start or advance a career in cyber security.</p><p>The course follows the official exam domains. You will start with general security concepts, including security controls, the CIA triad, authentication, cryptography and zero trust. Next you will study threats, vulnerabilities and mitigations, covering threat actors, social engineering, malware, application and network attacks and how to mitigate them. You will then cover security architecture, including secure network design, cloud and hybrid environments, data protection and resilience.</p><p>The course continues with security operations, such as hardening, vulnerability management, monitoring, identity and access management, incident response and digital forensics, and closes with security program management and oversight, covering governance, risk management, third-party risk, compliance and security awareness. Each domain includes practical examples, performance-based question practice and exam strategies. By the end, you will have a strong foundation in cyber security and be well prepared to pass the CompTIA Security+ exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C628' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1329;

-- C688 Generative AI for Design Thinking
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Generative AI for Design Thinking shows you how to combine the human-centred innovation methods of design thinking with the speed and creativity of generative AI to solve business challenges more effectively. Design thinking helps teams deeply understand users and explore better solutions; generative AI can accelerate research synthesis, ideation, prototyping and testing at every stage. The course is designed for managers, product and service designers, innovation teams, marketers and professionals who want to lead more creative, user-focused problem solving.</p><p>You will start with generative AI fundamentals for design thinking, understanding the five stages of empathise, define, ideate, prototype and test, and where AI tools such as ChatGPT, Claude and AI image generators add value. Next you will use AI for user research and opportunity discovery, creating interview guides, synthesising research findings, building personas and journey maps, and framing problem statements and how-might-we questions. You will then apply AI to ideation, prototyping and testing, generating and evaluating ideas and quickly creating mock-ups, storyboards and prototypes.</p><p>The final topic covers implementing and measuring AI-driven design solutions, planning pilots, gathering feedback and defining success measures. Throughout the course you will also discuss bias, ethics and keeping real user insight at the heart of the process. Every topic is hands-on with a team design challenge. By the end, you will be able to use generative AI to run faster, richer design thinking projects that lead to better products, services and experiences.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C688' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1039;

-- C689 Scrum Master and Design Sprint Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Scrum Master and Design Sprint Masterclass equips you with the knowledge and skills to lead agile teams using Scrum and to run focused design sprints that validate ideas quickly. Scrum helps teams deliver value in short, iterative cycles, while a design sprint compresses months of debate into a structured process for understanding a problem, generating solutions, prototyping and testing with real users. The masterclass is designed for aspiring Scrum Masters, project managers, product owners, team leads and innovation practitioners.</p><p>You will start with Scrum foundations, including the Agile Manifesto, agile values and principles, empiricism and the Scrum framework. Next you will explore Scrum roles and accountabilities, understanding the responsibilities of the Scrum Master, Product Owner and Developers and how the Scrum Master serves the team and organisation. You will then cover agile and Scrum meetings, learning how to plan and facilitate sprint planning, daily scrums, sprint reviews and retrospectives effectively.</p><p>The course continues with Scrum and agile project management, including user stories, estimation, velocity and scaling considerations, and Scrum artifacts such as the product backlog, sprint backlog and increment with their commitments. You will also learn how to plan and facilitate a design sprint, from mapping the challenge and sketching solutions to prototyping and user testing. Practical exercises and simulations bring each concept to life. By the end, you will be able to lead Scrum teams and run effective design sprints with confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C689' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 974;

-- C691 Business Transformation with OpenClaw Digital Employees
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Business Transformation with OpenClaw Digital Employees shows you how to build and deploy a digital AI workforce using the OpenClaw agent platform. OpenClaw digital employees are autonomous AI agents that can take on defined roles, use tools, follow skills and work alongside your team to handle tasks such as research, reporting, customer communication and operations support. The course is designed for business leaders, operations managers, IT professionals and transformation teams who want to use AI agents to change how work gets done.</p><p>You will start by setting up the OpenClaw agent platform, installing and configuring it, connecting models, messaging channels and business tools, and creating your first digital employee with a clear role and instructions. Next you will develop OpenClaw agent skills and sub-agents, packaging repeatable work processes into reusable skills, delegating tasks to specialised sub-agents and orchestrating them so a team of digital employees can complete multi-step workflows together.</p><p>The final topic covers optimising and securing the OpenClaw digital workforce, including monitoring agent performance, improving reliability, managing permissions and data access, protecting against prompt injection and keeping humans in control of important decisions. Throughout the course you will apply OpenClaw to realistic business scenarios and identify where digital employees can deliver the greatest value. By the end, you will be able to plan, build, deploy and govern OpenClaw digital employees that drive real business transformation.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C691' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1499;

-- C695 Agentic AI Applications with Codex
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Agentic AI Applications with Codex teaches you how to design, build, test and optimise agentic AI applications using Codex, OpenAI\'s AI coding agent. Codex can plan, write, run and check code inside your project from plain-English instructions, so you can turn application requirements into working software faster while you review and guide the work. The course is designed for developers, technical professionals, data practitioners and product builders who want to create AI-powered applications with an agentic development workflow.</p><p>You will start with agentic AI application planning and development, learning how to brief Codex effectively, plan before editing, set project rules in AGENTS.md and build a working application step by step. Next you will build reusable AI workflows with Codex skills, packaging repeatable tasks so they can be applied consistently across projects. You will then develop retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) and multi-agent applications with Codex, connecting AI models to your own documents and data and orchestrating several agents to complete complex tasks.</p><p>The final topic covers testing, evaluating and optimising agentic AI applications, including writing tests, measuring answer quality against golden questions, improving reliability and performance, and managing permissions and secrets safely. Throughout the course you will practise reviewing agent output critically and keeping humans in control. Every topic is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to use Codex to build, test and refine agentic AI applications that are reliable enough for real use.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C695' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1499;

-- C698 Agile Project Management Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Agile Project Management Masterclass equips you with the fundamentals and practical techniques of agile methods such as Scrum and Kanban so you can deliver projects that adapt to change and deliver value early and often. Agile approaches are now used far beyond software, in marketing, operations, product development and transformation programmes. The masterclass is designed for project managers, team leads, product owners, business analysts and professionals who want to manage projects in a more flexible, collaborative way.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to agile project management, comparing agile and traditional predictive approaches, and exploring the Agile Manifesto, its values and principles, and when agile is the right fit. Next you will cover agile essentials, including Scrum roles, events and artifacts, Kanban boards and flow, user stories, backlogs, prioritisation techniques and estimation methods such as story points and planning poker. You will learn how agile teams plan releases and sprints and how leaders support self-organising teams.</p><p>The final topic focuses on agile project execution and tracking, including running iterations, managing work in progress, tracking progress with burndown and burnup charts and velocity, managing risks and stakeholder expectations, and continuously improving through retrospectives. Practical exercises and simulations let you apply each concept to realistic projects. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to plan, run and track agile projects effectively and help your team deliver better results.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C698' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1017;

-- C711 AB-731 Microsoft Certified AI Transformation Leader
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AB-731 Microsoft Certified AI Transformation Leader prepares business leaders and decision-makers for the Microsoft AB-731 certification, which validates the ability to recognise AI opportunities, plan adoption and drive organisational transformation with Microsoft AI solutions. The focus is on strategy, value and change rather than coding, making it ideal for executives, managers, transformation leads, business consultants and IT decision-makers who guide AI investments and initiatives.</p><p>The course follows the official exam domains. You will start by identifying the business value of generative AI solutions, understanding how generative AI and agents work, their capabilities and limitations, and how to evaluate use cases, return on investment and risk. Next you will identify the benefits, capabilities and opportunities of Microsoft AI solutions, including Microsoft 365 Copilot, Copilot Chat, Copilot Studio agents and Azure AI Foundry, and how they fit different business needs.</p><p>The final domain covers identifying an implementation and adoption strategy, including responsible AI principles, governance, data security and privacy, change management, skills development and measuring adoption and value. Each domain combines explanation, business scenarios and exam-style practice questions. By the end, you will be able to lead AI transformation conversations with confidence, build a practical roadmap for adopting Microsoft AI in your organisation and be well prepared to pass the AB-731 exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C711' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1012;

-- C716 Semiconductor Process Fundamentals Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Semiconductor Process Fundamentals Masterclass gives you comprehensive knowledge of the CMOS process modules and process flow used in modern semiconductor manufacturing. Understanding how each module works and how modules are integrated is essential for engineers and technicians who need to control processes, solve problems and improve yield. This masterclass is designed for process, equipment, yield and integration engineers, technicians and technical professionals who are new to or growing in the semiconductor industry.</p><p>You will start with CMOS process modules and the process flow, covering wafer preparation, oxidation, photolithography, etching, thin film deposition, ion implantation, diffusion and annealing, chemical mechanical planarisation and metallisation. You will learn the purpose of each module, the key equipment and process parameters, and how they come together in a typical CMOS flow from isolation and well formation to gate, source and drain and interconnects.</p><p>The second topic focuses on CMOS process integration and performance, examining how process variation and interactions between modules affect transistor characteristics, reliability and yield, and how metrology, inspection and statistical process control are used to keep processes in control. You will work through practical examples of common process issues and their root causes. By the end of the masterclass, you will understand the CMOS manufacturing flow and be better equipped to support process control and yield improvement.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C716' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 870;

-- C718 CompTIA Certified SecurityX Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>CompTIA Certified SecurityX Training prepares experienced security professionals for CompTIA SecurityX (exam CAS-005), the expert-level certification formerly known as CASP+. SecurityX validates the advanced skills needed to architect, engineer and integrate secure solutions across complex enterprise environments, and to lead governance, risk and compliance efforts. The course is designed for senior security engineers, security architects, technical leads and cyber security practitioners with several years of hands-on experience.</p><p>The course follows the official exam domains. You will start with governance, risk and compliance, covering security programme governance, risk management frameworks, legal and regulatory requirements, and AI-related security considerations. Next you will study security architecture, including resilient and secure enterprise designs, zero trust, cloud and hybrid architectures and data security. You will then cover security engineering, such as identity and access management, endpoint and server hardening, cryptography, PKI and securing specialised and legacy systems.</p><p>The final domain covers security operations, including threat hunting, monitoring and response, vulnerability management, incident handling and digital forensics. Throughout the course you will work through complex scenarios and performance-based question practice that reflect the advanced nature of the exam. By the end, you will be able to design and integrate enterprise-grade security solutions with confidence and be well prepared to pass the CompTIA SecurityX certification exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C718' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1005;

-- C728 AI Vibe Coding for Algorithmic Trading
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI Vibe Coding for Algorithmic Trading teaches you how to build, test and run algorithmic trading strategies in Python by directing AI coding assistants such as Cursor, GitHub Copilot and Claude. You describe the strategy you want in plain English, review the code the AI writes and refine it until it does exactly what you intend. The course is designed for traders, investors, finance professionals and technical learners who want to automate trading ideas without needing to be expert programmers.</p><p>You will start by getting started with AI vibe coding for trading, setting up your tools, connecting to market data sources and learning how to prompt an AI assistant to write and explain Python code. Next you will analyse markets with AI, working with price and volume data, calculating returns and technical indicators such as moving averages, RSI and MACD, and visualising trends. You will then build and backtest strategies with AI, turning trading rules into code, measuring performance, drawdown and risk, and avoiding pitfalls such as overfitting and look-ahead bias.</p><p>The final topic covers automating and running trading with AI, including paper trading, connecting to a broker API, scheduling strategies and adding risk controls and logging. Throughout the course you will learn to verify AI-generated code carefully and keep human control over capital. The course is educational and does not provide financial advice. Every topic is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to develop and test algorithmic trading strategies efficiently with AI vibe coding.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C728' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1052;

-- C731 Budgeting for SMEs
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Budgeting for SMEs equips business owners, managers and finance staff with the practical skills to plan, prepare, control and review budgets that keep a small or medium-sized enterprise financially healthy. A well-built budget turns business goals into numbers, highlights cash pressures before they become a crisis and gives managers a clear benchmark for decisions. The course is tailored to the realities SMEs face, such as limited resources, seasonal cash flow and fast-changing conditions, and requires no advanced finance background.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to financial budgeting, exploring the purpose of budgets, the main budget types and how budgeting links to strategy. Next you will learn financial forecasting, using historical data, trends and assumptions to project sales, costs and cash flow. You will then work through budget preparation, building sales, operating, capital and cash budgets step by step in a spreadsheet, followed by developing a budget control plan that assigns responsibility and sets review points.</p><p>The later topics cover budget analysis, including variance analysis and identifying the causes of over- and under-spending, budget approval, presenting and justifying budgets to owners, boards and lenders, and financial compliance, ensuring budgets and spending align with internal controls and regulatory requirements. Practical exercises use realistic SME scenarios throughout. By the end, you will be able to prepare a sound budget, monitor performance against it and use budget insights to make better financial decisions for your business.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C731' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1022;

-- C734 Microsoft Copilot for Power BI
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Microsoft Copilot for Power BI shows you how to bring AI into your business intelligence workflow using Copilot, Microsoft\'s AI assistant built into Power BI and Microsoft Fabric. Copilot can create report pages from a simple prompt, suggest visuals, summarise insights in plain language, help write DAX measures and answer questions about your data, making analysis faster and more accessible. The course is designed for analysts, report developers, managers and business users who build or consume Power BI reports.</p><p>You will start by getting started with Copilot in Power BI, understanding the requirements, where Copilot appears in Power BI Desktop and the Power BI service, and how to write prompts that produce accurate, useful results. You will learn how to prepare your semantic model with clear names, descriptions and relationships so Copilot understands your data. Next you will create reports and visuals with Copilot, generating report pages, refining charts and layouts, and adding narrative summaries that explain key trends to your audience.</p><p>The final topic covers AI-assisted data modelling and analysis, using Copilot to suggest and explain DAX measures, explore the data with natural-language questions, identify outliers and drivers, and validate results. Throughout the course you will learn the limits of Copilot, how to check its output and how to apply data security and governance. Every exercise is hands-on with realistic business datasets. By the end, you will be able to use Microsoft Copilot in Power BI to build insightful reports faster and with confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C734' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1080;

-- C735 Agentic AI with n8n
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Agentic AI with n8n teaches you how to combine n8n\'s low-code workflow orchestration with autonomous AI agents to design, build and deploy intelligent automations. n8n connects hundreds of apps and services, and its AI agent capabilities let workflows reason, make decisions, call tools and retrieve knowledge, so you can automate processes that once needed a person at every step. The course is designed for operations and IT professionals, business analysts, developers and automation enthusiasts.</p><p>You will start with workflow automation in n8n, learning triggers, nodes, credentials, data mapping and error handling by building practical automations across email, spreadsheets, CRMs and chat. Next you will move into agentic process automation with AI agents, giving agents instructions, memory and tools so they can classify requests, extract information and take the right action. You will then build agentic automations with webhooks and HTTP requests, integrating external systems and APIs to make your agents part of real business processes.</p><p>The course continues with enhancing workflow automation with agentic RAG, connecting agents to your documents through vector stores so they can answer accurately from company knowledge, and closes with human-in-the-loop controls, monitoring and deployment, adding approval steps, logging, testing and secure hosting. Every topic is hands-on with realistic scenarios. By the end, you will be able to design and run reliable agentic AI workflows in n8n that save time and scale your operations.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C735' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 985;

-- C740 Google Professional Machine Learning Engineer Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Google Professional Machine Learning Engineer Training prepares you for the Google Cloud Professional Machine Learning Engineer certification, which validates your ability to design, build, deploy and operate machine learning solutions on Google Cloud. Certified ML engineers bring models from experimentation into reliable production systems, using Vertex AI and Google Cloud\'s data and AI services. The course is designed for data scientists, ML engineers, data engineers and developers with some machine learning and Python experience.</p><p>You will start with Google Cloud big data and machine learning fundamentals, exploring BigQuery, Dataflow, Vertex AI and the ML lifecycle on Google Cloud. Next you will learn how Google approaches machine learning, from framing business problems as ML problems to managing ML projects and responsible AI. You will then launch into machine learning, covering data exploration, model types, training, evaluation and generalisation, followed by TensorFlow on Google Cloud, building and training models with TensorFlow and Keras.</p><p>The course continues with feature engineering, including feature selection, transformation and Vertex AI Feature Store, and machine learning in the enterprise, covering MLOps, pipelines, model deployment, monitoring and retraining at scale, as well as generative AI capabilities in Vertex AI. Each topic is mapped to the exam guide and reinforced with practice questions and scenarios. By the end, you will be able to architect production ML solutions on Google Cloud and be well prepared for the certification exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C740' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1326;

-- C744 Claude Design for UX/UI
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Claude Design for UX/UI shows you how to combine your design skills with Claude, Anthropic\'s AI assistant, to plan, create and evaluate user interfaces faster. Claude can turn requirements into wireframes and interactive prototypes, generate component variations, write UX copy, review designs against usability principles and produce clear documentation for developers. The course is designed for UX and UI designers, product managers, front-end developers and anyone who designs digital products and wants to speed up the design process with AI.</p><p>You will start with requirements for AI-enhanced UI design, using Claude to analyse user needs, create personas and user flows, and turn requirements into a clear design brief. Next you will work with components and states, generating buttons, forms, navigation, cards and other UI components, and defining their states, variants and responsive behaviour for a consistent design system. You will then design and evaluate AI-driven graphical user interfaces, building interactive prototypes with Claude and refining layout, hierarchy, colour and typography.</p><p>The course also covers evaluating your designs for usability and accessibility, including contrast, readability and keyboard navigation, using Claude as a critical reviewer. The final topic focuses on documentation and collaboration, producing design specifications, component guidelines and handoff notes for developers and stakeholders. Every topic is hands-on with a realistic product brief. By the end, you will be able to use Claude confidently to design, test and document high-quality UX/UI work in a fraction of the usual time.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C744' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 922;

-- C748 ISO 9001:2015 Quality Management System Internal Auditor Course
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>ISO 9001:2015 Quality Management System Internal Auditor Course equips you with the knowledge and skills to plan, conduct, report and follow up internal audits of a quality management system against the ISO 9001:2015 standard. Internal audits are a requirement of ISO 9001 and one of the most effective tools for verifying that processes work as intended and for driving improvement. The course is designed for quality professionals, managers, supervisors and staff who are, or will be, members of an internal audit team.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to audit activities and compliance, reviewing the structure and key requirements of ISO 9001:2015, audit principles from ISO 19011, types of audit and the roles and responsibilities of internal auditors. You will learn how to plan an audit programme, prepare audit checklists and conduct opening meetings. Next you will cover the analysis and interpretation of audit results, gathering objective evidence through interviews, observation and records, and classifying findings as conformities, nonconformities or opportunities for improvement.</p><p>The course then covers risk mitigation and improvement measures, writing clear nonconformity reports, agreeing corrective actions and verifying their effectiveness, followed by adherence to compliance standards, including reporting to management and supporting certification audits. Role plays and audit case studies give you practical experience throughout. By the end, you will be able to plan and conduct effective ISO 9001:2015 internal audits and contribute to the continual improvement of your quality management system.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C748' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 875;

-- C752 Sustainability Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Sustainability Masterclass equips professionals and organisations with practical skills to measure, analyse and reduce their carbon footprint and drive meaningful environmental sustainability. With growing expectations from customers, investors and regulators, organisations need credible plans to cut emissions and report progress. The masterclass is designed for sustainability and ESG officers, operations and facilities managers, business owners and professionals who are responsible for, or want to contribute to, their organisation\'s sustainability goals.</p><p>You will start by identifying and analysing carbon footprint hotspots, learning the basics of greenhouse gas accounting, Scope 1, 2 and 3 emissions and how to collect activity data and apply emission factors to calculate an organisation\'s footprint. You will identify the processes, assets and supply chain activities that contribute most to emissions. Next you will prioritise carbon footprint reduction initiatives, evaluating options such as energy efficiency, renewable energy, sustainable procurement, waste reduction and transport changes by cost, impact and feasibility.</p><p>The final topic covers implementing a carbon footprint reduction plan, setting targets, assigning responsibilities, engaging stakeholders, tracking progress with key indicators and communicating results transparently. Throughout the masterclass you will work on practical exercises and case studies drawn from real organisations. By the end, you will be able to measure your organisation\'s carbon footprint, identify the most effective reduction opportunities and lead a practical plan that moves your organisation towards its sustainability targets.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C752' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1073;

-- C756 AZ-104 Azure Administrator Associate Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AZ-104 Azure Administrator Associate Training prepares you for the Microsoft Certified: Azure Administrator Associate certification by building the skills to implement, manage and monitor an organisation\'s Microsoft Azure environment. Azure administrators manage identities, governance, storage, compute and networking, and keep cloud resources secure, available and cost-effective. The course is designed for IT administrators, system and network engineers, and cloud professionals with some Azure experience who want to advance their cloud career.</p><p>The course follows the official exam domains. You will start with managing Azure identities and governance, including Microsoft Entra ID users and groups, role-based access control, Azure Policy, resource locks, tags, subscriptions and cost management. Next you will implement and manage storage, configuring storage accounts, blob and file storage, access keys and shared access signatures, replication and data protection. You will then deploy and manage Azure compute resources, such as virtual machines, availability sets and scale sets, ARM and Bicep templates, containers and App Service.</p><p>The course continues with implementing and managing virtual networking, covering virtual networks, subnets, peering, network security groups, DNS, load balancing and connectivity, and closes with monitoring and maintaining Azure resources using Azure Monitor, alerts, Log Analytics, backup and site recovery. Hands-on labs and exam-style practice questions reinforce each domain. By the end, you will be able to administer Azure environments confidently and be well prepared to pass the AZ-104 exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C756' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1172;

-- C765 Develop Multi-Agent Systems with OpenAI Agent SDK
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Develop Multi-Agent Systems with OpenAI Agent SDK teaches you how to design, build and deploy multi-agent AI systems using OpenAI\'s Agents SDK. Multi-agent systems split complex work across specialised agents that use tools, retrieve knowledge, hand off tasks to one another and work under guardrails, enabling applications that are more capable and reliable than a single chatbot. The course is designed for developers, AI engineers, data scientists and technical professionals with Python experience who want to build production-ready agentic applications.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to the OpenAI Agents SDK, covering agents, instructions, tools, handoffs, guardrails, sessions and tracing, and building your first agents in Python. Next you will build a retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) agent that answers questions accurately from your own documents using file search and vector stores. You will then orchestrate multiple agents, designing triage and specialist agents, managing handoffs and parallel work, and tracing runs to debug and improve agent behaviour.</p><p>The course continues with the Model Context Protocol (MCP), connecting your agents to external tools and data sources through MCP servers, and closes with fine-tuning LLM models, learning when and how to customise a model for your domain and evaluate the results. Throughout the course you will also cover safety, guardrails, cost control and deployment practices. Every topic is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to develop, evaluate and deploy multi-agent systems with the OpenAI Agents SDK confidently.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C765' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1162;

-- C769 Statistical Process Control (SPC) Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Statistical Process Control (SPC) Training equips you with the knowledge and tools to monitor, control and improve processes using statistics. SPC helps organisations detect problems early, distinguish normal variation from real issues and make data-driven decisions that reduce scrap, rework and customer complaints. The course is designed for quality, production and process engineers, supervisors, technicians and operators in manufacturing and service environments who are responsible for process performance.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to statistical process control, covering the principles of variation, common and special causes, basic statistics and how SPC supports continuous improvement. Next you will learn about control charts, including how to construct and interpret X-bar and R, X-bar and S, individuals and moving range charts for variable data, and p, np, c and u charts for attribute data. You will then set up SPC in practice, selecting critical characteristics, planning sampling, collecting data and calculating control limits.</p><p>The course continues with process control capabilities, including process capability indices such as Cp, Cpk, Pp and Ppk and how to interpret them against specifications, and closes with out-of-control conditions and follow-up actions, recognising out-of-control patterns, investigating root causes and implementing corrective actions and reaction plans. Practical exercises use real process data. By the end, you will be able to implement SPC, interpret control charts and capability studies, and take the right actions to keep processes stable and capable.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C769' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 988;

-- C776 AI Transformation with Microsoft Copilot
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI Transformation with Microsoft Copilot is a practical course for executives, senior managers and business leaders who want to lead AI adoption in their organisation using Microsoft Copilot. Rather than treating AI as a technology project, the course shows how to use Copilot in everyday leadership work, redesign workflows safely, build simple agents and drive measurable business value. No technical background or coding is required, making it ideal for leaders who need to make informed decisions about AI.</p><p>You will start by using Microsoft 365 Copilot for everyday business work, experiencing first-hand how it drafts documents, summarises email and meetings, analyses data and prepares presentations, and learning prompting techniques that produce reliable results. Next you will design safe Copilot workflows with human control, mapping a business process, identifying where AI adds value and building a no-code Copilot workflow with clear checkpoints. You will then create and test bounded Copilot agents that work within defined knowledge, scope and permissions.</p><p>The final topic focuses on leading adoption, measuring value and scaling outcomes, including building a business case, managing change and skills, setting governance and responsible AI guardrails, and tracking productivity and quality gains. Throughout the course you will work on scenarios from your own organisation. By the end, you will be able to lead an AI transformation with Microsoft Copilot confidently, balancing opportunity with risk and turning AI pilots into lasting business results.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C776' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1268;

-- C781 Power BI Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Power BI Masterclass teaches you how to turn complex data into compelling, interactive reports and dashboards with Microsoft Power BI, one of the world\'s most popular business intelligence tools. Power BI connects to a wide range of data sources and lets you clean, model, analyse and share data insights across your organisation. The masterclass is designed for analysts, managers, finance and operations staff, and business users who want to make better data-driven decisions.</p><p>You will start by getting started with Power BI, installing Power BI Desktop, connecting to Excel, CSV and database sources, and using Power Query to clean and transform data. Next you will create data visualisations, building bar, line, pie, map, table and matrix visuals and applying formatting and best practices for clear communication. You will then create dashboards and scorecards, combining visuals into interactive report pages and publishing them to the Power BI service for sharing and collaboration.</p><p>The course continues with dynamic visualisation, using slicers, filters, drill-down, bookmarks and tooltips to make reports interactive, and data modelling, designing relationships and star schemas that keep reports fast and accurate. The final topic covers data analytics with DAX, writing calculated columns and measures, time intelligence and key performance indicators. Every topic is hands-on with realistic datasets. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to build professional, insightful Power BI reports and dashboards with confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C781' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 834;

-- C790 CompTIA Project+ Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>CompTIA Project+ Training prepares you for the CompTIA Project+ certification (exam PK0-005), a vendor-neutral credential that validates the skills to manage small to medium-sized projects, with a focus on IT and technology environments. Project+ covers both traditional and agile approaches and is ideal for project coordinators, team leaders, IT professionals and business staff who manage projects as part of their role and want a recognised qualification without the experience requirements of more advanced certifications.</p><p>The course follows the official exam domains. You will start with project management concepts, including project roles and responsibilities, methodologies such as waterfall and agile, scope, schedule, cost, risk, quality and communication management, and change control. Next you will study the project life cycle phases, from discovery and initiation through planning, execution, monitoring and controlling, to closure, and the key activities and outputs of each phase.</p><p>The course continues with tools and documentation, covering project charters, work breakdown structures, Gantt charts, RACI matrices, risk registers, status reports and project management software, and closes with the basics of IT and governance, including IT infrastructure concepts, data privacy, security and compliance considerations for technology projects. Each domain is reinforced with real-world scenarios and exam-style practice questions. By the end, you will be able to manage projects more effectively and be well prepared to pass the CompTIA Project+ exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C790' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1766;

-- C797 Sustainability Reporting Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Sustainability Reporting Masterclass equips senior leaders and professionals with the knowledge and practical strategies to develop credible sustainability and ESG reports that meet stakeholder and regulatory expectations. Sustainability reporting is fast becoming mandatory for listed companies and expected across supply chains, and investors, customers and employees increasingly judge organisations on their environmental, social and governance performance. The masterclass is designed for leaders, sustainability and ESG managers, finance and compliance professionals and business owners.</p><p>You will start with the foundations of sustainability and ESG, understanding the key concepts, global trends and why sustainability matters to business value and risk. Next you will explore ESG strategy, stakeholder engagement and materiality, identifying the issues that matter most to your organisation and its stakeholders and setting goals and targets. You will then cover sustainability reporting and ESG disclosure, working with frameworks and standards such as GRI, ISSB (IFRS S1 and S2) and TCFD, and learning how to collect data, measure performance and write clear, balanced disclosures.</p><p>The final topic covers the circular economy, sustainable supply chains and continuous improvement, including how to extend sustainability beyond your own operations and strengthen your reporting year on year. Case studies and practical exercises help you apply each topic to your own organisation. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to plan and lead a sustainability reporting process that is credible, compliant and supports long-term business strategy.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C797' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1028;

-- C803 Microsoft Copilot for Power Apps
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Microsoft Copilot for Power Apps shows you how to build business applications faster with AI using Copilot, Microsoft\'s AI assistant built into the Power Platform. With Copilot, you can describe the app you need in plain English and have it create a working canvas app with tables, screens and controls, then refine it through conversation. The course is designed for business users, analysts, citizen developers and IT professionals who want to digitise processes and build useful apps without traditional coding.</p><p>You will start by getting started with Copilot in Power Apps, understanding the Power Platform, environments and Dataverse, and creating an app from a natural-language description. You will learn how to write prompts that produce the right data structure and screens. Next you will build canvas apps with Copilot, adding and editing tables, designing screens and forms, generating Power Fx formulas with Copilot\'s help, and improving layout, navigation and usability.</p><p>The final topic covers automating and extending your apps with Copilot, connecting to data sources such as SharePoint and Excel, building Power Automate flows for approvals and notifications, and adding a Copilot control so users can ask questions about the app\'s data. Throughout the course you will also cover sharing, security and governance considerations. Every exercise is hands-on with realistic business scenarios. By the end, you will be able to build, extend and share practical business apps with Microsoft Copilot for Power Apps.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C803' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1007;

-- C810 Certified Kubernetes Application Developer (CKAD) Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Certified Kubernetes Application Developer (CKAD) Training prepares you for the CKAD certification from the Cloud Native Computing Foundation and The Linux Foundation, a performance-based exam that tests your ability to design, build, configure and expose cloud-native applications on Kubernetes. Because the exam is completed entirely at the command line, the course is highly practical and hands-on. It is designed for software developers, DevOps engineers and platform engineers who build and deploy containerised applications.</p><p>The course follows the official CKAD domains. You will start with application design and build, covering container images, multi-container pod patterns, Jobs and CronJobs, and persistent and ephemeral volumes. Next you will learn application deployment, including Deployments, rolling updates and rollbacks, blue-green and canary strategies, and using Helm and Kustomize. You will then cover application observability and maintenance, such as liveness, readiness and startup probes, logging, monitoring, debugging and handling API deprecations.</p><p>The course continues with application environment, configuration and security, including ConfigMaps, Secrets, resource requests and limits, ServiceAccounts, SecurityContexts and custom resources, and closes with services and networking, covering Services, Ingress and NetworkPolicies. Throughout the course you will practise with timed exercises and exam-style tasks to build speed and accuracy with kubectl. By the end, you will be able to develop and run applications on Kubernetes confidently and be well prepared to pass the CKAD exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C810' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 996;

-- C811 Job Assessment and Redesign for AI Adoption
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Job Assessment and Redesign for AI Adoption shows leaders, HR professionals and managers how to get real value from artificial intelligence by redesigning work rather than simply adding tools to existing jobs. Real gains come from assessing work at the task level and deciding deliberately which tasks AI should automate, which it should augment and which must stay with people. The course is designed for HR and organisation development professionals, department heads, transformation leads and managers responsible for workforce planning.</p><p>You will start by assessing jobs for AI adoption, breaking roles down into tasks, evaluating each task for AI suitability based on its nature, risk and value, and identifying where generative AI and AI agents can save time or improve quality. You will use practical frameworks and templates to map current work, skills and pain points, and to estimate the potential impact of AI on each role. You will also consider the data, tools and controls needed for safe adoption.</p><p>The second topic covers redesigning work and allocating gains, creating new task allocations and job designs, defining new skills and training needs, and deciding how freed capacity will be reinvested in higher-value work, service improvement or growth. You will also address change management, employee engagement, fairness and communication so people embrace rather than fear the change. Hands-on exercises use roles from your own organisation. By the end, you will be able to lead a structured job assessment and redesign that turns AI adoption into measurable results.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C811' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1039;

-- C814 Creating  AI Agents and Chatbots with Microsoft Copilot Studio
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Creating AI Agents and Chatbots with Microsoft Copilot Studio teaches you how to design, build, publish and improve intelligent AI agents and chatbots using Microsoft Copilot Studio, Microsoft\'s low-code platform for conversational AI. Copilot Studio lets you create agents that answer questions from your own knowledge sources, guide users through tasks and take actions in business systems, without needing to be a developer. The course is designed for business users, customer service and HR teams, IT professionals and digital transformation staff.</p><p>You will start with content strategy for chatbots, defining the purpose, audience and scope of your agent, identifying common questions and tasks, and planning the knowledge sources and conversation flows it will need. Next you will create chatbot content with Microsoft Copilot Studio, building an agent grounded in your websites and documents, using generative answers, designing topics with questions, conditions and variables, and adding actions and Power Automate flows to complete tasks for users.</p><p>The final topic covers publishing and evaluating your chatbot, testing conversations, deploying the agent to channels such as Microsoft Teams and your website, and using analytics to track usage, resolution rates and user satisfaction so you can improve it over time. Throughout the course you will also cover security, authentication and responsible AI considerations. Every topic is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to create, publish and continuously improve AI agents and chatbots with Microsoft Copilot Studio.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C814' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1055;

-- C817 Gemini for Google Sheet
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Gemini for Google Sheet shows you how to use Gemini, Google\'s AI assistant, inside Google Sheets to build formulas, clean and organise data, analyse trends and create reports in a fraction of the usual time. Instead of searching for the right function or manually reworking data, you can describe what you need in plain English and let Gemini do the heavy lifting while you check and refine the results. The course is designed for professionals, administrators, analysts, teachers and anyone who works with spreadsheets in Google Workspace.</p><p>You will start by getting started with AI in Google Sheets, learning how to access Gemini in the side panel, write effective prompts and use AI to create tables, generate formulas and explain how existing formulas work. You will practise cleaning and organising data, such as removing duplicates, splitting and combining columns, standardising formats and categorising entries. Next you will analyse and automate data with AI in Sheets, asking Gemini to summarise data, highlight trends and outliers, build pivot tables and charts and suggest insights.</p><p>Throughout the course you will also learn how to use AI functions to process text and data at scale, connect Sheets with other Google Workspace apps and automate repetitive steps. You will cover how to verify AI results and protect sensitive information. Every exercise is hands-on with realistic business datasets. By the end, you will be able to use Gemini in Google Sheets confidently to work faster, reduce errors and turn your spreadsheet data into clear, useful insights.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C817' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 784;

-- C818 ChatGPT WORK for Digital Marketing
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>ChatGPT WORK for Digital Marketing shows marketers how to use ChatGPT Work, the agentic work mode in the ChatGPT desktop app, to plan, produce and analyse marketing activity far faster than prompting a chatbot one message at a time. ChatGPT Work can take a marketing brief, work through it step by step with your files, data and connected apps, and return finished deliverables such as campaign plans, content drafts and performance summaries for you to review. The course is designed for digital marketers, content and social media teams, marketing managers and business owners.</p><p>You will start by getting started with ChatGPT Work for marketing, setting it up, understanding how it differs from regular ChatGPT chat, and writing clear task briefs with goals, audience, brand voice and expected outputs. Next you will create campaign assets, using ChatGPT Work to research audiences and competitors, build campaign plans and content calendars, and produce blog posts, social media posts, email sequences, ad copy and landing page drafts in a consistent brand voice.</p><p>The course then covers data and analytics, using ChatGPT Work to clean and analyse campaign data, summarise performance, compare channels and recommend improvements, followed by integrating your marketing stack, connecting the tools and files your team already uses so routine marketing work can be handled end to end. Throughout the course you will keep human review over brand and accuracy, and protect customer data. By the end, you will be able to use ChatGPT Work as a reliable AI teammate that speeds up your digital marketing.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C818' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 287;

-- C820 Microsoft Copilot for HR
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Microsoft Copilot for HR equips HR professionals with practical skills to use Microsoft 365 Copilot, SharePoint, AI agents and Microsoft Copilot Studio to enhance and automate HR processes across the employee lifecycle. Copilot can draft job descriptions and policies, summarise candidate information, prepare onboarding materials, answer employee questions and analyse HR data, freeing HR teams to focus on people and strategy. The course is designed for HR practitioners, HR business partners, talent acquisition and learning and development professionals, and HR managers.</p><p>You will start with Microsoft Copilot and AI agents for recruitment, using Copilot to write job descriptions and advertisements, screen and summarise applications, prepare interview questions and draft candidate communications. Next you will use Microsoft Copilot for employee onboarding and engagement, creating onboarding plans, welcome packs and FAQs, and building a SharePoint knowledge base that an AI agent can draw on to answer employee questions. You will then apply Copilot to talent development, leave and HR administration, including training plans, performance review support and policy queries.</p><p>The final topic covers Microsoft Copilot Studio for HR workflow automation, building HR agents and connecting them to Power Automate flows for requests, approvals and notifications. Throughout the course you will address data privacy, fairness, bias and governance when using AI with employee information. Every exercise is hands-on with realistic HR scenarios. By the end, you will be able to use Microsoft Copilot confidently to streamline HR processes and deliver a better employee experience.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C820' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1533;

-- C829 Building Multi Agent Aplications with Gemini ADK
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Building Multi Agent Aplications with Gemini ADK teaches you how to design, build and deploy multi-agent AI applications using Google\'s Agent Development Kit (ADK) and Gemini models. ADK is an open-source framework for creating agents that reason, use tools, retrieve knowledge and collaborate with other agents, so you can build applications that tackle complex tasks more reliably than a single chatbot. The course is designed for developers, AI engineers, data scientists and technical professionals with Python experience.</p><p>You will start with an overview of agentic AI in Gemini ADK, understanding large language models, agents, tools, sessions, state and memory, and building your first agent with Gemini. Next you will build a multi-agent app with Gemini ADK, designing a coordinator agent and specialist sub-agents, using sequential, parallel and loop workflow agents, and managing how agents share context and hand off work. You will then build agentic AI retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) in Gemini ADK, connecting agents to your own documents and data so they answer accurately.</p><p>The final topic covers building an agentic AI application with the Gemini Agent ADK and deploying it, adding tools and external APIs, evaluating agent behaviour, and deploying to Google Cloud with options such as Cloud Run and Vertex AI Agent Engine. Throughout the course you will also cover safety, guardrails and cost considerations. Every topic is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to develop, test and deploy multi-agent applications with Gemini ADK confidently.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C829' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 844;

-- C831 AI for Early Childhood
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI for Early Childhood shows preschool teachers, early childhood educators and centre leaders how to bring generative AI tools such as ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and AI image generators into their work in safe, practical and developmentally appropriate ways. AI can help educators plan lessons, create engaging learning materials, prepare documentation and communicate with parents more efficiently, giving them more time to focus on the children. No technical background is required.</p><p>You will start by getting started with AI for early childhood, understanding what generative AI can and cannot do, how to write effective prompts and how to use AI responsibly with young children\'s information. Next you will use AI for lesson planning and learning materials, creating themed lesson plans, activity ideas, songs, rhymes, stories and worksheets aligned to early learning frameworks and children\'s interests. You will then use AI for creative classroom content, generating illustrations, flashcards, posters, simple storybooks and play-based activities.</p><p>The final topic covers AI for documentation and parent communication, using AI to help write observations and learning stories, summarise children\'s progress, draft newsletters and prepare clear, warm messages to parents. Throughout the course you will discuss child safety, privacy, consent and the importance of keeping educators\' professional judgement at the centre. Every activity is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to use AI confidently to save time and enrich teaching and learning in your early childhood setting.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C831' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1125;

-- C841 AI Vibe Coding for Web Design
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI Vibe Coding for Web Design teaches you how to create effective, user-friendly and business-focused websites by directing AI coding assistants with plain-English instructions. With vibe coding you describe the page or feature you want, review the HTML, CSS and JavaScript the AI produces and refine it until it looks and works exactly as intended, so you can build professional sites without hand-coding every line. The course is designed for business owners, marketers, designers and aspiring web developers.</p><p>You will start with AI vibe coding for web content, planning a site structure, generating pages and sections, and writing clear, persuasive copy that speaks to your target audience. Next you will apply AI vibe coding for web usability, making sites responsive on mobile, improving navigation, layout, readability and page speed, and checking accessibility so everyone can use your site. You will then use AI vibe coding for lead generation and online visibility, adding forms, calls to action, landing pages and basic SEO so your site attracts and converts visitors.</p><p>The final topic covers AI vibe coding for user experience, refining visual design, interactions and consistency, gathering feedback and making improvements. Throughout the course you will learn to review AI-generated code, fix problems and publish your site online. Every topic is hands-on, so you finish with a working website you have built yourself. By the end, you will be able to use AI vibe coding to design and launch attractive, effective websites quickly and confidently.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C841' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1109;

-- C852 Internet of Things (IoT) Fundamentals for Beginners
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Internet of Things (IoT) Fundamentals for Beginners gives you a solid, hands-on foundation in IoT, the technology that connects everyday devices and sensors to the internet so they can collect data and be controlled remotely. IoT is transforming smart homes, buildings, cities, healthcare, agriculture and manufacturing. This course is designed for beginners, students, educators, IT and engineering professionals, and anyone curious about how connected devices work, with no prior electronics experience required.</p><p>You will start with an overview of the Internet of Things, exploring IoT architecture, devices, sensors and actuators, connectivity options such as Wi-Fi and Bluetooth, protocols such as MQTT and HTTP, and real-world applications. Next you will collect and post data to the cloud, connecting sensors to a microcontroller or single-board computer, writing simple code to read measurements such as temperature and humidity, and sending them to a cloud IoT platform.</p><p>The course then covers reading data and remotely controlling devices from the cloud, so you can switch lights, motors and relays from a dashboard or phone, and IoT data analytics and visualisation, building dashboards and charts that turn sensor data into insights and alerts. You will also learn basic IoT security practices, such as protecting device credentials and keeping firmware up to date. Every topic is hands-on with real hardware. By the end, you will understand how IoT systems work and be able to build a simple end-to-end IoT project with confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C852' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 959;

-- C855 CompTIA Cloud+ Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>CompTIA Cloud+ Training prepares you for the CompTIA Cloud+ certification (exam CV0-004), a vendor-neutral credential that validates the skills to deploy, secure, operate and troubleshoot cloud infrastructure across public, private and hybrid environments. Cloud+ is ideal for systems administrators, cloud engineers, network and IT professionals who manage cloud resources and want a certification that is not tied to a single provider.</p><p>The course follows the official exam domains. You will start with cloud architecture, covering cloud service and deployment models, compute, storage and network design, high availability, disaster recovery and cost considerations. Next you will study deployment, including migrating workloads, provisioning resources, infrastructure as code and containers. You will then cover operations, such as monitoring, logging, scaling, backup and lifecycle management, followed by security, including identity and access management, encryption, compliance, vulnerability management and securing cloud networks.</p><p>The course continues with DevOps fundamentals, including CI/CD pipelines, version control, automation and orchestration, and closes with troubleshooting, applying a structured methodology to resolve deployment, connectivity, performance and security issues in the cloud. Each domain combines explanation, real-world scenarios and exam-style practice questions, including performance-based items. By the end, you will be able to manage cloud environments confidently across providers and be well prepared to pass the CompTIA Cloud+ exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C855' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1123;

-- C859 Power App Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Power App Masterclass teaches you how to build custom business applications and automate workflows with Microsoft Power Apps and Power Automate, without traditional coding. The Power Platform lets organisations digitise paper forms, spreadsheets and manual processes quickly, connecting to data in SharePoint, Excel, Dataverse and hundreds of other services. The masterclass is designed for business users, analysts, citizen developers and IT professionals who want to improve how their teams work.</p><p>You will start by exploring opportunities for using Power Platform apps, identifying processes in your organisation that are good candidates for apps and automation, and understanding the components of the Power Platform. Next you will learn Power Automate, building cloud flows with triggers, actions, conditions and approvals to automate notifications, data updates and document workflows. You will then move into Power Apps, designing canvas apps with screens, forms, galleries and controls, connecting to data and writing Power Fx formulas.</p><p>The final topic covers integrating Power Apps and Power Automate, so your apps can trigger flows to submit requests, route approvals, send emails and update records automatically. You will also learn how to test, share and manage apps securely, and how Copilot in Power Apps can speed up development. Every topic is hands-on with realistic business scenarios. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to build, connect and deploy practical business apps and automated workflows with confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C859' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 899;

-- C864 AB-730 Microsoft Certified AI Business Professional
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AB-730 Microsoft Certified AI Business Professional prepares business users and professionals for the Microsoft AB-730 certification, which validates the ability to use generative AI productivity tools such as Microsoft 365 Copilot effectively and responsibly in everyday work. The certification focuses on practical business use rather than technical development, making it ideal for professionals, managers, administrators and knowledge workers who want to demonstrate their AI productivity skills.</p><p>The course follows the official exam domains. You will start by understanding generative AI fundamentals, including how large language models work, what generative AI can and cannot do, common risks such as inaccuracy and bias, and responsible AI principles. Next you will learn to manage prompts and conversations by using AI, writing effective prompts with clear goals, context, sources and expectations, refining responses through follow-up and using Copilot Chat and agents productively.</p><p>The final domain covers drafting and analysing business content by using AI, using Microsoft 365 Copilot in Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook and Teams to create documents, analyse data, build presentations, manage email and summarise meetings, while protecting sensitive information. Each domain combines hands-on practice with realistic workplace tasks and exam-style questions. By the end, you will be able to use Microsoft AI tools confidently to work more productively and be well prepared to pass the AB-730 exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C864' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1050;

-- C882 Quantum Computing Fundamentals for Beginners
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Quantum Computing Fundamentals for Beginners introduces you to the exciting and fast-moving field of quantum computing in a clear, accessible way. Quantum computers use the principles of quantum mechanics, such as superposition and entanglement, to tackle certain problems that are extremely hard for classical computers, with potential impact on cryptography, optimisation, chemistry, finance and artificial intelligence. The course is designed for beginners, IT professionals, students and business leaders, and no advanced physics background is required.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to quantum computing, exploring how it differs from classical computing, the history and current state of the technology, and the main types of quantum hardware. Next you will learn about quantum states and gates, including qubits, superposition, measurement, entanglement and the Bloch sphere, and how single- and multi-qubit gates build quantum circuits. You will create and run simple circuits using Qiskit and cloud-based quantum simulators and hardware.</p><p>The course continues with quantum algorithms, introducing landmark algorithms such as Deutsch-Jozsa, Grover\'s search and Shor\'s factoring algorithm, and why they offer speed-ups. The final topic covers quantum computing applications, current limitations, quantum-safe security and what organisations should be doing now to prepare. Hands-on exercises reinforce each concept. By the end, you will understand the fundamentals of quantum computing and be able to build and run basic quantum circuits with confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C882' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 838;

-- C897 Photoshop Fundamentals for Beginners
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Photoshop Fundamentals for Beginners introduces you to Adobe Photoshop, the industry-standard software for editing photos and creating digital images. Whether you want to retouch portraits, create social media graphics, design marketing materials or simply improve your photos, Photoshop gives you powerful tools to bring your ideas to life. This course is designed for complete beginners, marketers, small business owners, content creators and anyone who wants to edit images confidently and professionally.</p><p>You will start with basic Photoshop techniques, exploring the workspace, tools and panels, opening and creating documents, understanding image size and resolution, and working with layers, selections and masks. You will learn how to crop, straighten and resize images and add text and shapes. Next you will improve your digital imagery, using adjustment layers to correct exposure, colour and contrast, retouching blemishes and removing unwanted objects with healing tools and generative AI features, and combining images into simple composites.</p><p>The final topic covers evaluating digital imaging techniques, reviewing your work against principles such as composition, colour and consistency, choosing the right approach for each task and preparing files correctly for print, web and social media. Every topic is hands-on with sample images, so you build practical skills step by step. By the end, you will be able to edit, enhance and create professional-looking images in Adobe Photoshop with confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C897' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 767;

-- C903 Workplace Evaluation and Innovation for AI Adoption
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Workplace Evaluation and Innovation for AI Adoption shows leaders and managers how to make AI adoption succeed by looking closely at the work first. Many organisations buy AI tools and run pilots, only to find months later that little has changed; lasting gains come from evaluating how work is really done, identifying genuine opportunities and building a practical adoption roadmap. The course is designed for managers, team leads, HR and transformation professionals, and business owners responsible for introducing AI in their organisation.</p><p>You will start by understanding AI adoption in the workplace, exploring what generative AI and AI agents can realistically do today, why AI initiatives stall and the conditions that make adoption succeed. Next you will evaluate your workplace, mapping processes, tasks, pain points, data and skills, and assessing readiness across people, process, technology and culture. You will then identify innovation opportunities, prioritising use cases by value, feasibility and risk, and designing small experiments to test them.</p><p>The final topic covers building the adoption roadmap, including setting goals and measures, sequencing initiatives, planning training and change management, putting governance and responsible AI guardrails in place, and engaging employees so they become champions rather than sceptics. Practical templates and exercises let you apply each step to your own organisation. By the end, you will have a clear, evidence-based plan to adopt AI in your workplace and turn it into measurable improvements.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C903' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1426;

-- C904 Leadership Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Leadership Masterclass equips aspiring and experienced leaders with the mindset and practical skills to lead people, teams and change effectively. Great leadership is not about title or authority; it is about building trust, communicating clearly, making sound decisions and bringing out the best in others. This masterclass is designed for new and experienced managers, team leaders, supervisors and high-potential professionals who want to strengthen their leadership impact.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to effective leadership, exploring leadership styles, self-awareness, emotional intelligence and the difference between managing and leading. Next you will develop communication and collaboration skills, including active listening, giving feedback, running effective meetings and building trust across teams. You will then cover decision making and problem solving, using structured approaches to analyse situations, weigh options and make timely decisions, followed by motivation and performance, setting goals, coaching and recognising good work.</p><p>The course continues with conflict resolution and negotiation, handling disagreements constructively and reaching win-win outcomes, and team building, creating a positive culture, developing people and leading through change. Role plays, case studies and self-assessments help you apply each topic to your own situation and create a personal leadership development plan. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to lead with greater confidence, inspire your team and deliver better results for your organisation.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C904' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 843;

-- C913 Certified Lean Six Sigma Black Belt (CLSSBB)
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Certified Lean Six Sigma Black Belt (CLSSBB) provides in-depth training in Lean Six Sigma for professionals who lead complex improvement projects and mentor Green and Yellow Belts. Black Belts apply advanced statistical and Lean tools to solve critical business problems, reduce variation and deliver significant financial and customer benefits. The course is designed for experienced quality and process improvement professionals, engineers, Green Belts and managers who want to lead strategic improvement initiatives and earn the Certified Lean Six Sigma Black Belt credential.</p><p>You will start with organisational roadblocks and Lean management, including change management, Lean tools and techniques, and how to align projects with strategy. Next you will cover the pre-Define and Define phases, selecting and scoping projects, building charters, capturing the voice of the customer and managing teams and stakeholders. You will then move into the Measure phase, covering process mapping, data collection, measurement system analysis, advanced statistics and process capability.</p><p>The course continues with the Analyse phase, applying hypothesis testing, regression and multi-vari analysis to identify root causes, the Improve phase, using design of experiments and Lean solutions to optimise processes, and the Control phase, sustaining results with statistical process control and control plans. Case studies and practical exercises using statistical software reinforce every phase. By the end, you will be able to lead complex Lean Six Sigma projects and be prepared to sit for the CLSSBB certification exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C913' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1020;

-- C914 Robot Operating System (ROS) Fundamentals
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Robot Operating System (ROS) Fundamentals teaches you how to build and program robots using ROS, the industry-standard open-source framework for robot software. ROS provides the tools, libraries and conventions that let robotics developers connect sensors, motors, perception and planning into working robotic systems, and is used in research, manufacturing, logistics and autonomous vehicles. The course is designed for engineers, developers, students and technical professionals with basic programming knowledge who want a practical introduction to robotics software.</p><p>You will start by getting started with ROS, understanding its architecture, installing and setting up a workspace, and using command-line tools to explore a running robot system. Next you will learn ROS nodes, topics and messages, writing publisher and subscriber nodes in Python, and using services, actions and parameters so different parts of a robot can communicate. You will then cover robot modelling, sensors and simulation, describing a robot with URDF, visualising it in RViz and simulating sensors such as cameras and lidar in Gazebo.</p><p>The final topic covers navigation, motion and robot applications, including transforms, mapping, localisation, path planning and autonomous navigation, and how to bring these together into a practical robot application. Every topic is hands-on in simulation, so you can experiment safely without expensive hardware. By the end, you will understand how ROS-based robots work and be able to develop, simulate and test your own robot software with confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C914' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 793;

-- C915 PL-400 Microsoft Power Platform Developer Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>PL-400 Microsoft Power Platform Developer Training prepares you for the Microsoft Certified: Power Platform Developer Associate certification by building the skills to design, develop, secure and extend Power Platform solutions. Power Platform developers go beyond low-code, using code, APIs and extensibility to create enterprise-grade apps, automations and integrations. The course is designed for developers and technical professionals with experience in Power Platform and programming who want to validate their expertise.</p><p>The course follows the official exam domains. You will start by creating a technical design, including solution architecture, security, data models and choosing between low-code and pro-code approaches. Next you will build Power Platform solutions, working with Dataverse, solutions, environments and application lifecycle management. You will then implement Power Apps improvements, optimising canvas and model-driven apps and using Power Fx and component libraries, followed by extending the user experience with client scripting, PowerApps Component Framework (PCF) controls and command customisations.</p><p>The course continues with extending the platform through plug-ins, custom APIs, Azure Functions and the Dataverse Web API, and developing integrations with custom connectors, webhooks and Azure services. Each domain combines explanation, hands-on labs and exam-style practice questions. By the end, you will be able to build and extend sophisticated Power Platform solutions confidently and be well prepared to pass the PL-400 exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C915' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 770;

-- C916 CompTIA Cybersecurity Analyst (CySA+) Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>CompTIA Cybersecurity Analyst (CySA+) Training prepares you for the CompTIA CySA+ certification (exam CS0-003), which validates the skills to detect, analyse and respond to cyber security threats using behavioural analytics. CySA+ is designed for security analysts, security operations centre staff, incident responders and IT professionals who want to move into or advance in hands-on cyber defence roles, and it builds naturally on CompTIA Security+.</p><p>The course follows the official exam domains. You will start with security operations, covering system and network architecture, analysing indicators of malicious activity, threat intelligence and threat hunting, and using tools such as SIEM, EDR and packet analysis to monitor and investigate events. Next you will study vulnerability management, including scanning methods, analysing and prioritising vulnerabilities, and recommending controls and mitigations for systems, applications and cloud environments.</p><p>The course continues with incident response and management, covering attack frameworks such as MITRE ATT&amp;CK, the incident response lifecycle, containment, eradication, recovery and post-incident activities, and closes with reporting and communication, including vulnerability and incident reports, metrics and stakeholder communication. Each domain includes practical scenarios and performance-based question practice. By the end, you will be able to analyse and respond to threats confidently and be well prepared to pass the CompTIA CySA+ exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C916' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 819;

-- C923 CompTIA Data+ Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>CompTIA Data+ Training prepares you for the CompTIA Data+ certification, a vendor-neutral credential that validates the skills to collect, analyse, visualise and govern data to support business decisions. Data+ covers the full analytics process, from understanding data structures and mining data to statistical analysis, reporting and data quality. The course is designed for data analysts, business analysts, reporting specialists and professionals who work with data and want a recognised analytics certification.</p><p>The course follows the official exam domains. You will start with data concepts and environments, including database types, data structures, file formats, data warehouses and data lakes. Next you will cover data mining, acquiring and integrating datasets, cleansing and profiling data, handling missing values and outliers, and transforming data for analysis. You will then study data analysis, applying descriptive and inferential statistics, choosing the right analysis technique and interpreting results to identify trends and patterns.</p><p>The course continues with visualisation, designing effective reports and dashboards, choosing appropriate chart types and communicating insights clearly to different audiences, and closes with data governance, quality and controls, covering data privacy, security, quality dimensions, master data management and compliance. Each domain combines hands-on exercises with exam-style practice questions. By the end, you will be able to turn raw data into reliable insights and be well prepared to pass the CompTIA Data+ exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C923' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 888;

-- C924 Generative AI for Agile Design Thinking
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Generative AI for Agile Design Thinking equips professionals with the tools and methods to drive innovation by combining design thinking, agile delivery and generative AI. Design thinking helps teams understand users and frame the right problems; agile turns ideas into working solutions through short, iterative cycles; and generative AI accelerates research, ideation, prototyping and testing at every step. The course is designed for managers, product owners, innovation and transformation teams, designers and project professionals.</p><p>You will start with the foundations of design thinking, agile and generative AI, understanding how the three approaches complement each other and where AI tools such as ChatGPT, Claude and image generators add the most value. Next you will cover problem framing and ideation with design thinking and AI, synthesising user research, building personas and journey maps, defining problem statements and generating and prioritising ideas. You will then apply agile development and AI for rapid solution delivery, turning ideas into backlogs, prototypes and minimum viable products and testing them quickly with users.</p><p>The final topic covers scaling and sustaining innovations with agile, including measuring outcomes, iterating based on feedback, embedding an innovation culture and governing the responsible use of AI. Throughout the course you will work in teams on a realistic innovation challenge. By the end, you will be able to lead agile design thinking initiatives powered by generative AI that deliver user-centred solutions faster and more effectively.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C924' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 928;

-- C926 AI-103 Microsoft Certified Azure AI Apps and Agents Developer Associate
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI-103 Microsoft Certified Azure AI Apps and Agents Developer Associate prepares developers to design, build and deploy AI applications and agents on Microsoft Azure and to pursue the AI-103 certification. The course focuses on building generative AI solutions with Microsoft Foundry and Azure AI services, from retrieval-augmented chat applications to agents that use tools and act on data. It is designed for software developers, AI engineers and technical professionals with programming experience who build AI-powered solutions on Azure.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to Microsoft Azure AI applications, exploring Microsoft Foundry, model selection and deployment, the Azure OpenAI service, Azure AI Search and the wider set of Azure AI services for language, speech, vision and document intelligence. Next you will evaluate Azure AI applications, learning how to measure quality, groundedness and safety, apply content filters and responsible AI practices, and monitor cost and performance.</p><p>The final topic covers developing Azure AI solutions, building retrieval-augmented generation applications grounded in your own data, creating agents with tools and knowledge using the Foundry Agent Service, integrating AI capabilities into applications through SDKs and APIs, and securing and deploying your solutions. Each topic combines explanation with hands-on labs and exam-style practice. By the end, you will be able to build, evaluate and deploy AI apps and agents on Azure confidently and be prepared for the AI-103 exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C926' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1110;

-- C947 FMEA Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>FMEA Masterclass equips you with the knowledge and practical skills to perform Failure Mode and Effects Analysis, a structured method for identifying potential failures in a product, process or system, assessing their risk and taking action before they occur. FMEA is widely used in manufacturing, automotive, electronics, medical devices, aerospace and service industries to improve reliability, safety and quality. The masterclass is designed for engineers, quality and reliability professionals, process owners and team leaders.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to Failure Mode and Effects Analysis, understanding the purpose and benefits of FMEA, the differences between design FMEA and process FMEA, and how FMEA fits with other quality tools and standards such as the AIAG-VDA FMEA handbook. Next you will learn how to perform an FMEA, defining scope, building a cross-functional team, analysing functions and process steps, identifying failure modes, effects and causes, and rating severity, occurrence and detection.</p><p>The final topic covers interpreting FMEA results and recommending follow-up actions, using risk priority numbers and action priority to decide where to focus, developing preventive and detection actions, assigning responsibilities and updating the FMEA as changes are made. Practical workshops let you complete an FMEA on a realistic product or process. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to lead FMEA sessions confidently and use the results to reduce risk and improve quality.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C947' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1007;

-- C950 Design of Experiment (DOE) Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Design of Experiment (DOE) Masterclass equips you with the essential skills to plan, run, analyse and optimise experiments that improve process and product performance. Rather than changing one factor at a time, DOE lets you study several factors together, uncover interactions and find the best settings with far fewer runs, saving time and cost. The masterclass is designed for engineers, scientists, quality and process improvement professionals, and Six Sigma practitioners in manufacturing, R&amp;D and service environments.</p><p>You will start with the fundamentals of design of experiments, including key terminology, factors, levels and responses, randomisation, replication and blocking, and how to plan an experiment that answers the right question. Next you will learn factorial DOE, designing and analysing full factorial experiments, interpreting main effects and interaction plots and using analysis of variance to identify significant factors. You will then cover fractional factorial DOE, reducing the number of runs while understanding confounding and resolution.</p><p>The final topic focuses on screening, modelling and optimising DOE, including screening designs to find the vital few factors, regression models, response surface methods and finding optimal process settings. Throughout the masterclass you will use statistical software and practical case studies to design and analyse real experiments. By the end, you will be able to apply DOE confidently to solve problems, optimise processes and make data-driven improvements.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C950' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 853;

-- C975 Cisco Certified Network Associate (CCNA) Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Cisco Certified Network Associate (CCNA) Training prepares you for the Cisco CCNA certification (exam 200-301), one of the most respected entry-level networking credentials in the world. CCNA validates the skills to install, configure, operate and troubleshoot small to medium-sized networks, covering routing, switching, wireless, security and automation. The course is designed for network administrators, IT support engineers, students and career switchers who want to build a strong career foundation in networking.</p><p>The course follows the official exam domains. You will start with network fundamentals, including network components, topologies, cabling, TCP/IP, IPv4 and IPv6 addressing and subnetting. Next you will cover network access, configuring VLANs, trunking, EtherChannel, spanning tree and wireless LANs. You will then study IP connectivity, including routing concepts, static routing and OSPF, followed by IP services such as DHCP, DNS, NAT, NTP, SNMP, syslog and quality of service.</p><p>The course continues with security fundamentals, covering security concepts, device hardening, access control lists, port security, VPNs and wireless security, and closes with automation and programmability, introducing controller-based and software-defined networking, REST APIs, JSON and configuration management tools. Hands-on labs with Cisco IOS and practice questions reinforce every domain. By the end, you will be able to configure and troubleshoot networks confidently and be well prepared to pass the CCNA exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C975' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 930;

-- C976 AI Vibe Coding for Blockchain dApps
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI Vibe Coding for Blockchain dApps teaches you how to build decentralised applications on the blockchain by directing AI coding assistants such as Cursor, GitHub Copilot and Claude. With vibe coding, you describe the smart contract or feature you want in plain English, review the code the AI produces and guide it until it works, letting you build Web3 applications far faster than coding everything by hand. The course is designed for developers, technical professionals and entrepreneurs interested in blockchain and Web3.</p><p>You will start with the essentials of blockchain, cryptocurrency, smart contracts and Web3, including how transactions, consensus, wallets and gas work on networks such as Ethereum. Next you will develop a dApp with vibe coding, using AI to write Solidity smart contracts, set up a development framework and connect a web front end to the blockchain through a wallet. You will learn how to prompt the AI effectively and review its code with a critical eye.</p><p>The course continues with smart contract testing, writing automated tests, checking for common vulnerabilities such as reentrancy and access control flaws and using AI to help audit your code, followed by smart contract deployment to a public test network and interacting with your live dApp. Throughout the course you will learn security best practices that matter when real value is at stake. Every topic is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to build, test and deploy blockchain dApps efficiently using AI vibe coding.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C976' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1265;

-- C978 Build a RAG Chatbot with n8n
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Build a RAG Chatbot with n8n shows you how to create an AI chatbot that answers questions accurately from your organisation\'s own documents and data. Generic chatbots only know what their AI model was trained on, so they fall short when asked about your products, policies or procedures; Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) solves this by retrieving relevant information from your knowledge base and giving it to the AI before it answers. The course is designed for business users, operations and IT professionals, and anyone who wants to build practical AI assistants without heavy coding.</p><p>You will start by understanding RAG chatbots, learning how embeddings, vector databases and retrieval work, how RAG reduces hallucinations, and how to prepare and organise documents such as FAQs, manuals and policies for best results. You will see where RAG chatbots add value in customer service, HR, internal help desks and sales support. Next you will build a RAG chatbot with n8n, creating workflows that load and chunk documents, generate embeddings, store them in a vector database and connect an AI agent that retrieves the right information to answer questions.</p><p>Throughout the course you will also learn how to test and improve answer quality, add memory and source citations, embed the chatbot in a website or chat app and keep data secure. Every step is hands-on in n8n. By the end, you will be able to build, deploy and maintain a RAG chatbot that gives accurate, trustworthy answers grounded in your own knowledge.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C978' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1094;

-- C989 Codex Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Codex Masterclass teaches you how to master Codex, the agentic coding surface in the ChatGPT desktop app that plans, writes, runs and checks code inside your project while you review and guide the work. Instead of coding every step yourself, you describe the goal, approve the plan and evaluate the result against evidence. The masterclass is designed for developers, technical professionals, analysts and product builders who want to use an AI coding agent to build and govern real applications.</p><p>You will start with the fundamentals of Chat, Work and Codex in the ChatGPT app, then work as the AI-assisted developer behind a fictitious cooking school, taking one business from a written brief to a live website. Codex plans the site with /plan, builds it from the course catalogue, adds durable rules in AGENTS.md and a sign-up form for every course, and publishes it to GitHub Pages. Next you will explore tools and build a SQLite RAG assistant, turning course brochures into a knowledge base, driving it to 30 out of 30 golden questions with /goal, red-teaming it and testing the site with Computer Use.</p><p>The final topic covers skills and hooks, the features that make an agent dependable, including community skills from skills.sh, custom skills created with the skill creator, a timed workshop popup and a hook that re-checks the site after every edit. Throughout the masterclass you will practise planning before editing, permission control, keeping secrets out of static sites and human review. By the end, you will be able to use Codex confidently to build, test and govern real applications.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C989' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1368;

-- C991 Build Multi Agent Systems with ADK, Streamlit, Autogen and CrewAI
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Build Multi Agent Systems with ADK, Streamlit, Autogen and CrewAI teaches you how to design and build multi-agent AI applications using some of the most popular open-source agent frameworks. Multi-agent systems assign specialised AI agents to different parts of a complex task and coordinate them to deliver results that a single model cannot achieve on its own. The course is designed for developers, AI engineers, data scientists and technical professionals with Python experience who want hands-on experience with leading agent frameworks.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to large language model (LLM) AI agents, understanding how LLMs reason, use tools and keep memory, and comparing Google\'s Agent Development Kit (ADK), Microsoft AutoGen and CrewAI so you can choose the right framework for each problem. You will build simple agents in each framework and create user interfaces for them with Streamlit. Next you will implement retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), connecting agents to vector databases and your own documents so they answer accurately from trusted knowledge.</p><p>The final topic covers implementing a multi-agent AI workflow, designing agent roles and tasks, orchestrating collaboration and handoffs, and building an end-to-end application with a Streamlit front end. Throughout the course you will also learn how to evaluate agent output, handle errors, control costs and apply guardrails. Every topic is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to build, compare and deploy multi-agent systems using ADK, AutoGen, CrewAI and Streamlit with confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C991' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 836;

-- C995 AutoCAD Electrical Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AutoCAD Electrical Masterclass teaches you how to design, document and manage electrical control systems efficiently with AutoCAD Electrical, the specialised version of AutoCAD built for electrical engineers and designers. AutoCAD Electrical includes libraries of standard symbols, automatic wire numbering and component tagging, cross-referencing and report generation, which save significant time and reduce errors compared with drafting schematics in standard AutoCAD. The masterclass is designed for electrical engineers, designers, draughtspersons and technicians.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to technical drawing using AutoCAD Electrical, setting up projects and drawings, understanding the interface and using symbol libraries to insert components into schematic diagrams. You will create ladder diagrams, add wires and wire numbers, and work with multi-line circuits and PLC input and output modules. Next you will learn to analyse technical drawings, using cross-references, component tagging, terminal strips and error-checking tools to ensure your schematics are accurate and consistent.</p><p>The final topic covers drafting design documentation and specifications, creating panel layouts, generating bills of materials, wire lists and terminal reports automatically, applying drawing standards and title blocks, and publishing your project. Every topic is hands-on with realistic electrical control projects. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to produce professional electrical schematics, panel layouts and reports in AutoCAD Electrical with speed and accuracy.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C995' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 854;

-- C996 AutoCAD Mechanical Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AutoCAD Mechanical Masterclass teaches you how to create accurate mechanical drawings faster with AutoCAD Mechanical, the specialised version of AutoCAD built for mechanical engineering and manufacturing. AutoCAD Mechanical adds standards-based parts libraries, mechanical layers, power dimensioning, balloons and bills of materials, and tools for generating standard components such as fasteners, shafts and springs. The masterclass is designed for mechanical engineers, designers, draughtspersons and technicians who produce detailed manufacturing drawings.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to technical drawing using AutoCAD Mechanical, setting up drawings to industry standards, understanding the interface and using mechanical drawing tools to create accurate 2D part geometry and orthographic views. You will insert standard parts from the content library and use generators for common machine elements. Next you will learn to analyse technical drawings, working with assemblies, hidden lines, section and detail views, and checking designs for accuracy and fit.</p><p>The final topic covers drafting design documentation and specifications, applying power dimensioning, tolerances, geometric dimensioning and tolerancing symbols, surface finish annotations, balloons and parts lists, and preparing title blocks and drawing sheets for manufacturing. Every topic is hands-on with realistic mechanical projects. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to produce professional, standards-compliant mechanical drawings and documentation in AutoCAD Mechanical efficiently.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C996' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1149;

-- C1018 AI for Healthcare
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI for Healthcare gives healthcare professionals and managers a practical understanding of how artificial intelligence is transforming patient care, clinical operations and healthcare administration. From medical imaging and clinical decision support to patient engagement, scheduling and population health analytics, AI is helping healthcare organisations improve outcomes, efficiency and access. The course is designed for clinicians, nurses, allied health professionals, healthcare administrators, IT staff and anyone working in or with the healthcare sector, and no programming background is required.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to AI in healthcare, exploring the main types of AI, including machine learning, generative AI and AI agents, real-world applications across hospitals, clinics and community care, and the opportunities and limitations of each. Next you will look at data science and business insights, understanding healthcare data sources such as electronic health records, imaging and wearables, and how analytics turns this data into insights for clinical and operational decisions. You will then explore data mining and analysis, identifying patterns and risk factors in patient and operational data.</p><p>The course continues with advanced data science techniques, such as predictive modelling, natural language processing of clinical notes and generative AI for documentation and patient communication. Throughout the course you will examine ethics, patient privacy, data protection, bias and regulatory considerations, and discuss how to evaluate and implement AI solutions safely. By the end, you will understand how AI can be applied responsibly in healthcare and be able to identify practical opportunities in your own organisation.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1018' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 894;

-- C1034 Multi Agents System with Autogen
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Multi Agents System with Autogen teaches you how to orchestrate teams of AI agents using Microsoft AutoGen, an open-source framework for building applications in which multiple agents converse, collaborate and use tools to complete complex tasks. Instead of relying on a single model, a multi-agent system assigns specialised roles, such as planner, researcher, coder and reviewer, and coordinates them to produce better results. The course is designed for developers, AI engineers, data scientists and technical professionals with Python experience.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to AutoGen and CrewAI, understanding agent roles, conversations, tools, memory and human-in-the-loop patterns, and comparing how the two frameworks approach multi-agent design. You will build your first conversational agents and give them tools such as code execution and web search. Next you will implement retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), connecting agents to vector databases and your own documents so they answer accurately from trusted, up-to-date knowledge.</p><p>The final topic covers implementing a multi-agent AI workflow, designing group chats and agent teams, defining tasks and termination conditions, orchestrating collaboration and building an end-to-end application that solves a realistic business problem. Throughout the course you will learn how to evaluate agent output, control costs, handle errors and apply guardrails for safe operation. Every topic is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to design, build and run multi-agent systems with AutoGen confidently.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1034' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1224;

-- C1048 CompTIA Server+ Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>CompTIA Server+ Training prepares you for the CompTIA Server+ certification, a vendor-neutral credential that validates the skills to install, configure, manage, secure and troubleshoot server hardware and software in on-premises, virtualised and hybrid environments. Server+ is ideal for server administrators, data centre technicians, systems engineers and IT support professionals who maintain the infrastructure that businesses depend on.</p><p>You will start with server administration concepts, including server roles, operating system installation and configuration, scripting basics, licensing and asset documentation. Next you will cover virtualisation and cloud computing, understanding hypervisors, virtual machines, storage and networking for virtual environments, and how cloud services integrate with on-premises servers. You will then study physical and network security concepts, such as physical access controls, data security, hardening, authentication and network security for servers.</p><p>The course continues with managing physical assets and server hardware, including rack installation, power and cooling, server components, RAID and storage configuration, and closes with disaster recovery, backup strategies and troubleshooting hardware, storage, operating system and network issues using a structured methodology. Each topic combines explanation, practical examples and exam-style practice questions. By the end, you will be able to administer and troubleshoot servers confidently and be well prepared to pass the CompTIA Server+ exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1048' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 931;

-- C1058 Articulate Storyline 360 Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Articulate Storyline 360 Masterclass teaches you how to design and build engaging, interactive e-learning courses with Articulate Storyline 360, one of the most widely used e-learning authoring tools. Storyline lets you create custom interactions, scenarios, quizzes and simulations without programming, and publish them to any learning management system. The masterclass is designed for instructional designers, trainers, learning and development professionals, educators and HR teams who want to create professional digital learning content.</p><p>You will start by getting started with Articulate Storyline 360, exploring the interface, creating a project, using templates and themes, and planning a course structure with scenes, slides and story view. Next you will work with assets, adding and formatting text, images, characters, audio, video and screen recordings, and using the Content Library to speed up development. You will then build interactivity, using triggers, states, layers, variables and conditions to create clickable interactions, branching scenarios and drag-and-drop activities.</p><p>The final topic covers presentation, including designing quizzes and result slides, adding accessibility features, previewing and testing, and publishing your course to SCORM and xAPI for a learning management system or to the web. Throughout the masterclass you will apply instructional design principles so your courses are both engaging and effective. Every topic is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to plan, build and publish professional interactive e-learning courses in Articulate Storyline 360 with confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1058' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1276;

-- C1063 Power Automate Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Power Automate Masterclass equips you with practical skills to identify automation opportunities and automate repetitive work across desktop applications, websites, documents and databases using Microsoft Power Automate. With robotic process automation (RPA) in Power Automate for desktop, you can record and build flows that mimic the clicks and keystrokes people perform every day, freeing time for more valuable work. The masterclass is designed for business users, operations and finance staff, analysts and IT professionals.</p><p>You will start by learning how to automate processes with robotic process automation, understanding when RPA is the right choice and how to identify and prioritise suitable processes. Next you will get started with Power Automate for desktop, exploring the designer, recorder, actions and variables, and building your first desktop flows. You will then work with different technologies in Power Automate for desktop, automating Excel, Outlook, web browsers, files and folders, PDFs and legacy applications.</p><p>The course continues with implementing advanced logic, including conditions, loops, subflows, error handling and exception management, and building and running robust flows that can be scheduled or triggered from cloud flows. You will also learn good practices for testing, maintaining and securing automations. Every topic is hands-on with realistic business scenarios such as data entry, report generation and invoice processing. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to design and deploy reliable automations with Power Automate.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1063' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 895;

-- C1067 WordPress Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>WordPress Masterclass teaches you how to build, manage and maintain professional websites with WordPress, the world\'s most popular content management system. WordPress powers a large share of all websites, from blogs and business sites to online stores, because it is flexible, scalable and easy to update without coding. This masterclass is designed for business owners, marketers, communications staff, freelancers and anyone who wants to create and manage their own website with confidence.</p><p>You will start with an overview of the WordPress CMS, setting up a site, understanding the dashboard, users and settings, and creating pages and posts with the block editor. Next you will manage multimedia content on WordPress, adding and optimising images, video, audio and galleries, and organising content with categories, tags and menus. You will then manage site appearance, choosing and customising themes, using the site editor, templates and patterns, and adding widgets and plugins to extend your site\'s functionality.</p><p>The final topic covers maintaining your WordPress web design, including updates, backups, security, performance optimisation, basic SEO and managing forms and comments. You will also learn how AI tools can help you draft content and design pages faster. Every topic is hands-on, so you finish with a working website you have built yourself and can keep improving. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to create, customise and maintain a professional WordPress website independently.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1067' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 834;

-- C1071 AI-901 Microsoft Azure AI Fundamentals
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI-901 Microsoft Azure AI Fundamentals prepares you for the Microsoft AI-901 certification exam, which validates foundational knowledge of artificial intelligence concepts and the ability to build simple AI solutions on Microsoft Azure. The course introduces core AI workloads and shows how Microsoft Foundry and Azure AI services make them accessible to developers and business users alike. It is designed for students, business professionals, technical staff and anyone starting their AI journey on Azure, with no advanced data science background required.</p><p>The course follows the official exam domains. You will start by identifying AI concepts and capabilities, covering machine learning, computer vision, natural language processing, speech, document intelligence and generative AI, along with responsible AI principles such as fairness, reliability, privacy, inclusiveness, transparency and accountability. You will learn how large language models, prompts, agents and retrieval-augmented generation work and where each type of AI workload delivers business value.</p><p>The second domain covers implementing AI solutions by using Microsoft Foundry, including exploring and deploying models, building and testing generative AI chat solutions and simple agents, and using Azure AI services for vision, language and speech tasks. Each topic combines explanation with hands-on exercises in the Azure portal and exam-style practice questions. By the end, you will understand the fundamentals of AI on Azure and be well prepared to pass the AI-901 exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1071' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 890;

-- C1088 Achieving Sales Goals with Customer-Centric Selling Techniques
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Achieving Sales Goals with Customer-Centric Selling Techniques equips you with empathy-driven, people-focused selling skills that build trust, uncover real customer needs and close more sales. Today\'s buyers are well informed and resistant to pushy tactics; they respond to salespeople who listen, understand their challenges and offer genuine solutions. The course is designed for sales executives, account managers, business development staff, retail and customer-facing teams, and business owners who want to improve their sales results.</p><p>You will start with the foundations of selling, exploring the customer-centric sales mindset, the buyer\'s journey, building rapport and trust, and setting clear sales goals. Next you will develop selling techniques and problem-solving skills, using effective questioning and active listening to identify needs, presenting solutions in terms of customer value and benefits, and tailoring your approach to different personalities and buying styles. You will then learn how to close the sale, recognising buying signals and using natural, ethical closing techniques.</p><p>The final topic covers handling objections and rejections, turning concerns into opportunities, negotiating confidently and maintaining motivation and resilience after setbacks. You will also learn how to follow up and build long-term relationships that generate repeat business and referrals. Role plays and real sales scenarios let you practise each skill. By the end, you will be able to apply customer-centric selling techniques confidently to achieve your sales goals and strengthen customer loyalty.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1088' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 897;

-- C1097 Excel Power Query and Power Pivot Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Excel Power Query and Power Pivot Masterclass equips you with the skills to clean, combine, model and analyse large volumes of data in Microsoft Excel using Power Query and Power Pivot. These powerful built-in tools let you automate data preparation that once took a great deal of manual work, build data models across multiple tables and create insightful reports that refresh with a single click. The masterclass is designed for analysts, finance and operations staff, and experienced Excel users who want to take their data skills further.</p><p>You will start by reviewing data with Power Query, connecting to Excel files, CSV files, folders and databases, and using the Power Query editor to clean data, remove errors and duplicates, change data types, split and merge columns, and unpivot and reshape tables. Next you will move on to data analysis with Power Query and Power Pivot, appending and merging queries, loading data into the data model, creating relationships between tables and building PivotTables and PivotCharts from the model.</p><p>The final topic covers advanced data analysis using Power Query and Power Pivot, including custom columns, parameters and query folding, writing DAX measures and calculated columns, time intelligence calculations and key performance indicators. Every topic is hands-on with realistic business datasets, so you build reusable, automated reports. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to prepare and analyse complex data efficiently in Excel and deliver reliable, refreshable insights.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1097' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 856;

-- C1098 Google Cloud Certified Associate Cloud Engineer Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Google Cloud Certified Associate Cloud Engineer Training prepares you for the Google Cloud Associate Cloud Engineer certification, which validates the ability to deploy applications, monitor operations and manage enterprise solutions on Google Cloud. Associate Cloud Engineers use the Google Cloud console and command-line interface to set up environments, maintain solutions and keep them secure and reliable. The course is designed for IT administrators, system and cloud engineers, developers and professionals starting their Google Cloud career.</p><p>The course follows the official exam sections. You will start by setting up a cloud solution environment, including resource hierarchy, projects, billing accounts, the Cloud SDK and identity configuration. Next you will plan and implement a cloud solution, choosing and deploying compute options such as Compute Engine, Google Kubernetes Engine, Cloud Run and App Engine, and configuring storage, databases and networking resources. You will then learn how to ensure the successful operation of a cloud solution, managing resources, monitoring and logging, and handling scaling and updates.</p><p>The final section covers configuring access and security, including Identity and Access Management roles, service accounts, audit logs and security best practices. Each section combines hands-on labs with exam-style practice questions and review of key services. By the end, you will be able to deploy and manage solutions on Google Cloud confidently and be well prepared to pass the Associate Cloud Engineer exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1098' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 857;

-- C1101 Quantum Computing Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Quantum Computing Masterclass equips you with the knowledge to understand, design and implement quantum computing applications, from the underlying physics to algorithms, protocols and security. Quantum computing promises breakthroughs in optimisation, materials science, finance, cryptography and machine learning, and organisations are already preparing for its impact. The masterclass is designed for engineers, developers, IT professionals, researchers and technical leaders who want a deeper, hands-on understanding of the field.</p><p>You will start with quantum physics fundamentals, including the mathematics of linear algebra and complex numbers, quantum states, superposition, measurement and entanglement. Next you will be introduced to quantum computing systems, exploring qubit technologies, quantum hardware architectures and the current noisy intermediate-scale era. You will then study quantum gates and circuits, building and simulating single- and multi-qubit circuits with Qiskit, followed by quantum protocols such as superdense coding and quantum teleportation.</p><p>The course continues with quantum algorithms, including Deutsch-Jozsa, Grover\'s search, the quantum Fourier transform and Shor\'s algorithm, and variational approaches for near-term devices, then covers quantum cryptography and quantum safety, including quantum key distribution and post-quantum cryptography. Practical coding exercises on simulators and cloud quantum hardware reinforce each topic. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to design and run quantum circuits and evaluate real-world quantum computing applications.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1101' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 753;

-- C1123 Wireshark Network Analysis Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Wireshark Network Analysis Masterclass equips you with the skills to capture, analyse and troubleshoot network traffic using Wireshark, the world\'s most widely used network protocol analyser. Wireshark lets you see exactly what is happening on your network, making it invaluable for diagnosing performance problems, investigating security incidents and understanding how applications communicate. The masterclass is designed for network administrators, security analysts, IT support engineers and anyone responsible for keeping networks running smoothly.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to network analysis and Wireshark, understanding packet capture, the Wireshark interface and how to open and navigate trace files. Next you will learn capture methods and how to use capture filters, including where to capture on switched, wireless and virtual networks. You will then customise Wireshark for efficiency, configuring global and personal preferences and profiles, and learn to navigate quickly and focus faster with colouring rules, display filters, columns and time settings.</p><p>The course continues with analysing key protocols such as Ethernet, IP, TCP, UDP, DNS, DHCP and HTTP, following streams, using the expert information system and statistics, and graphing traffic to identify latency, packet loss and retransmissions. You will also apply Wireshark to detecting suspicious and malicious traffic. Every topic is hands-on with real trace files. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to use Wireshark confidently to troubleshoot network problems and investigate security issues.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1123' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1347;

-- C1143 AI Vibe Coding for React Development
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI Vibe Coding for React Development teaches you how to build modern React web applications by directing AI coding assistants such as Cursor, GitHub Copilot and Claude. With vibe coding you describe the component, page or feature you want in plain English, review the code the AI generates and refine it until it works exactly as intended, so you can build front-end applications faster while still understanding how they work. The course is designed for web developers, front-end engineers, designers who code and technical learners with basic JavaScript knowledge.</p><p>You will start by getting started with AI vibe coding for React, setting up a React project with modern tooling and learning how to prompt AI assistants effectively, review their output and iterate. Next you will build React components and user interfaces with AI, creating reusable components, handling props and events, styling with modern CSS approaches and building responsive layouts. You will then manage state, hooks and routing with AI assistance, using useState, useEffect and custom hooks, fetching data from APIs and adding client-side navigation.</p><p>The final topic covers debugging, testing and deploying React apps with AI, including using AI to diagnose errors, writing component tests, improving performance and accessibility, and deploying your app to the cloud. Throughout the course you will learn to review AI-generated code critically and keep your project clean and maintainable. Every topic is hands-on, building a complete application. By the end, you will be able to develop and deploy React applications efficiently using AI vibe coding.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1143' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1212;

-- C1148 Generative AI for Strategic Planning
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Generative AI for Strategic Planning shows leaders and managers how to use generative AI tools such as ChatGPT, Claude and Microsoft Copilot to strengthen the way they plan, make decisions and turn strategy into action. AI can rapidly analyse markets and competitors, generate and stress-test strategic options, draft plans and communications, and help track execution, giving leaders more time for judgement and alignment. The course is designed for senior and middle managers, business owners, strategy and planning professionals, and project and programme leaders.</p><p>You will start by using AI to initiate a strategic initiative, analysing the business environment with frameworks such as SWOT and PESTLE, defining objectives and framing the problem. Next you will develop a strategic and project plan with AI, generating options, building scenarios, defining priorities, milestones and key performance indicators, and applying methods and tools to drive the initiative forward. You will then use AI to manage strategic and project risk, identifying risks and assumptions, assessing impact and planning mitigations.</p><p>The course continues with collaborating with stakeholders, using AI to analyse stakeholder needs and prepare clear communications, deploying resources effectively, and tracking delivery against plan with AI-generated progress reports and insights. Throughout the course you will learn to verify AI output, protect confidential information and keep leadership judgement at the centre. Practical exercises use your own organisation\'s challenges. By the end, you will be able to use generative AI to plan more strategically and execute with greater confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1148' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 935;

-- C1150 UIPath RPA Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>UIPath RPA Masterclass teaches you how to automate repetitive, time-consuming business tasks using UiPath, one of the world\'s leading robotic process automation (RPA) platforms. Software robots built in UiPath can log into applications, copy and enter data, process documents, send emails and generate reports just as a person would, but faster and without errors. The masterclass is designed for beginners, business analysts, operations and finance staff, and IT professionals who want to start building automations.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to RPA, understanding what robotic process automation is, its benefits and limitations, how to identify good candidates for automation and the components of the UiPath platform, including Studio, Robots and Orchestrator. Next you will build RPA workflows, learning sequences, flowcharts, variables, arguments and control flow activities. You will then create automations for common tasks, such as Excel and email automation, web and desktop UI automation, data scraping and working with PDFs and files.</p><p>The course continues with debugging and exception handling, using breakpoints, logging, try-catch and retry mechanisms to build robust automations, and closes with managing RPA, publishing processes to Orchestrator, scheduling and monitoring robots and following good practices for maintenance and governance. Every topic is hands-on with realistic business scenarios. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to design, build and deploy reliable software robots with UiPath.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1150' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 923;

-- C1154 AI Vibe Coding for SQL
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI Vibe Coding for SQL equips you with practical skills to design, query and manage relational databases by giving natural-language instructions to AI coding assistants such as Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor and GitHub Copilot. Instead of memorising syntax, you describe the question or structure you need, review the SQL the AI writes and refine it until the results are right, while building a solid understanding of how databases work. The course is designed for analysts, developers, business users and anyone who works with data.</p><p>You will start with AI-assisted SQL data modelling and database design, using AI to design tables, choose data types, define keys and relationships and create a database from a business scenario. Next you will cover SQL data processing, querying and analysis, prompting AI to write SELECT statements with filtering, sorting, joins and subqueries, and checking that the results answer your question correctly. You will then move into SQL data aggregation and transformation, using GROUP BY, window functions, common table expressions and functions to summarise and reshape data.</p><p>The final topic covers data mapping, warehousing and dashboard development, including designing simple star schemas, preparing data for reporting and connecting SQL queries to dashboards. Throughout the course you will learn how to validate AI-generated SQL, optimise slow queries and avoid mistakes that could change or delete data unintentionally. Every topic is hands-on with real databases. By the end, you will be able to use AI vibe coding to work with SQL quickly, accurately and confidently.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1154' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1348;

-- C1158 Improve Employee Wellness and Work Resilience
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Improve Employee Wellness and Work Resilience equips HR professionals, managers and wellness champions with the knowledge and practical tools to promote health and wellbeing in the workplace and help employees build resilience. Stress, burnout and poor mental health affect productivity, engagement and retention, while organisations that invest in wellbeing see stronger performance and loyalty. The course is designed for HR and people managers, team leaders, workplace health coordinators and anyone responsible for employee wellbeing.</p><p>You will start with health and wellness trends and legislative compliance, exploring emerging trends in employee wellbeing, the link between wellness and performance, workplace safety and health obligations, and guidelines that shape responsible wellness programmes. Next you will cover the development and integration of health and wellness programmes, assessing employee needs, designing initiatives for physical, mental, social and financial wellbeing, and integrating them into policies, work design and culture. You will also learn practical techniques for building personal and team resilience and managing stress.</p><p>The final topic focuses on communication strategies and feedback assessment, promoting programmes effectively, encouraging participation, gathering feedback and measuring the impact of wellness initiatives so they can be improved over time. Case studies and group activities help you apply each concept to your own organisation. By the end, you will be able to plan, implement and evaluate workplace wellness initiatives that improve employee wellbeing, resilience and performance.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1158' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1366;

-- C1162 CompTIA Linux+ Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>CompTIA Linux+ Training prepares you for the CompTIA Linux+ certification (exam XK0-006), a vendor-neutral credential that validates the skills to configure, manage, secure and troubleshoot Linux systems in on-premises and cloud environments. Linux runs most servers, cloud platforms and containers, so Linux administration is a core skill for system administrators, DevOps engineers, cloud engineers and cyber security professionals. The course is designed for IT professionals with some Linux experience who want to advance their careers.</p><p>The course follows the official exam domains. You will start with system management, covering the boot process, kernel modules, storage and file systems, logical volumes, package management, networking configuration and system services. Next you will study services and user management, including managing users, groups and permissions, configuring common services and working with containers. You will then cover security, such as authentication, access controls, SELinux and AppArmor, firewalls, SSH hardening, encryption and compliance.</p><p>The course continues with automation, orchestration and scripting, writing Bash and Python scripts, using Git and infrastructure as code tools such as Ansible, and closes with troubleshooting, applying a structured methodology to diagnose system, network, storage and performance problems. Hands-on labs and exam-style practice questions reinforce every domain. By the end, you will be able to administer Linux systems confidently and be well prepared to pass the CompTIA Linux+ exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1162' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 845;

-- C1164 Multi AI Agents System for Algorithmic Trading
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Multi AI Agents System for Algorithmic Trading shows you how to design and build a team of specialised AI agents that work together on trading research, strategy development and execution. Instead of relying on a single model to predict prices, a multi-agent system assigns roles such as market research agent, technical analysis agent, strategy and backtesting agent, and risk manager, and coordinates them under clear rules and human oversight. The course is designed for traders, quantitative analysts, developers and finance professionals with basic Python knowledge.</p><p>You will start with an overview of multi-agent systems for trading, understanding how AI agents reason, use tools and collaborate, and how to design agent roles, workflows and guardrails for a trading system. Next you will build market research and analysis agents that gather market data and news, analyse sentiment and calculate technical indicators. You will then create strategy and backtesting agents that turn ideas into rules, write and test strategies on historical data, and evaluate performance and risk metrics.</p><p>The final topic covers trade execution and risk management agents, including position sizing, stop-loss rules, paper trading, broker API integration and monitoring, with human approval before any capital is committed. Throughout the course you will learn to avoid common pitfalls such as overfitting and look-ahead bias and to keep a clear audit trail. The course is educational and does not provide financial advice. By the end, you will be able to build and run a multi AI agents system for algorithmic trading responsibly.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1164' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 902;

-- C1176 Generative AI for Instructional Design
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Generative AI for Instructional Design shows you how to design better learning experiences faster using generative AI tools such as ChatGPT, Claude and Gemini. AI can help you analyse learning needs, write learning outcomes, outline courses, draft content and activities, create assessments and produce supporting materials, while you apply your expertise to ensure quality and learner impact. The course is designed for instructional designers, trainers, learning and development professionals, educators and subject matter experts who create training.</p><p>You will start by getting started with generative AI for instructional design, understanding what AI can and cannot do, how to write effective prompts and how AI fits into models such as ADDIE and backward design. You will use AI to analyse audiences and learning needs, write measurable learning outcomes and outline course structures, lesson plans and storyboards. Next you will create learning content and assessments with AI, drafting explanations, examples, case studies, scenarios and activities, and generating quiz questions, rubrics and feedback aligned to your outcomes.</p><p>Throughout the course you will learn how to review AI-generated material for accuracy, clarity, inclusiveness and instructional quality, adapt it for different delivery modes such as classroom, virtual and e-learning, and manage copyright and data privacy. Every activity is hands-on, building materials for a course of your choice. By the end, you will be able to use generative AI confidently to design engaging, effective learning experiences in a fraction of the usual time.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1176' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 941;

-- C1259 AI Agents with Gemini Spark
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI Agents with Gemini Spark shows you how to put your productivity on autopilot using Google Gemini Spark, an autonomous AI agent that works in the background to carry out tasks on your behalf across Gmail, Calendar, Drive, Docs and other connected apps. Instead of prompting a chatbot one request at a time, you hand Gemini Spark a goal and it plans and completes the work, checking in when it needs your input. The course is designed for professionals, managers, entrepreneurs and anyone who wants to delegate routine digital work to an AI agent.</p><p>You will start by getting started with AI agents and Gemini Spark, understanding how agentic AI differs from chatbots, setting up Gemini Spark, connecting your apps and giving clear instructions with the right permissions. Next you will automate work with Gemini Spark tasks, delegating email triage and replies, meeting scheduling, research, document drafting and follow-ups. You will then build reusable skills and schedules, turning repeat processes into skills Gemini Spark can apply consistently and scheduling recurring tasks such as daily briefings and weekly reports.</p><p>The final topic covers advanced agentic workflows and real-world automation, chaining tasks across apps, monitoring progress and reviewing results. Throughout the course you will learn how to keep control of what the agent can access and do, protect sensitive information and check its output. Every topic is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to use Gemini Spark confidently as an AI agent that saves you time every day.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1259' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1027;

-- C1262 Business Negotiation Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Business Negotiation Masterclass equips you with the strategies, techniques and confidence to negotiate better outcomes in business, whether you are closing a sale, agreeing a contract, managing suppliers, resolving disputes or negotiating internally. Skilled negotiators create value for both sides, protect their interests and build lasting relationships. The masterclass is designed for managers, sales and procurement professionals, business owners, account managers and anyone who negotiates as part of their work.</p><p>You will start with preparation for negotiation, the stage where most negotiations are won or lost. You will learn how to identify your goals and desired outcomes, understand the context and the other party\'s interests, determine your BATNA (best alternative to a negotiated agreement), set your walk-away point and plan your opening position and concessions. You will also explore different negotiation styles and how culture, power and relationships influence the process.</p><p>The second topic covers negotiation tactics, including building rapport, asking powerful questions, active listening, anchoring, framing offers, trading concessions, handling pressure tactics and deadlocks, and closing the deal while preserving the relationship. You will also learn how to negotiate ethically and follow up effectively. Role plays and realistic business scenarios let you practise each technique and receive feedback. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to plan and conduct negotiations confidently and achieve better results for your organisation.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1262' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 935;

-- C1276 Generative AI for Creativity
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Generative AI for Creativity shows you how to unlock your creative potential using AI assistants such as ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and AI image generators. Generative AI is a powerful creative partner that can help you overcome blank-page moments, explore new directions, produce written and visual content quickly and refine ideas through conversation, while you remain the creative director. The course is designed for marketers, designers, writers, educators, entrepreneurs and anyone who wants to boost their creativity at work or in personal projects.</p><p>You will start by getting started with generative AI for creative work, understanding how AI tools work, their strengths and limitations, and how to write prompts that spark original, useful ideas rather than generic output. Next you will create written and visual content with AI, drafting stories, articles, social posts, slogans and scripts, and generating images, illustrations and design concepts that match a style or brand. You will learn techniques for refining and combining AI output with your own creative judgement.</p><p>The final topic covers AI-assisted ideation and creative workflows, using AI for brainstorming, mind mapping, concept development and turning ideas into finished pieces, and building repeatable creative processes. Throughout the course you will also discuss originality, copyright, disclosure and the responsible use of AI-generated content. Every activity is hands-on and practical. By the end, you will be able to use generative AI confidently to generate better ideas, create faster and bring your creative projects to life.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1276' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 927;

-- C1285 Docker Fundamentals for Beginners
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Docker Fundamentals for Beginners gives you hands-on skills to containerise, run and manage applications using Docker, and introduces you to Kubernetes for running containers at scale. Containers package an application with everything it needs to run, so it behaves the same on a laptop, a server or the cloud, which has made Docker a cornerstone of modern DevOps and cloud-native development. The course is designed for developers, system administrators, DevOps and IT professionals, and students who are new to containers.</p><p>You will start with Docker fundamentals, understanding containers versus virtual machines, installing Docker, running containers from images, writing Dockerfiles to build your own images, and managing images, volumes and networks. You will also learn how to push images to a container registry. Next you will learn Docker Compose, defining and running multi-container applications, such as a web app with a database, in a single configuration file, and managing environment variables, dependencies and persistent data.</p><p>The course continues with Kubernetes fundamentals, introducing clusters, pods, deployments and services and deploying your containerised application to Kubernetes, followed by advanced Kubernetes concepts such as scaling, rolling updates, ConfigMaps, Secrets and persistent storage. Throughout the course you will also learn container security and best practices. Every topic is hands-on with guided labs. By the end, you will be able to containerise applications with Docker, orchestrate them with Compose and deploy them to Kubernetes with confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1285' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1460;

-- C1306 Revit BIM Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Revit BIM Masterclass equips you with the skills to create, coordinate and document building projects using Autodesk Revit and Building Information Modelling (BIM). BIM brings architects, engineers and contractors together around a single intelligent 3D model, improving coordination, reducing errors and supporting better decisions across the building lifecycle. The masterclass is designed for architects, engineers, draughtspersons, BIM coordinators and construction professionals who want to work productively in a BIM environment.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to BIM and Revit, understanding BIM concepts, workflows and standards, the Revit interface and project setup, including levels, grids and templates. Next you will cover BIM modelling, building architectural elements such as walls, floors, roofs, doors, windows and stairs, and working with families, materials and parameters. You will then explore BIM applications, including coordination between disciplines, clash detection concepts, worksharing, linking models and using the model for quantity take-off and visualisation.</p><p>The final topic focuses on BIM documentation, creating plans, sections, elevations, schedules, annotations and sheets directly from the model, and exporting to formats such as DWG, PDF and IFC for collaboration. Every topic is hands-on with a realistic building project. By the end of the masterclass, you will be able to model, coordinate and document building projects in Revit and contribute effectively to BIM-based project teams.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1306' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 879;

-- C1311 Generative AI for Sustainability Reporting
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Generative AI for Sustainability Reporting shows you how to use generative AI to streamline and strengthen the sustainability reporting process, from collecting and analysing ESG data to drafting, reviewing and presenting credible reports. Sustainability reporting is increasingly mandatory and complex, demanding data from across the organisation and alignment with frameworks such as GRI, ISSB and TCFD; AI can reduce the manual effort while improving consistency and insight. The course is designed for sustainability and ESG professionals, finance and compliance teams, and managers involved in reporting.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to AI for sustainability reporting, understanding reporting requirements and frameworks, where generative AI tools such as ChatGPT, Claude and Microsoft Copilot fit into the reporting cycle, and how to prompt them effectively. Next you will use AI for sustainability data analysis and reporting, organising and analysing emissions, energy, social and governance data, identifying trends and gaps, and drafting report sections, metrics tables and narratives aligned to your chosen framework.</p><p>The final topic covers AI-assisted report review, compliance and presentation, using AI to check disclosures against framework requirements, improve clarity and consistency, identify unsupported claims and greenwashing risks, and prepare presentations and summaries for stakeholders. Throughout the course you will learn to verify AI output and keep accountability with people. Every exercise is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to use generative AI to produce sustainability reports more efficiently and with greater confidence.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1311' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1319;

-- C1358 PL-900 Microsoft Power Platform Fundamentals Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>PL-900 Microsoft Power Platform Fundamentals Training prepares you for the Microsoft Certified: Power Platform Fundamentals certification and shows how the Power Platform helps organisations analyse data, build apps, automate processes and create AI agents with low-code tools. The certification is ideal for business users, analysts, IT professionals, students and anyone who wants to understand the business value and core capabilities of Microsoft Power Platform before going deeper.</p><p>You will start with an introduction to Microsoft Power Platform, understanding its components, environments, connectors, security and how it fits within Microsoft 365, Dynamics 365 and Azure. Next you will explore Dataverse, learning about tables, columns, relationships and business rules. You will then get hands-on with Power Apps, building canvas and model-driven apps, followed by Power Automate, creating cloud flows to automate approvals, notifications and data tasks, and Power BI, connecting to data and building reports and dashboards.</p><p>The course continues with Copilot Studio, formerly Power Virtual Agents, creating AI agents that answer questions and take actions, and covers how Copilot and AI capabilities are built into the Power Platform. Each topic combines practical labs with exam-style practice questions. By the end, you will be able to identify how Power Platform solutions can solve business problems, build simple apps, flows, reports and agents, and be well prepared to pass the PL-900 exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1358' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 965;

-- C1373 Generative AI for Video Creation
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Generative AI for Video Creation shows you how to produce engaging, professional videos faster using generative AI tools for scripting, footage, voiceover, editing and enhancement. AI video platforms can turn text into video, create AI avatars and voices, generate B-roll, remove background noise and automate captions, helping marketers, trainers and content creators produce more video with smaller budgets and teams. The course is designed for marketers, social media managers, trainers, educators, communications staff and content creators.</p><p>You will start by creating and editing video scripts using generative AI, using tools such as ChatGPT and Claude to research topics, write hooks, structure scripts and storyboards, and adapt them for different platforms and audiences. Next you will improve video footage on AI-powered video platforms, generating scenes and B-roll from prompts, creating AI presenters and voiceovers, enhancing audio and image quality, and editing with AI features such as automatic cutting, captions and reframing for vertical formats.</p><p>The final topic covers applying new AI technologies to improve video production, exploring the latest text-to-video and image-to-video models, building an efficient AI-assisted production workflow and repurposing long videos into short clips. Throughout the course you will also discuss copyright, likeness rights, disclosure and responsible use of AI-generated media. Every topic is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to use generative AI confidently to plan, create and polish compelling videos efficiently.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1373' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1118;

-- C1382 Claude Cowork Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Claude Cowork Masterclass shows you how to put an AI coworker on your team. Claude Cowork is Anthropic\'s agentic AI workspace that works directly with your files and folders, organising documents, drafting reports, building spreadsheets and presentations, and completing multi-step tasks from a single plain-English brief, with no coding required. The masterclass is designed for professionals, managers, administrators, analysts and business owners who want to delegate routine knowledge work to AI and focus on higher-value tasks.</p><p>You will start by getting started with Claude Cowork, setting it up on your computer, giving it access to the right folders, understanding how it plans and carries out tasks, and learning how to write clear briefs with goals, context and expected outputs. Next you will automate everyday work with Cowork, using it to sort and rename files, summarise and compare documents, extract data from PDFs into spreadsheets, draft reports and emails, and create presentations from your notes and data.</p><p>The final topic covers advanced Cowork workflows, including connecting Cowork to other apps and data sources through connectors, creating reusable skills for tasks you repeat, scheduling recurring work and chaining multi-step processes. Throughout the masterclass you will learn how to review Cowork\'s output, manage permissions and keep sensitive information safe. Every activity is hands-on with realistic work scenarios. By the end, you will be able to use Claude Cowork confidently as a productive AI coworker.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1382' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1090;

-- C1415 DP-900 Azure Data Fundamentals Exam Prep
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>DP-900 Azure Data Fundamentals Exam Prep prepares you for the Microsoft Certified: Azure Data Fundamentals certification, which validates foundational knowledge of core data concepts and how they are implemented using Microsoft Azure data services. Understanding data is essential in every modern role, and this certification provides a strong starting point for careers in data analysis, data engineering and database administration. The course is designed for students, business users, IT professionals and anyone beginning to work with data in the cloud.</p><p>You will start by exploring core data concepts, including structured, semi-structured and unstructured data, data storage formats, transactional and analytical workloads, and the roles of database administrators, data engineers and data analysts. Next you will explore relational data in Azure, understanding relational concepts, normalisation, SQL basics and services such as Azure SQL Database, Azure SQL Managed Instance and Azure Database for PostgreSQL and MySQL.</p><p>The course continues with non-relational data in Azure, covering Azure Blob Storage, Azure Files, Azure Table Storage and Azure Cosmos DB with its multiple APIs, and closes with data analytics in Azure, exploring large-scale analytics, data warehousing, real-time analytics, Microsoft Fabric and data visualisation with Power BI. Each topic combines explanation, demonstrations and exam-style practice questions. By the end, you will understand core data concepts on Azure and be well prepared to pass the DP-900 exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1415' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 763;

-- C1417 Claude Code Masterclass
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Claude Code Masterclass teaches you how to master agentic coding with Claude Code, Anthropic\'s AI coding tool that works in your terminal and IDE. Claude Code navigates your codebase, edits files, runs commands and tests, and works through multi-step development tasks from plain-English instructions while you review and guide the work. The masterclass is designed for software developers, engineers, data professionals and technical leads who want to build, refactor and maintain software significantly faster with an AI coding agent.</p><p>You will start by getting started with Claude Code, installing it, understanding how it reads and edits your project, managing permissions and writing effective instructions and project memory files such as CLAUDE.md. Next you will learn agentic development workflows, including planning before coding, exploring unfamiliar codebases, implementing features, fixing bugs, writing tests, refactoring and working with Git and pull requests. You will then extend Claude Code with hooks, skills and MCP servers, automating checks, packaging repeatable expertise and connecting external tools and data.</p><p>The final topic covers building real-world projects with Claude Code, taking an application from requirements to a tested, deployed result and using subagents and headless automation for larger tasks. Throughout the masterclass you will practise reviewing AI-generated code critically, keeping humans in control and protecting secrets. Every topic is hands-on. By the end, you will be able to use Claude Code confidently to deliver high-quality software faster.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1417' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1082;

-- C1426 AZ-900 Azure Fundamentals Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AZ-900 Azure Fundamentals Training prepares you for the Microsoft Certified: Azure Fundamentals certification, which validates foundational knowledge of cloud concepts and core Microsoft Azure services. Whether you work in a technical or business role, understanding cloud computing and how Azure delivers it is increasingly essential. The course is designed for beginners, business and sales professionals, IT staff, students and anyone starting a cloud career, with no prior Azure experience required.</p><p>You will start by getting started with Azure cloud computing, exploring cloud concepts such as the shared responsibility model, public, private and hybrid clouds, consumption-based pricing, and the benefits of high availability, scalability, reliability and security. You will learn the differences between infrastructure as a service, platform as a service and software as a service. Next you will cover the implementation of Azure compute and networking, including regions, availability zones, resource groups, virtual machines, containers, Azure Functions, virtual networks and storage services.</p><p>The final topic covers monitoring and managing Azure cloud solutions, including identity and access with Microsoft Entra ID, governance and compliance tools such as Azure Policy and resource locks, cost management and pricing calculators, and monitoring with Azure Advisor, Service Health and Azure Monitor. Each topic combines demonstrations in the Azure portal with exam-style practice questions. By the end, you will understand Azure fundamentals and be well prepared to pass the AZ-900 exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1426' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 992;

-- C1433 PL-300 Microsoft Power BI Data Analyst Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>PL-300 Microsoft Power BI Data Analyst Training prepares you for the Microsoft Certified: Power BI Data Analyst Associate certification by building the skills to prepare, model, visualise and analyse data with Power BI. Certified Power BI data analysts help organisations make data-driven decisions by delivering reliable, insightful and well-designed reports and dashboards. The course is designed for data analysts, business intelligence professionals, report developers and business users with some Power BI experience.</p><p>You will start by discovering data analysis and getting started with Power BI, understanding the role of a data analyst and the Power BI Desktop and service workflow. Next you will get data in Power BI from a variety of sources, then clean, transform and load it using Power Query, profiling data and resolving quality issues. You will then design a data model in Power BI, creating relationships and star schemas, and writing DAX calculations, including measures, calculated columns and time intelligence.</p><p>The course continues with creating effective reports and visuals, designing interactive report pages, dashboards and paginated reports, performing analytics such as trends, forecasts and anomaly detection, and finally managing and securing Power BI, including workspaces, sharing, row-level security, refresh schedules and governance. Hands-on labs and exam-style practice questions reinforce every topic. By the end, you will be able to deliver professional Power BI solutions and be well prepared to pass the PL-300 exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1433' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1305;

-- C1434 AI Agent with Openclaw
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI Agent with Openclaw teaches you how to build your own autonomous AI agent using the OpenClaw platform. OpenClaw lets you design, configure and deploy AI agents that can take on defined roles, use tools, follow skills, communicate through messaging channels and carry out multi-step tasks on your behalf, from research and reporting to customer replies and routine operations. The course is designed for professionals, entrepreneurs, IT staff and technology enthusiasts who want practical, hands-on experience building an AI agent.</p><p>You will start by getting started with OpenClaw, installing and configuring the platform, connecting an AI model and messaging channels, and understanding how agents plan, use tools and keep memory. You will create your first agent with a clear role, instructions and boundaries, and test how it responds to real requests. Next you will build and deploy autonomous agents with OpenClaw, adding tools and skills, connecting business apps and data sources, scheduling recurring tasks and deploying your agent so it can work continuously.</p><p>Throughout the course you will also learn how to monitor what your agent is doing, review its results, manage permissions and data access, protect it against risks such as prompt injection and keep humans in control of important actions. Every activity is hands-on with realistic use cases. By the end, you will be able to build, deploy and safely manage an autonomous AI agent with OpenClaw that saves you time and handles real work.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1434' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 828;

-- C1440 AI Security and Governance
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI Security and Governance equips you to manage the risks that artificial intelligence introduces as it becomes embedded in everyday business systems. Chatbots answering customers, models scoring decisions and AI agents acting on live data all create new exposures, such as prompt injection, data leakage, model manipulation and unintended actions, that traditional security controls were not designed to handle. The course is designed for security, risk and compliance professionals, IT and data leaders, and managers responsible for deploying AI safely.</p><p>You will start with the AI risk and threat landscape, understanding how AI systems work, the attack surface they create and key threats catalogued by resources such as the OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications and MITRE ATLAS. Next you will explore AI governance frameworks and policy, including the NIST AI Risk Management Framework, ISO/IEC 42001, regulatory developments and how to set AI policies, roles, inventories and approval processes. You will then cover securing models, data and agents, applying access controls, data protection, guardrails, monitoring and least-privilege design.</p><p>The final topic covers assurance, oversight and response, including testing and red-teaming AI systems, auditing and monitoring for drift and misuse, human oversight and incident response for AI failures. Case studies and practical exercises help you apply each concept to your own organisation. By the end, you will be able to assess AI risks, build a practical governance programme and implement controls that let your organisation adopt AI securely and responsibly.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1440' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1376;

-- C1468 Generative AI for Social Media Marketing
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>Generative AI for Social Media Marketing shows you how to plan, create and optimise social media campaigns faster and more effectively with generative AI tools such as ChatGPT, Claude, Canva AI and AI image and video generators. AI can help you research audiences, generate content ideas, write captions, create visuals and short videos, and analyse performance, so you can publish consistent, engaging content without burning out. The course is designed for marketers, social media managers, business owners and content creators.</p><p>You will start by planning a social media marketing campaign with generative AI, defining goals and audiences, researching trends and competitors, and building a content strategy and calendar across platforms such as Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn and TikTok. Next you will evaluate social media marketing opportunities, using AI to identify the best channels, formats, hashtags and posting times for your audience. You will then create a social media marketing campaign with generative AI, writing captions and hooks in your brand voice and producing images, carousels and short videos.</p><p>The final topic covers evaluating social media marketing performance with generative AI, analysing engagement and reach data, summarising insights and deciding what to improve next. Throughout the course you will also cover brand consistency, disclosure, copyright and responsible use of AI-generated content. Every activity is hands-on using your own brand or a sample business. By the end, you will be able to use generative AI to run more effective, efficient social media marketing.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1468' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 884;

-- C1750 CompTIA SecAI+ Training
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>CompTIA SecAI+ Training prepares you for the CompTIA SecAI+ certification (exam CY0-001), which validates the skills to secure, govern and responsibly integrate artificial intelligence into cyber security operations. As organisations adopt AI rapidly, security teams must both protect AI systems from new threats and use AI to strengthen their own defences. The course is designed for security analysts, engineers, architects, IT professionals and risk and compliance staff with a background in cyber security who want to specialise in AI security.</p><p>The course follows the official exam domains. You will start with basic AI concepts related to cyber security, including machine learning, large language models, generative AI, AI agents, data pipelines and how AI systems are built and deployed. Next you will study securing AI systems, the largest domain, covering threats such as prompt injection, data poisoning, model theft, model inversion and supply chain attacks, along with controls for securing data, models, APIs and agents across the AI lifecycle.</p><p>The course continues with AI-assisted security, using AI for threat detection, analysis, automation and incident response while understanding its limitations, and closes with AI governance, risk and compliance, including AI risk frameworks, policies, regulations, responsible AI and auditing. Each domain combines explanation, real-world scenarios and exam-style practice questions. By the end, you will be able to secure and govern AI in your organisation confidently and be well prepared to pass the CompTIA SecAI+ exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1750' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 980;

-- C1752 DP-700 Microsoft Certified Fabric Data Engineer Associate Exam Prep
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>DP-700 Microsoft Certified Fabric Data Engineer Associate Exam Prep equips you with the practical knowledge and skills to design, implement and manage modern data engineering solutions with Microsoft Fabric, and prepares you for the DP-700 certification exam. Microsoft Fabric unifies data integration, engineering, warehousing, real-time analytics and business intelligence in a single software-as-a-service platform built on OneLake. The course is designed for data engineers, BI developers, data analysts moving into engineering and database professionals.</p><p>You will start by ingesting data with Microsoft Fabric, using Data Factory pipelines, dataflows and shortcuts to bring data from a variety of sources into OneLake. Next you will implement a lakehouse with Microsoft Fabric, organising data in a medallion architecture and transforming it with Apache Spark notebooks, PySpark and Delta tables. You will then implement real-time intelligence, working with eventstreams, eventhouses and KQL to ingest, analyse and act on streaming data.</p><p>The course continues with implementing a data warehouse with Microsoft Fabric, modelling and loading data with T-SQL, and managing a Microsoft Fabric environment, including workspaces, security, monitoring, performance optimisation and deployment pipelines with version control. Each topic combines explanation, hands-on labs and exam-style practice questions mapped to the official skills outline. By the end, you will be able to build end-to-end data engineering solutions in Microsoft Fabric and be well prepared to pass the DP-700 exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1752' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1095;

-- C1756 AB-100 Microsoft Certified Agentic AI Business Solutions Architect
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AB-100 Microsoft Certified Agentic AI Business Solutions Architect prepares solution architects and senior consultants for the Microsoft AB-100 certification, which validates the ability to plan, design and deploy AI-powered, agent-first business solutions using Microsoft technologies. The course focuses on how to combine Microsoft 365 Copilot, Copilot Studio, Dynamics 365, Power Platform and Azure AI Foundry into solutions where AI agents work alongside people to transform business processes. It is designed for solution architects, functional consultants and technical leads.</p><p>The course follows the official exam domains. You will start by planning AI-powered business solutions, assessing business requirements and processes, identifying opportunities for agents, evaluating readiness, data and risk, and building a business case. Next you will design AI-powered business solutions, selecting the right Microsoft platforms and agent patterns, designing agent roles, orchestration, knowledge sources, integrations, security and responsible AI controls, and planning for extensibility and governance.</p><p>The largest domain covers deploying AI-powered business solutions, including application lifecycle management, testing and evaluating agents, monitoring performance and cost, managing change and adoption, and continuously improving solutions after go-live. Each domain combines architecture scenarios, design exercises and exam-style practice questions. By the end, you will be able to architect agentic AI business solutions on Microsoft technologies with confidence and be well prepared to pass the AB-100 exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1756' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1052;

-- C1759 AI-200 Microsoft Certified Azure AI Cloud Developer Associate
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI-200 Microsoft Certified Azure AI Cloud Developer Associate prepares developers for the Microsoft AI-200 certification, which validates the skills to build, deploy and operate AI-enabled cloud solutions on Microsoft Azure. The course emphasises the cloud development foundations that AI applications depend on, including containers, data services, integration, security and monitoring, alongside the AI services that power intelligent features. It is designed for software developers, cloud engineers and technical professionals with programming experience.</p><p>The course follows the official exam domains. You will start by developing containerised solutions on Azure, building container images and deploying them with Azure Container Registry, Azure Container Apps and Azure Kubernetes Service. Next you will develop AI solutions by using Azure data management services, working with Azure Cosmos DB, Azure SQL and Azure Storage, including vector search capabilities that support retrieval-augmented generation. You will then learn to connect to and consume Azure services, integrating Azure AI services and Azure OpenAI models, messaging and event services, and APIs into your applications.</p><p>The final domain covers securing, monitoring and troubleshooting Azure solutions, including managed identities, Azure Key Vault, application configuration, Application Insights and Azure Monitor. Each domain combines explanation, hands-on labs and exam-style practice questions. By the end, you will be able to build and operate AI-enabled cloud solutions on Azure confidently and be well prepared to pass the AI-200 exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1759' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 998;

-- C1760 AB-620 Microsoft Certified AI Agent Builder Associate
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AB-620 Microsoft Certified AI Agent Builder Associate prepares developers and advanced makers for the Microsoft AB-620 certification, which validates the skills to design, build, extend and integrate custom AI agents using Microsoft Copilot Studio and related Microsoft technologies. AI agents can answer questions from organisational knowledge, carry out tasks and automate processes across business systems, and certified agent builders deliver them reliably and securely. The course is designed for developers, Power Platform makers, consultants and IT professionals.</p><p>The course follows the official exam domains. You will start by planning and configuring agent solutions, gathering requirements, choosing agent types and models, configuring knowledge sources, instructions, topics and generative orchestration, and setting up environments, authentication and security. Next you will integrate and extend agents in Copilot Studio, adding actions and tools, connectors and Power Automate flows, using Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers and REST APIs, building multi-agent solutions and publishing agents to Microsoft 365 Copilot, Teams and other channels.</p><p>The final domain covers testing and managing agents, including evaluating agent quality, monitoring analytics, troubleshooting conversations, applying governance and data loss prevention policies, and managing the agent lifecycle with solutions and pipelines. Each domain combines hands-on labs with exam-style practice questions. By the end, you will be able to build and manage production-ready AI agents in Copilot Studio confidently and be well prepared to pass the AB-620 exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1760' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1040;

-- C1762 AI-300 Microsoft Certified Machine Learning Operations Engineer Associate Exam Prep
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI-300 Microsoft Certified Machine Learning Operations Engineer Associate Exam Prep equips you with the knowledge and skills to set up and operate machine learning operations (MLOps) and generative AI operations (GenAIOps) on Microsoft Azure, and prepares you for the AI-300 certification exam. MLOps engineers bring discipline to how models are built, deployed, monitored and improved, so AI solutions stay reliable, secure and cost-effective in production. The course is designed for ML engineers, data scientists, DevOps engineers and AI platform engineers.</p><p>You will start by designing and implementing an MLOps infrastructure, setting up Azure Machine Learning workspaces, compute, data assets, environments and source control, and automating with CI/CD pipelines. Next you will implement the machine learning model lifecycle and operations, including training pipelines, experiment tracking, model registration, deployment to managed endpoints, and monitoring for performance and data drift. You will then design and implement a GenAIOps infrastructure for generative AI applications using Microsoft Foundry.</p><p>The course continues with operating generative AI solutions, covering prompt and model versioning, evaluation of quality, groundedness and safety, content filtering, tracing, cost management and continuous improvement in production. Each topic combines explanation, hands-on labs and exam-style practice questions mapped to the official skills outline. By the end, you will be able to run robust MLOps and GenAIOps practices on Azure and be well prepared to pass the AI-300 exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1762' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 988;

-- C1768 AB-900 Microsoft 365 Copilot and Agent Administration Fundamentals
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AB-900 Microsoft 365 Copilot and Agent Administration Fundamentals equips you with the foundational knowledge to administer Microsoft 365 Copilot and AI agents securely and effectively, and prepares you for the AB-900 certification exam. As organisations roll out Copilot and agents, administrators must understand how they work, how they use organisational data and how to keep that data protected and governed. The course is designed for Microsoft 365 administrators, IT support staff, security and compliance professionals and anyone new to Copilot administration.</p><p>The course follows the official exam domains. You will start by identifying the core features and objects of Microsoft 365, Copilot and agents, including tenants, users, groups, licences, Microsoft Graph, Copilot Chat, Microsoft 365 Copilot and how agents are built, published and used. Next you will understand data protection and governance tasks, covering permissions and oversharing risks, sensitivity labels, Microsoft Purview, data loss prevention, retention and responsible AI considerations.</p><p>The final domain covers performing basic administrative tasks for Copilot and agents, such as assigning licences, configuring Copilot settings, managing agent availability and access, monitoring usage and adoption reports, and supporting users. Each domain combines demonstrations, hands-on exercises and exam-style practice questions. By the end, you will be able to support a secure, well-governed rollout of Microsoft 365 Copilot and agents and be well prepared to pass the AB-900 exam.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1768' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 981;

-- C1800 AI Vibe Coding for Full Stack Web Development
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI Vibe Coding for Full Stack Web Development equips aspiring developers and IT professionals with practical skills to build modern, end-to-end web applications using AI-assisted development. With vibe coding you describe features in plain English, review the front-end and back-end code that AI coding assistants such as Cursor, GitHub Copilot and Claude produce, and steer it until the application works as intended. The course is designed for developers, career switchers, technical professionals and entrepreneurs who want to build complete web applications faster.</p><p>You will start by designing full stack web applications with AI, planning features, data models and architecture, and setting up a modern project with a front end, back end and database. Next you will build dynamic and responsive user interfaces, creating layouts and pages that work well on every device. You will then create interactive controls and application logic, handling forms, validation, events and state, followed by developing reusable components and full stack features that connect the front end to APIs and a database.</p><p>The later topics cover authentication, testing, debugging and deployment, including securing user accounts, writing tests, fixing issues with AI assistance and deploying your application to the cloud. Throughout the course you will learn to review AI-generated code critically, maintain a clean codebase and avoid common security mistakes. Every topic is hands-on, so you finish with a working full stack application. By the end, you will be able to use AI vibe coding to design, build and deploy full stack web applications confidently.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1800' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 1465;

-- C1871 AI Agent with Hermes Agent
UPDATE catalog_product_entity_text t JOIN catalog_product_entity e ON e.entity_id = t.entity_id SET t.value = '<p>AI Agent with Hermes Agent teaches you how to build your own autonomous AI agent using Hermes Agent, an open-source agent framework designed to plan and carry out multi-step tasks, use tools, remember context and improve its skills over time. Hermes Agent can work through messaging channels and the command line, run scheduled jobs and automate research, writing, data and operations tasks on your behalf. The course is designed for professionals, developers, IT staff and technology enthusiasts who want hands-on experience building a practical AI agent.</p><p>You will start by getting started with Hermes Agent, installing and configuring it, connecting an AI model and the channels you want to use, and understanding how the agent plans, calls tools and manages memory. You will create your first agent with a clear role, instructions and boundaries, and test it on real requests. Next you will build and deploy autonomous agents with Hermes Agent, adding tools and skills, connecting files, apps and data sources, scheduling recurring tasks and deploying your agent so it can run continuously.</p><p>Throughout the course you will also learn how to monitor and review what your agent does, manage permissions and access to data, protect it against risks such as prompt injection, and keep humans in control of important actions. Every activity is hands-on with realistic use cases. By the end, you will be able to build, deploy and safely manage an autonomous AI agent with Hermes Agent that handles real work and saves you time every day.</p>' WHERE @sg = 1 AND t.attribute_id = @a_short AND t.store_id = 0 AND TRIM(e.sku) = 'C1871' AND CHAR_LENGTH(t.value) = 834;
